{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "116",
 "name": "Hibarnhvidar",
 "file": "Map116_Hibarnhvidar.xml",
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":60,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, The Sky Road","descriptions":["The lights of a distant settlement dot the darkness to the southwest.  To the northeast, flickering torches flank a gate in a wall at the crest of the hill.  Behind the wall, a tower is dimly visible.","To the southwest, the steep but wide road rises from a distant valley, climbing to a gate in a stone wall to the northeast.  Behind the wall, a grey tower three or four stories high dominates the skyline."],"exits":[{"to":2,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":3,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":2,"x":40,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, The Sky Road","descriptions":["A long, steeply inclined span of graveled road stretches between two very different locales.  In the one direction, the road climbs to the top of the rocky eastern ridge, almost forbidding in its starkness in the other, it winds through the lower-lying meadows and orchards in the valley to the west."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":4,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":3,"x":87,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Lewkar Awg, The Courtyard","descriptions":["Lanterns light a round tower in a small cobblestone courtyard.  Their flickering beams reflect off the water in a trough and off a brass-studded door in the tower.  In the east and west walls are gates made of stout timbers.","A small cobblestone courtyard serves travelers as a place for a short rest, offering a water trough for the animals and benches out of the wind for their riders.  In the east and west walls are gates made of stout timbers strapped with brass.  A few stone steps lead up to the door of the round tower in the center of the yard."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}],"aliases":["E Gate","Raven's Point","Ain Ghazal","egate"],"linksTo":"Map123_Himineldar_Shel.xml"},
  {"id":4,"x":20,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, Wooded Slope","descriptions":["The road runs through a dense evergreen forest, following the steep incline of the mountainside with hardly a furlong of level ground in its route.  It bridges rivulets that rush downhill and winds around curves that edge past steep drops."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":2,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":5,"x":20,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, The High Meadow","descriptions":["For those who like bracing air, the smell of heather, and a constant wind fluttering the grass, this meadow is the place to be.  The road descends to the southwest but runs south along a hillside clearing until it disappears into the pines on the mountainside."],"exits":[{"to":4,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":6,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":6,"x":0,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["In a gentle decline westward to a walled city, the road passes through a valley lush with evergreen shrubs and trees.  To the northeast, it switches back and forth several times as it climbs into the mountains."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":10,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":7,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":9,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":7,"x":-20,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["The road that connects Hibarnhvidar to Zoluren and Ilithi rises steadily from the city toward a pass in the mountains to the east.  Despite the throngs that travel it on festival or market days, it is in good condition and free of litter, suggesting regular attention by the Dwarves who created it."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":6,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":10,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":8,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":8,"x":-40,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["To the west, the road leads down to a huge gate in a high wall.  On either side of the gate tower statues of black ravens, impressive even at this distance.  To the east, the road runs upward through the fields that lie on the lower slope of a high range of mountains."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":7,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":10,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":11,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":9,"x":-20,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["A meadow slopes gently to the north, then ends abruptly at an iron railing.  One would have the sense of a vast emptiness on the other side of the railing even without moonlight or starlight.  The occasional sound from that dark void seems impossibly remote.","A meadow slopes gently to the north, then ends abruptly in a sheer drop of hundreds of feet.  An iron railing keeps the unwary from falling but does not obscure the view.  Far below, the Segoltha River rolls along, and the lands north of it stretch to a far horizon in a landscape surpassing those of even the most talented painter.  One can see why a picnic table and benches have been placed here."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":7,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":8,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":10,"x":-20,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["A quiet open space lines the road, dotted here and there with an occasional tree.  Dark masses beneath the trees hint at bushes that by their shape may be cultivated rather than natural.  To the south, high cliffs rise in the distance.","A pleasant, park-like field lies along the road, covered with thick meadow grass and here and there dotted with pines and hemlocks surrounded by mountain laurel and rhododendron.  The dark color of the evergreens blends almost unnoticeably into the cliffs to the south."],"exits":[{"to":7,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":6,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":8,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":11,"x":-60,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Haalikshal Highway, East Park","descriptions":["The Raven Gate, with its famed obsidian statues on either side, opens from Hibarnhvidar into the city's East Park, a lush alpine valley just outside the city wall.  More like a meadow than the usual hovels and lean-tos that clutter the skirts of a big town, the verdant fields often attract residents to gather flowers or herbs."],"exits":[{"to":8,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":12,"exit":"go","move":"go raven gate"}],"color":"#FFBF00"},
  {"id":12,"x":-80,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Fewer travelers pass through the eastern gate of the city by night, but the well-known Raven Gate still sees its fair share of passage even after dark.  The namesake raven statues nearly disappear into the night sky, the tops only visible by the occasional reflection of firelight from their glassy forms.  Thronged with traffic by day, the road takes on an eerie quality in the relative quiet of the later hours.","The famed Raven Gate, so named for the towering obsidian raven statues that flank the entrance to the outer city, dominates the eastern end of Market Road.  Tired merchants and dusty travelers move through the gate and deeper into the city at a steady pace.  Beyond the gate lies the long Haalikshal highway, leading out to the lands of the east."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":11,"exit":"go","move":"go raven gate"},{"to":219,"exit":"go","move":"go fieldstone store"}]},
  {"id":13,"x":-100,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Dwarves and outlanders pass quietly through the area, intent on finishing the day's business.  A row of windows on the upper story of the local inn casts a welcome glow down onto the Market Road.  The bird-shaped sign over its doorway creaks slightly as it swings in any passing night breeze.","Heavy traffic winds its way up and down the broad right-of-way that makes up Market Road.  A battered wooden doorway flanked by large stone urns planted with artfully twisted trees marks the entrance to the local inn.  Overhead, a sign in the shape of a bird with wings outstretched creaks mournfully as it swings with each breath of wind."],"exits":[{"to":12,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":14,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":220,"exit":"go","move":"go inn"}]},
  {"id":14,"x":-120,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Standing like statues on either side of the front doors, guards maintain their watch of the bank into the small hours.  Even by night, light blazes from the windows of the bank and a sparse flow of people pass in and out of its guarded doors.  The muffled sound of singing and laughter carries into the street from some nearby building, hinting at a warmer side to the Dwarven city.","Caravans rumble by, forcing the pedestrian traffic to occasionally hop out of the way of the more stubborn traders.  Sturdy looking Dwarven guards flank the entrance to the bank, wordlessly observing all that passes before their stoic forms.  A rambling structure of off-white stone, the bank of the outer city diverts the footsteps of many a person towards its doors, subtly disrupting the normal flow of traffic along the road."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":15,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":225,"exit":"go","move":"go bank"}]},
  {"id":15,"x":-140,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Visible only in the shadowy light reflected out of the surrounding shop windows, a statue rises up in the center of the intersection over the meager traffic of the later hours.  A few of the many merchants located here are sweeping up the front steps of their respective shops before closing up for the night.","A large statue, supported by a great hexagonal plinth of stone, has been raised in the center of the intersection with Great Gate Road.  The crowds of the city sweep around the stone island, pushing down the roads on the day's business.  Multitudes of colorful signs hang from the frontages of the buildings, announcing a diversity of merchants and their wares."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":51,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":16,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":228,"exit":"go","move":"go flagstone shop"}]},
  {"id":16,"x":-180,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Light still spills out from the windows of the Traders' Guild despite the late hour, illuminating the apprentices sent out to sweep up the residues from the daytime animal traffic.  A few dedicated but tired-looking merchants wander in and out of the old brewery that houses the guild, determined to finish one more transaction before calling it a night.","The source for much of the local traffic, the Traders' Guild stands prominent along the south side of the busy avenue, occupying the premises of the old brewery.  Caravans jostle for position as they pass in and out of the Guild's doors, the handlers shouting greetings and friendly jibes at one another as they pass.  Crowded out by the beasts of burden, the remaining traffic is pressed back to the edges of the road."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":17,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":232,"exit":"go","move":"go old brewery"},{"to":233,"exit":"go","move":"go stable"}]},
  {"id":17,"x":-220,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["In the quiet of the evening hours, the sounds of the city's waterwheels carry clearly into the area without the sound of the daytime masses to drown them out.  Glimmers of light reflect off the silver characters of the tall stone spire in the center of the intersection.  A few desultory travelers trudge southward to East Valley Road, moving deeper into the outer city.","East Valley Road merges into the lane here, creating one of the busiest stretches of Market Road.  Despite the push and rush of the traffic, the clanking and splashing of the city's waterwheels to the northwest still manages to occasionally rise over the clamor of the crowds.  Nestled into the center of the chaos, a round patch of greenery shelters a tall spire of dark bluish stone and a few benches for the weary traveler."],"exits":[{"to":16,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":54,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":18,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":231,"exit":"go","move":"go auction tent"},{"to":426,"exit":"go","move":"go path"}]},
  {"id":18,"x":-240,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["The city's waterwheels continue their endless splashing revolutions in darkness, but the workshops that utilize their power by day on the opposite side of the road have closed up for the night.  Although not readily visible by night, the downstream end of the waterwheel system releases the powering water back into the Segoltha River.","The downstream end of the city's waterwheel system is clearly visible here, with the smallest of the many wheels releasing the driving waters out of the elaborate system and back into the mighty Segoltha River.  Carts and wagons stop to load or unload at the line of workshops lining the opposite side of the road, the source of many a good made within the outer city."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":19,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":270,"exit":"go","move":"go ironwork archway"}]},
  {"id":19,"x":-260,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["A few workers still wander around a large mill that dominates the local stretch of Market Road, moving a few last sacks of flour and cleaning up from another day's busy activities.  Across the way, the city's ever-churning waterwheels keep turning through the night and clanking noises rise up out of metal grates set into the road, both lending a regular rhythm to the workers' movements.","Facing out onto the intermeshing system of the city's churning waterwheels, a large mill dominates this section of road.  Visible within the mill's wide entrance, burly workers unload sacks of grain from carts, carrying them deeper into the mill for processing.  Grinding and clanking noises rise up out of metal gratings set at intervals into the street."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":20,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":218,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden hut"}]},
  {"id":20,"x":-280,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["The monumental nature of the stone structure that houses the city waterworks is still evident after dark, with lighted windows creating beacon-like icons high above the street.  Even by night, the sound of the waterwheels and their associated machinery below street level is hardly lessened, making the act of simple conversation difficult before the great building.","The monumental stone building that houses the city waterworks stands near the middle of the waterwheels, rising high enough to observe the entire length and breadth of the mammoth system from the upper levels of the structure.  The sound from the wall of waterwheels coupled with the noise of the mechanisms they drive below street level that rises up through metal gratings is enough to nearly drown out normal conversation."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":21,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":21,"x":-300,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["A pile of uncut lumber awaiting the coming workday is neatly stacked beside a respectably sized sawmill that stands opposite a section of the waterwheel system.  The big saws of the mill have been silenced for the evening and the junior employees putter about sweeping up piles of sawdust.  Creaking and splashing noises rise up from metal gratings set into the roadway.","Loads of uncut lumber are offloaded from caravans before a respectably sized sawmill that stands opposite of a section of the waterwheel system.  The grumbling buzz of big saws rises and falls from the mill and fine sawdust floats down onto the street, gathering into miniature drifts of powdery remnants all across the roadway.  The sound of creaking and splashing rises up out of metal gratings set into the roadway."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":22,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":22,"x":-320,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["A row of dark and silent warehouses faces the barrage of sound emanating from the upstream end of the city's famed waterwheel system churning and splashing through the night.  Harnessing the power of the mighty Segoltha River, the wheels turn through their endless patterns, driving the vast city's industry.","The upstream end of the city's famed elaborate waterwheel system churns and splashes in constant interconnected motion.  Powered by the waters of the Segoltha River, the wheels rotate around their respective axis to drive the machinery of the city.  The salt-stained cart of a merchant just in from the Tivshowldh mines, one of the scores of such that pass through the city each day, rolls past the rows of warehouses that flank the street without a glance towards the creaking waterwheels."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":23,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":23,"x":-340,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["The local stables, a low structure that sits at the corner of Market and West Valley Roads, shows less activity by night but remains open for late travelers.  Traffic through the intersection is minimal in the evening hours, leaving those few that wander through able to hear sentries calling out the hours from the nearby Northwest Gate.","The low, rambling structure of a stable commands the corner of Market and West Valley Roads.  Traffic flows easily between the two thoroughfares, winding its way through the city or towards the nearby Northwest Gate.  Standing awestruck in the middle of it all, a knot of Boar Clan hunters twist their heads around trying to take in all the sights of the big city at once."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":25,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":24,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":267,"exit":"go","move":"go low stable"}]},
  {"id":24,"x":-360,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Road","descriptions":["Almost invisible in the darkness, the massive stones of the Northwest Gate rise up in the night to mark the end of Market Road.  The outline of guards walking their rounds on the platforms high above can be seen as they pass near torches.  A few tired travelers still stagger in from the wilderness beyond, obviously anxious to be done with the day's business.","The impressive edifice of the outer city's Northwest Gate marks the end of Market Road.  Travelers from distant destinations jostle against one another as they pass in and out of the gate, making way for a wagonload of timber in from the Paasvadh Forest.  A wiry nomad from the distant Arid Steppes ignores all the distractions of the metropolis, striding purposefully into the city on his appointed task."],"exits":[{"to":23,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":217,"exit":"go","move":"go northwest gate"}],"color":"#FFBF00"},
  {"id":25,"x":-320,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Farther to the south, where the valley deepens and the mountains press towards each other, construction has been defined by lack of space.  This portion of West Valley Road has been populated by the more well-to-do class whose fine houses line the avenue.  A few are complete with gardens and fences and landscaped with local trees."],"exits":[{"to":26,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":23,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":26,"x":-320,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["A variety of housing lines the road here, indicative of the mixture of cultures and status found in this satellite to the Dwarven stronghold of Inner Hibarnhvidar.  When facing south, a slight bending and narrowing of the road creates an optical illusion that changes the location of a large red structure on the far right and makes it appear to straddle the center of the road.  Standing proudly on one lawn is a carved wooden rooster whose head faces whichever direction the wind blows."],"exits":[{"to":25,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":27,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":27,"x":-320,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Cloistered from the bustle of the area by a wood fence, a small plot of land surrounds a large, red wood structure that serves as the school for the children of Outer Hibarnhvidar.  A weathered set of wooden stocks faces the roadway, its proximity a sure deterrent to childish antics.  Hanging from a thick branch in an old tree is a rope swing, whose board seat is carved with initials."],"exits":[{"to":26,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":28,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":28,"x":-320,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Runoff from rain and snowmelt is guided to a deep, water-filled pit via rock-lined channels cut into the mountainside.  Mounded chunks of discarded stone line the catch-basin's edge, providing a small barrier to taking an accidental swim.  A small rope and pulley with a bucket attached enable horsemen to offer their steeds a drink."],"exits":[{"to":27,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":29,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":263,"exit":"go","move":"go granite boulder"}]},
  {"id":29,"x":-300,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["The back wall of a small hovel cants precariously as it leans against the mountainside.  A wood bench faces Upper Gate Road and serves as a gathering spot for local gossips even though its seat is missing a slat.  The road going north is pock-marked with holes and the one to the south has deep gouges where wagon wheels have gotten bogged down making the tight turn during rainy season."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":50,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":28,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":30,"x":-280,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["A marked improvement in this road's construction and care is evident when compared to that of the West Valley Road.  The sturdy roadbed, lined with pavers, is wide enough for several carts to pass each other on their way in and out of the Gate to Inner Hibarnhvidar.  On either side of the road, small shops and itinerant merchants cater to those traversing the highway."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":29,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":-260,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["Just off the road a battered shack dispenses occasional pulses of water into a small ditch that, when full, drains into an open pipe.  To the south, the tops of grand homes form geometric shapes against the night sky while to the northeast the entire city is cloaked in a shadowy basin as it slopes down between the mountains.  A wood platform, complete with noose, stands sentinel casting ghostly shadows that blend with those over the lower section of the city.","Just off the road a battered shack dispenses occasional pulses of water into a small ditch that, when full, drains into an open pipe.  The tops of grand homes can be seen to the south while to the northeast the entire city opens in a kaleidoscopic view as it slopes down between the mountains.  A wood platform, complete with noose, stands where it can be viewed from almost any spot in the lower section of the city."],"exits":[{"to":32,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":30,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":-240,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["Set on a slight ledge, this road separates the upper and lower sections of Outer Hibarnhvidar.  The upper city looks down and most of the city below looks up to easily view the traffic on this road.  Though utilized only for public shaming, the weathered stocks that edge the roadway serve as a caution to visitors as well as citizens that this city enforces its values."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":31,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":-220,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["Roads from all the cardinal directions intersect here, which results in an enormous amount of both wheeled and mounted traffic.  Also heavily traveled by those on foot, a row of wood slats has been laid next to the main roadbed on both sides to allow pedestrians safer passage.  Over time, the unsecured wood boards have become skewed when slower moving pushcarts have been crowded off the main road."],"exits":[{"to":56,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":34,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":38,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":32,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":-139,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["Movement is slowed in this area by the sheer numbers of those passing out of the Inner City and those headed toward it.  The entire lower city utilizes this thoroughfare to cross from one side to another in an attempt to avoid those sections of Outer Hibarnhvidar with less than savory reputations."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":33,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":-119,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["The few lackluster stands that line the road in this spot seek to make their fortunes on quantity instead of quality.  Fights erupt between the merchants -- to the delight of those stuck in traffic -- and constant price wars eliminate profits more often than not.  Nailed to a signpost erected on the low side of the road is a painted sign whose message smeared into oblivion when the letters ran in the rain."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":34,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":36,"x":-99,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Upper Gate Road","descriptions":["Traffic backs up on the wide and solidly paved avenue, forming a line whose occupants wait their turn to enter the Great Gate.  Sounds drift downward from the Great Gate Road and blend with the sounds of the road's milling carts creating a harmony with the cacophony that is the mark of Outer Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":35,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":37,"x":-80,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Before the Great Gate","descriptions":["A huge five-sided arch has been carved into the sheer face of the mountain, brightly illuminated by scores of torches set into iron brackets along the rocky walls.  The massive stone gate stands open, leading inside to relative darkness.  High overhead, a crenellated wall has been carved out of the cliff, accessible presumably from within the tunnel fastness.  The occasional the clink of metal on rock can be heard, marking the presence of Dwarven guards.","A huge five-sided arch has been carved into the sheer face of the mountain.  The massive stone gate stands open, leading inside to relative darkness.  High overhead, a crenellated wall has been carved out of the cliff, accessible presumably from within the tunnel fastness.  The occasional glint of metal marks the presence of Dwarven guards.","A huge five-sided arch has been carved into the sheer face of the mountain, brightly illuminated by scores of torches set into iron brackets along the rocky walls.  The massive stone gate stands open, leading inside to relative darkness.  High overhead, a crenellated wall has been carved out of the cliff, accessible presumably from within the tunnel fastness.  The occasional clink of metal on rock can be heard, marking the presence of Dwarven guards."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":53,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":75,"exit":"go","move":"go double-doored gate"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":-220,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["Nestled against the sheer rise of the mountain that contains Inner Hibarnhvidar, this area is part of a U-shaped belt that surrounds the sprawling darkened streets of the outer city.  A lonely tree casts its shadow over the roadbed, having taken root in a crack partway up the granite wall.","Nestled against the sheer rise of the mountain that contains Inner Hibarnhvidar, this area is part of a U-shaped belt that surrounds the sprawling streets of the outer city.  A lonely tree leans over the roadbed having taken root in a crack partway up the granite wall."],"exits":[{"to":33,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":39,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":239,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}]},
  {"id":39,"x":-200,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["The sleepy pace of the darkened side streets is broken as garbage collection and street cleaning rotates through its narrow alleys.  The service folk must be finished before the inhabitants awake to do business with the denizens of the Inner City.  To the southwest, the gold-tone on a cupola glints above the buildings that crowd the west side of the street.","Home to those who do business with the denizens of the Inner City, this narrow strip and crowded side streets are crammed with bustling activity.  To the southwest, a gold-toned cupola rises above the buildings that line the west side of the street."],"exits":[{"to":40,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":38,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":40,"x":-200,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["The silvery windows of this street's substantial homes reflect the night sky as they face the cliff wall across the road.  Almost hidden in the cliff's shadow, flags flutter from a small wagon set up on the southeast corner of the intersection.  Discerning eyes might notice a clerk has curled up beneath it for the evening, ready to serve any late shoppers.","The silvery windows of this street's substantial homes reflect the cliff wall across the road.  Bright flags flutter from a small wagon set up on the southeast corner of the intersection.  Further south is a shopping area where fresh produce can be purchased making it a prime destination for the housewives of the area."],"exits":[{"to":39,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":41,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Peddler's Wagon"]},
  {"id":41,"x":-200,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["Darkened shops have moved their display stands indoors leaving a wide promenade that could be better utilized during the day.  The nightly street cleaning has left some of the paving stones surrounded by little lakes.  Somewhere in the city a door slams which starts the neighborhood dogs barking.","Fresh produce markets compete with each other not only for customers but also for precious space.  Their outdoor stands thrust forward from the actual buildings leaving barely enough room for shoppers to pass.  A loud hawker down a side street proclaims the virtues of his merchandise in a voice honed raspy with use."],"exits":[{"to":40,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":42,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":245,"exit":"go","move":"go grocery"},{"to":246,"exit":"go","move":"go fruit shop"}]},
  {"id":42,"x":-220,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["On this side of Valley Road the homes are crammed together, with bare inches separating the rich from the poor.  Some of the hovels that line the main road have relinquished the air space over their roofs when a more well-to-do resident extended their second story over it.  Behind a flimsy wood barricade, a dog voices his displeasure with all who come near his turf."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":43,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":43,"x":-240,"y":270,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["Resourceful souls seeking business with the Dwarves within Hibarnhvidar utilized the available natural materials lying about to build homes and shops.  The irregularly shaped stones lend visual character and charm to what otherwise would have been a gloomy shantytown.  Carved troughs, crafted by apprentice stonemasons, have been arranged two deep on the mountain side of the street, the rear one for plants and flowers and the front one to catch rain water for pack animals."],"exits":[{"to":42,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":44,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":44,"x":-260,"y":290,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Valley Road","descriptions":["Squeezed between the soaring mountains, the narrow road curves northwest where helter-skelter construction is an ongoing process.  A small shed built in front of a house has closed its shutters for the night leaving only the dwindling scent of fresh adogbarg.","Squeezed between the soaring mountains, the narrow road curves northwest where helter-skelter construction is an ongoing process.  A small shed built in front of a house shelters an old woman whose griddles and batter spread the scent of vanilla and butter into the Gor'Tog district to the south as she cooks adogbargs to sell for a pittance."],"exits":[{"to":43,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":57,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":45,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":45,"x":-280,"y":270,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Few of the tall trees that once grew on this mountainside survived the demands for space and construction supplies.  Most have been chopped down and put to use as stilts upon which homes precariously balance over the valley.  Wide stones placed in cuts in the mountain form shadowy stairways to Hibarnhvidar's aerial neighborhoods.","Few of the tall trees that once grew on this mountainside survived the demands for space and construction supplies.  Most have been chopped down and put to use as stilts upon which homes precariously balance over the valley.  Wide stones placed in cuts in the mountain form stairways to Hibarnhvidar's aerial neighborhoods."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":46,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden bridge"}]},
  {"id":46,"x":-300,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Desultory trickles of water dribble down from the hillside and inner city to gather in a pond spanned by a small bridge.  The brackish water is the result of wastes and garbage funneled here when the rains come or the streets are cleaned.  A few darkened homes are clustered on the east side of the street, as far away from the smell of the effluent as possible.","Desultory trickles of water dribble down from the hillside and inner city to gather in a pond spanned by a small bridge.  The brackish water is the result of wastes and garbage funneled here when the rains come or the streets are cleaned.  A few homes are clustered on the east side of the street, as far away from the smell of the effluent as possible."],"exits":[{"to":47,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":45,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden bridge"}]},
  {"id":47,"x":-300,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["The poorest residents of Outer Hibarnhvidar utilize any available material to build their homes.  There are thatched huts, wooden sheds, piled-stone structures, metal lean-tos, tents, mud-brick hovels and hybrids made from several materials.  The residences along this part of the street seem to cower beneath the lavish homes on the hillside and the shopping district to the east."],"exits":[{"to":48,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":46,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":247,"exit":"go","move":"go threadbare tent"}]},
  {"id":48,"x":-300,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["During the night hours the bustling atmosphere and warm smiles of the residents are missing, leaving this narrow space claustrophobic, dark and gloomy.  Most of the ground is covered with buildings or streets, and only a few patches of earth aren't overshadowed by the towering mountains of granite that gird this area.  A sound like that of a sick pig emanates from an open window overhead but is probably only loud snoring.","Were it not for the bustling atmosphere and warm smiles of the residents, this narrow space could feel claustrophobic, dark and gloomy.  Most of the ground is covered with buildings or streets and only a few tiny patches of earth remain visible, overshadowed by the towering mountains of granite that gird this area.  The sound of children squealing with delight emanates from an open window overhead out of which bobs a bright red balloon."],"exits":[{"to":49,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":47,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":455,"exit":"go","move":"go brick shop"}]},
  {"id":49,"x":-300,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["Spacious homes cluster in the shadows of a large stone edifice whose gold cupola is visible even during the darkest night.  Atop the dome is a sculpture rendered in such a stylistic manner that it is impossible to discern the sculpture from the shadows it throws.  Down the side street the weary shopkeepers have taken their wares in and closed for the night.","Spacious homes cluster around a large stone edifice whose gold cupola glistens in the light.  Atop the dome is a sculpture rendered in such a stylistic manner that it is impossible to discern what it was designed to represent.  Down the side street several shops have set up colorful displays in front of their doors."],"exits":[{"to":50,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":48,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":50,"x":-300,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, West Valley Road","descriptions":["A multitude of shadowy buildings forms waves of colors and heights as this U-shaped area slopes gently downward towards a narrow passageway through the cliffs.  Stilt homes overlook the jumble, and sounds and scents blend into the distinctive mix of Outer Hibarnhvidar.  Chunky brown stones, dumped when the inner city was excavated, now form a solid roadbed that withstands the ravages of weather and time.","A multitude of buildings forms waves of colors and heights as this U-shaped area slopes gently downward towards a narrow passageway through the cliffs.  Stilt homes overlook the jumble, and sounds and scents blend into the distinctive mix of Outer Hibarnhvidar.  Chunky brown stones, dumped when the inner city was excavated, now form a solid roadbed that withstands the ravages of weather and time."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":49,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":439,"exit":"go","move":"go building"}]},
  {"id":51,"x":-140,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Great Gate Road","descriptions":["Stately and broad, and lined with massive rune-carved menhirs, the road points straight southeast toward the sheer side of the mountain against which the town is built.  Taking advantage of the constant traffic, enterprising shopkeepers have crowded stores of all sizes along both sides of the street."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":52,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":229,"exit":"go","move":"go discreet doorway"},{"to":230,"exit":"go","move":"go undistinguished hut"}]},
  {"id":52,"x":-120,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Great Gate Road","descriptions":["Forming the hypotenuse of the triangle between the Upper Gate and East Valley roads, the slightly elevated highway grants a superlative view of the valley and the mountain.  Each footstep on the road, which is laid with chunky stone pavers and bordered by a low wall, causes a small reverberation that creates an echo, lending weight and importance to the sojourner's progression."],"exits":[{"to":53,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":51,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":53,"x":-100,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Great Gate Road","descriptions":["Impressive as the highway is, the mountain containing Hibarnhvidar proper casts a huge shadow over the byway for the greater portion of every day.  The pavers contain dark spots of dripped grease deposited by the wheels of wagons awaiting entrance through the Great Gate."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":52,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":54,"x":-220,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["Deep channels on both sides of the roadway contain bits and pieces of many a cart driven off the side of the narrow street by oncoming traffic.  Pushed to the far side of one ditch, the bed of an abandoned wagon is full of sprung wheel rims and portions of assorted axles.  Residents of the nearby buildings have learned to ignore the sound of splintering wood."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":55,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":55,"x":-220,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["On the fringe of the city's outer section, shops here are constantly opening, closing, under construction or closed for repairs.  Traffic flows through the surrounding streets at a steady pace, but there is not enough to support the fledgling businesses that need to move deeper into the valley to survive.  An elegant street light, erected by businesses long gone, provides a focal point that actually distracts passersby from the shops on either side of the thoroughfare."],"exits":[{"to":54,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":56,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":107,"exit":"go","move":"go shop"}]},
  {"id":56,"x":-220,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, East Valley Road","descriptions":["Built of stone excavated from the inner city, and resembling a lighthouse more likely found at the seashore, a tower with a tall spire keeps watch over this area.  A picket fence surrounds the tower's broad base and serves to keep the lookout peaceful and segregated from the rabble of the outer city.  The Hibarnhvidar flag flutters atop the spire and a small light atop shines through the uppermost window.","Built of stone excavated from the inner city, and resembling a lighthouse more likely found at the seashore, a tower with a tall spire keeps watch over this area.  A picket fence surrounds the tower's broad base and serves to keep the lookout peaceful and segregated from the rabble of the outer city.  The Hibarnhvidar flag flutters atop the spire."],"exits":[{"to":55,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":33,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":57,"x":-260,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["Although not quite as busy as in the daytime, it is still far from quiet here at the beginning of the Gor'Tog District.  Passersby hurry along to the north and other parts of the city or south into the heart of Tog Town.","The hustle and bustle of many large people striding along the street marks the beginning of Hibarnhvidar's Gor'Tog district.  Those heading north to other parts of the city take somewhat careful steps lest they accidentally squash one of the local Dwarves."],"exits":[{"to":44,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":58,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":58,"x":-260,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["A rough stone building with three chimneys sits close by the road.  Roars of laughter and merriment can be heard from beyond the massive steel-banded wooden door.  A hanging sign depicting a frothing mug surrounded by four turnips identifies this as the local tavern, one of the most popular destinations in the 'Tog district."],"exits":[{"to":57,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":59,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":248,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"}]},
  {"id":59,"x":-280,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["A wide, whitewashed two-story stone building sits to one side of the street.  This is the dormitory, affectionately known as The Flophouse, where the less well-to-do residents of the neighborhood reside.  From time to time a handful of Gor'Togs, many in workmen's clothes, plod along the well-worn path to and from the front door."],"exits":[{"to":58,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":60,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":62,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":60,"x":-260,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Green","descriptions":["With the exception of an occasional hoot from a passing owl, the animals residing here are quiet for the evening.  A gaggle of grey geese sit placidly on the pond, heads tucked beneath downy wings.  The people who come here for a respite from frantic pace of the city are home now, snug in their beds.","The small pond here is home to a gaggle of grey geese.  Their constant honking makes the atmosphere less than completely relaxing.  Nevertheless, quite a few people show up to dip their toes in the water in the warmer months and skate on the ice in the winter.  A few bossy squirrels scurry about, trying to intercept bread crumbs meant for the birds."],"exits":[{"to":61,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":59,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":61,"x":-260,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Green","descriptions":["Tall hedges run along the edges of this pleasant park-like expanse.  This is a popular spot earlier in the day, but few visitors remain and stirrings are infrequent.  Dominating the view is a life-sized statue of Uthmor the Giant, although judging by the mess at the base, some of the local dogs are less than impressed.","Tall hedges run along the edges of this pleasant park-like expanse.  A few of the locals stroll by, enjoying the surroundings.  Dominating the view is a life-sized statue of Uthmor the Giant, although judging by the mess at the base, some of the local dogs are less than impressed."],"exits":[{"to":60,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":68,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":62,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":62,"x":-280,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["The grass is worn away on the edges of the roads here, effectively widening the thoroughfares where they meet at this busy intersection.  Many a pedestrian has veered to the side to avoid the wagons, working animals and some of the more aggressive walkers that dominate the center."],"exits":[{"to":59,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":61,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":67,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":63,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":63,"x":-300,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["The aroma of fresh-baked bread wafts from a sturdy hut built along the hillside.  Yellow-painted flowerboxes sit beneath the windows on either side of the wide wooden door, also yellow.  A hanging sign shows a picture of a smiling Gor'Tog matron holding a large tray of muffins."],"exits":[{"to":62,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":64,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":252,"exit":"go","move":"go sturdy hut"}]},
  {"id":64,"x":-320,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["A few hardy mountain goats, seemingly more intent on their grazing than on the world around them, roam within the confines of a whitewashed picket fence.  Two rain barrels sit on either side of a small, neat vegetable garden, which thrives despite the rocky soil, a testament to the determination of the Gor'Togs who live here."],"exits":[{"to":63,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":65,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":65,"x":-340,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["A few squat homes are scattered about the area.  Built on a hillside, the houses have their front ends propped up on stout wooden stilts to keep the floors level."],"exits":[{"to":64,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":66,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":66,"x":-360,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Rocky Trail","descriptions":["This small winding road meanders to an end here -- about halfway up the hill that rises to the south of the city.  Flowing down from above, the thin creek that provides water to the local Gor'Togs runs over timeworn slabs of shale as it wends its way toward the center of Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":65,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":67,"x":-280,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["As the street tops a rise, a panoramic view of the city spreads out to the north.  Nearby are the residential parts of this district and the Green.  Further north are the Trade, Gate, and Shop districts, with the Valley Roads curling around them to the east and west.  Beyond the northern wall of the outer city is the famous water wheel, drawing power from the mighty Segoltha.  The Himeneldar Shel mountains loom majestically to the south, protecting Hibarnhvidar from any possible threat from that direction."],"exits":[{"to":62,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":68,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":69,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":68,"x":-260,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Green","descriptions":["All is quiet here at this hour.  A few child-sized divots and discarded broken sticks used as toy swords are all that betray the frenetic energy present here during daylight.","Several Gor'Togs relax and chat on this wide swath of grass.  As their mothers watch fondly, a group of very young togglers attempt to play togball with an extremely displeased cat."],"exits":[{"to":61,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":67,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":254,"exit":"go","move":"go flagstone hut"}]},
  {"id":69,"x":-260,"y":410,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["A modest stone hut stands amid an assortment of boulders and smaller rocks.  Pebbles, sharp chips and a layer of coarse dust suggest that someone has been at work breaking the larger pieces down.  A pickaxe and shovel lean against the side of the building, lending support to this conclusion.  A narrow dirt path leads around to the back."],"exits":[{"to":70,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":74,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":67,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":255,"exit":"go","move":"go dirt path"}]},
  {"id":70,"x":-240,"y":410,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Pebble Lane","descriptions":["An example of local Gor'Tog art can be seen amid an otherwise unremarkable patch of grass and dirt.  On a background of tan rocks, cleverly placed stones form a large brown chicken pecking at the ground.  Begawk!"],"exits":[{"to":71,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":69,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":71,"x":-220,"y":410,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Pebble Lane","descriptions":["In a cleared space by the side of the road is a large ring of grey stones.  Within it, black rocks are arranged in the form of a charging bull.  His horns are formed from tight groupings of white pebbles."],"exits":[{"to":72,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":70,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":72,"x":-200,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Pebble Lane","descriptions":["Cunningly arranged colored stones are placed within a black square on the ground, forming a crude but clear design near the side of the road.  A bright red dragon is shown in flight within a pale blue sky.  A puff of grey-white smoke escapes its nostrils."],"exits":[{"to":73,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":71,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":73,"x":-180,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Pebble Lane","descriptions":["Sloping slightly upward to the east, the road ends here in a cul-de-sac.  A large grouping of stones forms a pattern set into the hillside: a snow white dove is set off by a contrasting field of black gravel."],"exits":[{"to":72,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":74,"x":-260,"y":430,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Granite Street","descriptions":["The road reaches its peak as it ends here, affording a view of the rest of the town to the north and abutting the mountain to the south.  A wooden fence, built by some careful residents, prevents the unwary from stepping off a small cliff that falls away to the southeast."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":256,"exit":"go","move":"go stone building"}]},
  {"id":75,"x":-60,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Entry","descriptions":["Framed at each end by a massive five-sided arch, this long passage is brightly lit by flaming torches in paired iron cressets.  At one end are the stone gates to Outer Hibarnhvidar, lying flat against the smooth walls, ready to be closed should danger threaten.  At the other end, iron gates stand open allowing entrance to the Inner city.  A warm breeze from within the mountain sighs past, carrying the sounds of bustling commerce, and a faint odor of hammered metal."],"exits":[{"to":76,"exit":"go","move":"go iron gate"},{"to":37,"exit":"go","move":"go stone gate"}],"color":"#808000","aliases":["Entry","Kraelyst start point","travel start point"]},
  {"id":76,"x":0,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The North Colonnade","descriptions":["Blasted from solid rock, and lovingly carved over thousands of anlaen by untold numbers of Dwarven craftsmen, the workmanship in this huge cavern cannot be matched outside Hibarnhvidar.  Thick, ornate columns support a balcony that looms over the eastern side of the hall, causing the area beneath it to disappear into the gloom save for the occasional glint of light reflected off treasured gold work.  To the northwest, ponderous leaves of hammered iron form the arch to Outer Hibarnhvidar.","Meticulously crafted, ponderous leaves of hammered iron form the arch to Outer Hibarnhvidar.  A balcony looms over the eastern side of the hall, causing the area beneath it to disappear into the gloom."],"exits":[{"to":99,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":98,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":97,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":77,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":75,"exit":"go","move":"go five-sided arch"},{"to":138,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}]},
  {"id":77,"x":-20,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The West Colonnade","descriptions":["Dark stains splattered over the wall and floor have permanently discolored the granite.  The carved herbs that decorate the wall and interior archway are in some places buried beneath layers of discoloration.  One possible explanation for the stale, coppery scent in this area is that it is considered honorable to have been severely wounded in the service of Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":76,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":105,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":78,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":206,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"}]},
  {"id":78,"x":-20,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The West Colonnade","descriptions":["Gold leaf defines the edges of the carvings on the wall while those on the ceiling and inside of the arch are outlined in silver.  Finished in black and white tile, this floor bestows the illusion of importance to all who pass through as it sends their footsteps reverberating through the gallery.  Set on a small table against the wall is an old scale with some weights next to it."],"exits":[{"to":77,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":105,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":79,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":203,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}]},
  {"id":79,"x":-20,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The West Colonnade","descriptions":["Staid and proper, the granite here is carved in interlocking circles, some of which resemble rings, others bracelets, others necklaces and still others beard jewelry.  Sprinkled judiciously throughout the carvings are actual gems.  A half-moon arch looks out upon the central plaza, teaming with the life of this underground city."],"exits":[{"to":78,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":105,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":80,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":209,"exit":"go","move":"go doors"}]},
  {"id":80,"x":0,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The South Colonnade","descriptions":["Instead of columns supporting the balcony, this area is partitioned from the center of the hall by a carved open-work stone wall that mimics a trellis covered with climbing white roses in full bloom.  The balcony above, reached by a spiral staircase, is supported by the latticework wall fashioned in memory of The Rose Maiden Caverns."],"exits":[{"to":95,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":94,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":81,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":79,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":142,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}]},
  {"id":81,"x":20,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The South Colonnade","descriptions":["A massive stairway to the balcony spirals against the far wall, its posts carved with tusked animals.  Except for the stairway, this entire space is an arched tunnel whose walls are engraved with what could well be the names of every Dwarf who worked on the construction of Hibarnhvidar.  On either side, the vista opens to soaring heights, allowing the larger area's illumination to dispel any shadows."],"exits":[{"to":94,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":104,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":82,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":80,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":135,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}]},
  {"id":82,"x":20,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tontawr Tunal","descriptions":["The roof of this cavern angles from the grandiose height of the Great Hall to the north to the lesser arch of the Tunal to the south.  Several candle wheels at different heights spread light to the adjoining areas.  A slowly growing wax drip hangs off one side of the highest wheel above another lit candle.  It appears that at times it gets close to the heat of the candle below, and its molten wax extinguishes the lower flame.  Several wax mounds on the floor indicate this is a common occurrence."],"exits":[{"to":81,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":83,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":83,"x":20,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tontawr Tunal","descriptions":["Not quite as ornately embellished as the rooms in the center hall, this tunnel is nevertheless decorated with moments from the city's history, carved into the walls in great detail."],"exits":[{"to":82,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":84,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":84,"x":20,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tontawr Tunal","descriptions":["This tunnel exudes an air of formality partly created by the illusion that a giant runner covers the floor.  Polished granite is bordered on either side by a red marble strip that edges shallow channels where the walls meet the floor.  Neither the marble nor the granite does much to deaden the heavy footsteps of the Dwarves who travel this corridor."],"exits":[{"to":83,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":85,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":456,"exit":"go","move":"go rough-hewn opening"}]},
  {"id":85,"x":20,"y":270,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tontawr Tunal","descriptions":["Subdued echoes carry footsteps whose origins are masked by the semi-circular walls that toss sound around with great ease.  Every so often, it is possible to discern a few complete words, most of which are probably portions of orders or curses issued by the city's guards or their prey.  Hung at eye level for a Dwarf is a small gold sign with an arrow that points south."],"exits":[{"to":84,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":86,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":86,"x":20,"y":290,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["Air and light filter down in patches from somewhere above the far recesses of the arched ceiling.  The dark grey granite walls have been inlaid with lighter shades of rose and cream to form frames around two bas-relief murals depicting epic moments in Dwarven history.  When compared to the bustle of the main cavern and the echoes of the tunnel, this area's subdued ambience befits the nearby administrative hub of the city."],"exits":[{"to":85,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":92,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":87,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":91,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":87,"x":20,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["Three granite pedestals form an isosceles triangle that is the mirror image of the layout in the room to the south.  Small gold placards affixed to the base of each pedestal briefly comment on the artist and history of the piece.  A narrow bench before each statue provides a place from which to study the artwork."],"exits":[{"to":86,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":92,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":93,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":88,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":90,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":91,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":88,"x":20,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["Three granite pedestals form an isosceles triangle that is the mirror image of the layout in the room to the north.  Small gold placards affixed to the base of each pedestal briefly comment on the artist and history of the piece.  A narrow bench before each statue provides a place from which to study the artwork."],"exits":[{"to":87,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":92,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":93,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":89,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":90,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":91,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":89,"x":20,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["The highly polished silvery granite walls mirror a mosaic floor laid to mimic the flow and shoreline of the Biiskbowr River.  Copper edging delineates the tile river from a small space along the west wall, where an ornate bench allows visitors to contemplate the river while they wait for those with business behind the double doors."],"exits":[{"to":88,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":93,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":90,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":195,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"}]},
  {"id":90,"x":0,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["The walls and floor of gold-veined grey marble create the perfect setting for an alabaster sculpture of the Bard Starastone.  Sometimes a Bard will sit behind a grey screen and play Threnody on a Child's Death which sends the notes drifting through the chamber towards the song's words incised into the west wall.  A small gold plaque is affixed to the base of the statue."],"exits":[{"to":91,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":87,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":88,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":89,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":91,"x":0,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["The granite out of which this area was carved is a mix of deep green and black with specks of white, which has been polished to a glassy shine.  Inlaid in an argyle pattern, thin gold bands both brighten and lend a subdued, formal air befitting the entrance to Hibarnhvidar's seat of Justice.  Two high-backed benches that can seat five rest against the wall on either side of an imposing door."],"exits":[{"to":86,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":87,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":88,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":90,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":200,"exit":"go","move":"go impressive door"}]},
  {"id":92,"x":40,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["Sufficiently mottled to appear wood-like, long, wide slabs of carved and polished brown granite cover the walls.  The alternating tiles on the floor are either light sandstone or a rose and cream interspersed with flecks of silver.  Dangling from a substantial gold chain, a sign hangs next to a carved inverted-panel mahogany door."],"exits":[{"to":93,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":88,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":87,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":86,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":187,"exit":"go","move":"go mahogany door"}]},
  {"id":93,"x":40,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Borg Kwarf","descriptions":["Roughly cleaved granite in its natural state forms the walls and floor in this portion of the cavern.  The angles and bare stone somehow muffle sounds from elsewhere, recreating the environment first encountered by Hibarnhvidar's founders.  There is neither artwork nor decorations nor monuments -- there is only a small sign incised into one wall."],"exits":[{"to":92,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":89,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":88,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":87,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":188,"exit":"go","move":"go wide entryway"}]},
  {"id":94,"x":20,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["Suspended from Hibarnhvidar's barrel-vaulted ceilings are wax-encrusted wagon wheels containing candles melted to various lengths.  A lone Dwarf pushes a contraption that is more stepladder than cart, with which he makes his rounds replacing the stubs that no longer sufficiently illuminate the glory of Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":95,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":104,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":81,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":80,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":293,"exit":"go","move":"go doors"}]},
  {"id":95,"x":20,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["The intricacy of the intaglio floor here differs only in layout from its twin on the other side of the central room, being an exact mirror image.  Thin veins of marble inlaid with a jeweler's precision divide the Dwarven shield in the center from the eight panels depicting the history of Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":96,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":106,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":104,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":94,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":80,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":105,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":96,"x":20,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["All things flow to this, the center of life in Hibarnhvidar.  Even the drafts carry scents peculiar to this underground city -- smoke and roasting meat, stone dust and heated steel, the sour sweat of Dwarven craftsmen, and the incense used to sweeten the trapped air.  A marble sculpture of Taratochs occupies the center of the hall."],"exits":[{"to":97,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":106,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":95,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":105,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":419,"exit":"go","move":"go meeting portal"}],"color":"#FF00FF","aliases":["Premium Portal","Portal"]},
  {"id":97,"x":20,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["Complex sets of ribs give a net-like appearance to the vaulted ceilings as they soar two stories high -- well over the side balconies -- to disappear into the darkness just above statues nestled between the net-like blind tracery embellishing the solid walls.  Elaborate columns encircle this cavern, concealing some areas in shadow as they stoically rise to support the arcade and restrain its thousands of pounds of rock from crashing down on the stone floor."],"exits":[{"to":98,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":100,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":106,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":96,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":105,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":76,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":98,"x":20,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["The bedrock floor, incised in blocks of alternating squares and triangles, reveals the travel patterns of the city.  The more heavily trafficked a direction is, the more worn the pavement.  Pale echoes from all over the city reverberate off the stones and populate this great hall with the choir of life.  Solid rock neither forgives nor absorbs."],"exits":[{"to":99,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":100,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":97,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":76,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":99,"x":20,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The North Colonnade","descriptions":["Stone steps whose centers have become shiny and indented from generations of traffic spiral around an enormous central pillar.  Posts carved in the likeness of different weapons support the railing on this circular staircase.  Behind the prominent staircase, carved ivy garlands form the arch that leads from beneath the balcony deeper into the mountain."],"exits":[{"to":100,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":98,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":76,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":137,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"},{"to":294,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}],"color":"#FF00FF","aliases":["North Colonnade"]},
  {"id":100,"x":40,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The North Colonnade","descriptions":["A stone bench, its gargantuan proportions calling to mind a race considerably larger than Dwarves, provides a king-sized view of the main cavern while remaining discreetly concealed in the shadows beneath the balcony.  A mosaic fills the wall behind the bench, and an archway in the wall has a border of carved steins set between piles of malt, hops and wheat.  Above the archway is a gem-encrusted sign that proclaims Bowr."],"exits":[{"to":101,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":97,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":98,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":99,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":276,"exit":"go","move":"go carved arch"}]},
  {"id":101,"x":60,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The East Colonnade","descriptions":["A stairway spirals around a central incised column as it rises to an upper balcony.  The steps and railing are hewn from granite, their coarse texture contrasting with the detail in the posts supporting the railing.  Each post is an exact replica of a famous shield, some of them overlaid with precious metals."],"exits":[{"to":102,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":106,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":100,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":108,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"},{"to":284,"exit":"go","move":"go recessed doorway"},{"to":492,"exit":"go","move":"go steel archway"}]},
  {"id":102,"x":60,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The East Colonnade","descriptions":["The granite ceiling is carved into large squares that depict banners and flags carried by Dwarven clans.  The floor tiles show the same subjects, but are inlaid with gold, silver, jet, lapis, jade and bloodstone, bringing the banners to colorful life.  An ornate but extremely substantial door provides entrance to the Carousel."],"exits":[{"to":101,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":103,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":106,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":286,"exit":"go","move":"go ornate door"}]},
  {"id":103,"x":60,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The East Colonnade","descriptions":["The granite from which Hibarnhvidar was carved assumes a different appearance according to what the stonemason had in mind.  Here, the arch and all supports including the back wall beneath the balcony were fashioned by a master artisan into the finest stone latticework -- fine both in quality and delicate appearance.  Tiny caved vines resplendent with ivy leaves entwine themselves into the fretwork to create a work of art.","The granite from which Hibarnhvidar was carved assumes a different appearance according to what the stonemason had in mind.  Here, the arch and all supports including the back wall beneath the balcony were fashioned by a master artisan into the finest stone latticework -- fine both in quality and delicate appearance.  Tiny carved vines resplendent with ivy leaves entwine themselves into the fretwork to create a work of art."],"exits":[{"to":102,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":104,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":106,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":133,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"},{"to":291,"exit":"go","move":"go glittering door"}]},
  {"id":104,"x":40,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, The South Colonnade","descriptions":["Some of the areas under the ornate balcony grant access to establishments necessary for the city to function.  The detailed mural on this wall has had its impasto so thickly applied that not only do the points on the Dwarven armor protrude, but the warrior's beards are deeply textured.  Depicting the Dwarven army pursuing a retreating enemy, the artist has rendered the losing side faceless in celebration of innumerable Dwarven routs."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":81,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":94,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":95,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":292,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow arch"}]},
  {"id":105,"x":0,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["Semi-precious stones set in the facade of arches beneath the balcony reflect the true Dwarven style of opulence.  A garland of amethyst jadice flowers graces the northwest arch while to the west white topaz forms the Haakish word awdh.  To the southwest three rings interlock -- one of bloodstone, lapis, and jade, the second of onyx, topaz and hematite, and the wide third band is gold."],"exits":[{"to":97,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":96,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":95,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":79,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":78,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":77,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":106,"x":40,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Main Cavern","descriptions":["The merchants set beneath the balconies preempt the ornate architecture of this cavern.  Set in the tympanum of the arch to the northeast is an ornate enameled shield, while the eastern arch depicts a locked vault such as one would use to store valuables.  When the gate to the northwest opens, a slight breeze sets the candles lighting the cavern flickering and creates the illusion of movement by the fashionably dressed Dwarves who linger over the southwest arch."],"exits":[{"to":101,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":102,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":103,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":95,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":96,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":97,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":107,"x":-239,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Hawst Tarshar, Herbs","descriptions":["Shelves line the walls of the tiny shop, each divided into boxy compartments.  Wicker baskets hold lichens, dried roots and other ingredients that perfume the air with a dusty, herbal fragrance.  Stacks of empty burlap bags along the far wall bear stenciled names of lowland herbs imported by traders, waiting to be filled with the mountains' bounty."],"exits":[{"to":55,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Herbs"]},
  {"id":108,"x":40,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The path of the balcony follows the gentle curve of the wall.  Mounted in the center of the wall, a large iron lantern holds the shadows at bay, ensuring that travelers keep their footing.  A thin wooden pole hangs from iron chains that descend from the darkness, supporting a trio of green fabric banners that sway slightly at the touch of any breeze.","Mounted in the center of the wall, a large iron lantern holds the shadows at bay.  A thin wooden pole hangs from iron chains, supporting a trio of green fabric banners."],"exits":[{"to":109,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":136,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":101,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}]},
  {"id":109,"x":40,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A thickly padded stone bench sits near the edge of the balcony, separated from open air only by the iron chains mounted between the columns on either side.  Noise echoes from the continuous bustle below, amplified by the granite cavern.  The image of a star is chiseled into the floor, with heavy attention paid to the directional points that indicate where one may travel."],"exits":[{"to":108,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":110,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":133,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":110,"x":60,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A stone plaque is mounted on the north wall of this passage, illuminated by well-tended torchlight.  Additional torches are positioned the length of the tunnel, placed alternately on opposite walls every few feet.  The path cants slightly, descending from west to east, as it widens to allow for the passage of groups traveling together."],"exits":[{"to":111,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":109,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":111,"x":80,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A steep incline marks this section of the passageway.  Shallow steps carved into the granite run along the center of the incline, providing an easier option for those who struggle on hills.  On either side of the steps, stone ramps with thin grooves accommodate any wheeled transport needing to traverse the incline.  Large iron lanterns are mounted on each wall, bathing the steps in light."],"exits":[{"to":112,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":110,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":112,"x":100,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A ramp with steps down its center descends to the west, banking slightly before merging with the main passage.  Torches mounted high on the walls extend light upward many feet before the walls disappear into inky blackness.  The rough granite rises steeply on either side of the path with no hint of curve to indicate how high the tunnel ascends."],"exits":[{"to":113,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":111,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":132,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":113,"x":120,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Walls of granite rise high on either side of the large cavern, arching at the top into the smooth curve of the ceiling.  Bright light from multiple lanterns and torches illuminates the area, giving an almost day-like appearance.  Occasional pinging sounds drift among the hushed murmurs that echo off the granite.  A small stone plaque is mounted on the north wall."],"exits":[{"to":120,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":114,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":119,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":112,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":475,"exit":"go","move":"go iron hatchway"}]},
  {"id":114,"x":140,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Rimmed by smooth stones evenly spaced, a reflecting pool serves as artistic companion to the large stalagmite located to the east.  The edges of the stones are uniformly rounded.  Small waves along the sides of the pool hint at an underground stream whose flow continues to provide the pool with fresh water."],"exits":[{"to":120,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":118,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":115,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":117,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":119,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":113,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":167,"exit":"go","move":"go moongate"}]},
  {"id":115,"x":160,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A stalagmite rises from the center of the area, pointed toward the arched stone ceiling high above.  Benches of polished wood mounted on stone ring the natural art.  Granite paths worn smooth by tool and foot curve around the seating area, branching off like wheel-spokes in several directions."],"exits":[{"to":118,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":116,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":117,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":119,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":114,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":120,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":116,"x":180,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The ceiling arcs lower than the main cavern due to the walkway overhead, with the path of the balcony following the curve of the wall.  Torches mounted at intervals along the wall provide adequate lighting, despite the shadow caused by the stalagmite to the west.  The shadow touches most of the area, halting several inches from a lit entry."],"exits":[{"to":117,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":115,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":118,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":318,"exit":"go","move":"go lit entry"}]},
  {"id":117,"x":160,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A thin stream of water courses down the granite wall, originating from a source beyond sight.  The stream funnels into a stone chute which branches into two smaller channels.  One channel guides the stream through an intricate system of alleys that meander over an archway before exiting into a small pool below.  The other channel deposits water into a shallow copper pan punctured with tiny holes.  Hammered tin squares are mounted at various levels below the pan, announcing the rain shower melodically."],"exits":[{"to":115,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":116,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":119,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":114,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":315,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}]},
  {"id":118,"x":160,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["An ogee arch rises high in the north wall, a beribboned spinner hanging from the center point.  Thin streamers in hues of russet, grey, green, blue, and yellow trail from the circular spinner, shifting and twirling with any passing breeze.  Twin niches flank the arch, mirroring the doorway in shape.  The air feels slightly heavy, and a faint crackling sound emanates from the niche on the left."],"exits":[{"to":116,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":115,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":114,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":120,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":336,"exit":"go","move":"go ogee arch"}]},
  {"id":119,"x":140,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The hum of voices mingles with a soft musical pinging coming from the east.  The cavern ceiling towers high above lit by the torches and lanterns on this level, as well as those of the second level.  An elaborate five-sided arch marks the entrance to a smaller tunnel leading south.  A small stone plaque is mounted on the southwest wall."],"exits":[{"to":114,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":115,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":117,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":121,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":113,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":120,"x":140,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The granite floor is darker here than in the rest of the cavern, inclining slightly to a recessed arch in the center of the wall.  Etched into the rock around the arch are the words Life Is Held Within.  A small bucket of water and a mop stand unobtrusively to the side of the entrance, ready for use.  To the left of the opening, a copper emblem embedded in granite adorns the wall."],"exits":[{"to":118,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":115,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":114,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":113,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":367,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}]},
  {"id":121,"x":140,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Well-lit and tall enough for a Gor'Tog to stand comfortably, the tunnel seems almost cozy compared to the echoing spaces of the larger caverns.  The rounded ceiling arches overhead, carved with criss-crossing beams of rock.  To either side, forged metal cressets are sunk into the stone in matched pairs."],"exits":[{"to":119,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":122,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":457,"exit":"go","move":"go glass door"}]},
  {"id":122,"x":140,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The floor slopes down to the south, and every few paces a shallow stairstep is carved into the rock.  The granite was left somewhat rough by its builders, presumably so as to give better traction to those walking over it daily.  The constant passage of many feet, though, has created a slightly polished pathway down the center of the tunnel."],"exits":[{"to":121,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":123,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":466,"exit":"climb","move":"climb circular staircase"}]},
  {"id":123,"x":140,"y":220,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The sloping floor levels somewhat, with only an occasional step down carved into the matte granite.  Warm air blows gently from an archway to the south, carrying the scent of forges and red-hot iron, and the sound of metal hammered on metal."],"exits":[{"to":122,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":124,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":215,"exit":"go","move":"go opening"}]},
  {"id":124,"x":140,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Rows of gleaming marble pillars run all through this cavern, each with four yellow-glowing torches attached branchlike just over head-level.  The columns soar upward toward a ceiling high enough overhead to be lost in the darkness.  An elaborate five-sided arch marks the entrance to a smaller tunnel leading north."],"exits":[{"to":123,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":125,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":126,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":127,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":214,"exit":"go","move":"go steel door"}]},
  {"id":125,"x":160,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["One of the archways leading out of the cavern to the shops and work-caverns has been carved with the images of thousands of tiny faces.  Looking closely, each one has an individual expression and is obviously someone the artist knew and liked -- or in some cases, apparently, despised."],"exits":[{"to":130,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":129,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":126,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":124,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":126,"x":140,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Sounds of commerce and industry echo from all directions, the stone throwing them back at each other in slowly fading repetitions.  The fires of Dwarven forges glow at all hours, and indeed, such terms as day and night lose their meaning in the fastness of the carved mountain."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":125,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":130,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":129,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":128,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":127,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":127,"x":120,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The smell of hot metal fills the cavern.  In the glowing yellow light, straight lines of gold crystal running through the polished dark granite floor glisten, passing out of sight in several directions."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":126,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":129,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":128,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":429,"exit":"go","move":"go uthamar arch"}]},
  {"id":128,"x":120,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The generations of skilled Dwarven craftsmen that cleaved this cavern out of the living rock of the mountain let their imaginations run free in the carvings surrounding the arches leading to the shops and work-caverns.  One is surrounded by flowing rock-hewn ribbons pleated in an intricate pattern, others are studded with cabochon gems or tiny carvings in minute detail."],"exits":[{"to":127,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":126,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":129,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":131,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":313,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"}]},
  {"id":129,"x":140,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Lines of sparkling golden crystals in the dark sheen of the granite floor converge here in the center of the cavern to form star shapes that glisten in the warm yellow light.  Rows of pillars rise on all sides and disappear into the darkness of the ceiling high overhead like tree trunks in a night forest."],"exits":[{"to":126,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":125,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":130,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":131,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":128,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":127,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":130,"x":160,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Bands of incised parallel lines run around the walls of the cavern about chest-high to a Dwarf, rising over the five-sided tops of the low arches spaced at intervals.  Above them, every part of the walls has been carefully chiseled in a star pattern, endlessly repeated with symmetrical purity."],"exits":[{"to":125,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":131,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":129,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":126,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":314,"exit":"go","move":"go solid arch"}]},
  {"id":131,"x":140,"y":300,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Firelight spills out of a large open arch leading into the southern wall of the cavern, flickering on the polished granite floor.  The sonorous sound of hammers pounding on metal fills the air with discordant music."],"exits":[{"to":129,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":130,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":128,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":401,"exit":"go","move":"go glaes arch"}]},
  {"id":132,"x":80,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["A narrow side passage leads off from the upper cavern, ending in a nearly closed iron-barred door.  The waves of heat that pour through the opening cause beads of sweat upon the faces of the guards posted outside, their axes held ready despite the lack of obvious threat.","A narrow side passage leads off from the upper cavern, ending in a nearly closed iron-barred door.  The waves of heat that pour through the opening cause beads of sweat upon the faces of the guards posted outside, their axes held ready despite the lack of obvious threat.  A roughed out tunnel leads east."],"exits":[{"to":112,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":186,"exit":"go","move":"go iron-barred door"},{"to":493,"exit":"east","move":""}]},
  {"id":133,"x":40,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The path of the balcony follows the gentle curve of the wall.  Mounted in the center of the wall, a large iron lantern holds the shadows at bay, ensuring that travelers keep their footing.  A thin wooden pole hangs from iron chains that descend from the darkness, supporting a trio of blue fabric banners that sway slightly at the touch of any breeze."],"exits":[{"to":109,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":134,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":103,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}]},
  {"id":134,"x":20,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["The occasional babble of voices drifts from the cavern below, pierced by laughter and ebbing into a low murmur before quieting again.  An ornate tapestry drapes from a rope suspended between two iron loops mounted high on the wall.  Framed by crystal-laced granite, the bottom of the tapestry dangles a few feet from the floor of the balcony, keeping the fabric from getting dirty."],"exits":[{"to":133,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":135,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":135,"x":0,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Simple columns of stone support the upper floor, towering to the ceiling above and following the arc of the balcony.  The columns are perfectly linear from ceiling to floor, uniformly rounded but for the barrier mounted between them to protect the wayward traveler from falling.  Thick iron chains are mounted in twin rows from one column to the next.  Nestled in the curve of the wall sits a rounded bench, softly padded with a velvet cushion."],"exits":[{"to":134,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":81,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}]},
  {"id":136,"x":20,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Resounding voices and clangs sound from below as shoppers barter and mill around in the area.  Chips of crystal glint in the granite wall that rises high on one side of the balcony.  An iron sculpture is mounted on a pedestal near the wall, its blackened metal forged into the shape of a hand grasping a shield.  A copper boss on the shield serves as the only color deviation in the dark metal art."],"exits":[{"to":108,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":137,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":311,"exit":"go","move":"go bronze-banded door"}]},
  {"id":137,"x":0,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Upper Cavern","descriptions":["Simple columns of stone support the upper floor, towering to the ceiling above and following the arc of the balcony.  The columns are perfectly linear from ceiling to floor, uniformly rounded but for the barrier mounted between them to protect the wayward traveler from falling.  Thick iron chains are mounted in twin rows from one column to the next.  Nestled in the curve of the wall sits a rounded bench, softly padded with a velvet cushion."],"exits":[{"to":136,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":99,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"},{"to":145,"exit":"go","move":"go gem-studded door"}],"aliases":["Upper Cavern"]},
  {"id":138,"x":-60,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Western Cavern","descriptions":["The balcony ends at a smooth wall, hung with a tapestry embroidered in glowing jewel tones.  Behind and almost concealed by it, a narrow tunnel leads off into darkness.  Although this area apparently sees infrequent traffic, the sounds of commerce drift up from below."],"exits":[{"to":139,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":76,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"},{"to":143,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow tunnel"}]},
  {"id":139,"x":-80,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Western Cavern","descriptions":["A broad balustrade created from a sheet of intricately carved and cut-out white alabaster runs along the edge of the balcony, guarding against accidental falls.  Narrow pillars of the same material rise at intervals to the ceiling, curving just overhead."],"exits":[{"to":138,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":140,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":140,"x":-80,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Western Cavern","descriptions":["From this vantage point, the entire Main Cavern of Inner Hibarnhvidar spreads out before you, and the sounds of conversation and commerce never cease.  A pale alabaster bench placed along the balustrade glimmers in the bright candlelight."],"exits":[{"to":139,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":141,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":141,"x":-80,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Western Cavern","descriptions":["Smells drift by on a barely perceptible breeze, just identifiable as incense, burning candles, hot metal and hard-working Dwarf.  The Dwarven engineers who built this city apparently provided for a means of circulating the air, so that smoke and soot are removed and fresh, sweet air flows in."],"exits":[{"to":140,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":142,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":312,"exit":"go","move":"go copper-banded door"}]},
  {"id":142,"x":-60,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Western Cavern","descriptions":["Thousands of candles set in circular spoked candelabra hanging over the main cavern brightly illuminate the balcony.  Suspended at all levels, some of the candelabra appear almost within reach, while others are high overhead near the cavern's ceiling.  The only shadows are cast by the carved alabaster balustrade along the balcony's edge."],"exits":[{"to":141,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":80,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}]},
  {"id":143,"x":-40,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Battlements","descriptions":["Overlooking the Great Gate, the battlements have been carved into the solid rock face.  Huge kettles stand at intervals, empty now but ready to be filled with boiling oil in the event of war.  Only a single lonely guard patrols during peacetime, occasionally leaning back against the wall and enjoying a good smoke of a pipe almost as big as his head."],"exits":[{"to":144,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":138,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow tunnel"}]},
  {"id":144,"x":-20,"y":40,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Battlements","descriptions":["From this vantage point, the houses and shops of Outer Hibarnhvidar spread out in an untidy sprawl.  Thatch-roofed cottages lean against sturdy slate-roofed shops and warehouses, and whitewashed stucco mingles with brick and stonework.  Looking straight down the Great Gate Road, the rows of menhirs lining it to either side resemble grey soldiers standing at attention."],"exits":[{"to":143,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":145,"x":-20,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["A pair of Dwarven guards stands on either side of the massive gem-studded door that seals this cavern off from other areas of Hibarnhvidar's interior.  A curving pathway has been coaxed out of the stone and winds lazily around the large terraced cavern.  Though the path is easily wide enough to accommodate the occasional supply-laden caravan, a steel fence placed near the terrace's edge prevents any mishaps from excited visitors."],"exits":[{"to":146,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":137,"exit":"go","move":"go gem-studded door"}]},
  {"id":146,"x":-40,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["A small clumping of Dwarven dwellings is recessed along the cavern's wall.  Decorative silk banners and ribbons are woven into the protective fence in an effort to add color to the neighborhood and draw attention away from the drab housing and tenants.","A small clumping of Dwarven dwellings is recessed along the cavern's wall."],"exits":[{"to":145,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":147,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Harst Haalm"]},
  {"id":147,"x":-60,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["Always guarded by a small contingent of armored guards, a large structure -- carved from the stone around it -- protrudes from the wall.  As the Dwarves come and go, they stop by the racks of Dwarven axes, spears, and swords that line the sides of the armory, carefully inspecting the weaponry and replacing those that have been damaged during their sparring exercises.  In the event of threat from the outside, there can be little doubt that the Dwarves will defend the homes that line the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":146,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":148,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":148,"x":-60,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["Plain and dark, the cave doors here are crafted from iron.  Of the more prominent in view, one features a carving of badgers while another displays a pair of crossed hammers.  Between them sits a dark red clay pot with long pale feathers resting within it."],"exits":[{"to":147,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":149,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":149,"x":-40,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["The pathway widens considerably here, jutting out into the open cavern as a pier would in water.  Visitors and natives alike venture out onto the fenced area and gaze down to the expansive terraces below.  A massive stone tower climbs from the ground level to just above the cavern's second terrace and emits brilliant flashes of light that provide the illumination for the inhabitants."],"exits":[{"to":150,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":148,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":150,"x":-20,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["Wooden stalls line the pathway as it continues to circle the cavern's upper region.  Affixed to the front of each is an iron shelf bearing a line of clay pots and jugs that descend in size from left to right.  Occasionally a string of Dwarven children will run through, sometimes pausing in front of one stall or another to blow across the mouths of the jugs in some manner of a game -- often the one making the loudest noise taking up the lead position as they run onwards through the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":149,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":151,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy recess"}]},
  {"id":151,"x":0,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["Set back into the corner, a pair of hammocks has been strung up on either side of a table.  A tattered deck of cards and a set of stained ivory dice are scattered across the table, each covered in dust from long periods of disuse.  Though almost always enveloped in a thick blanket of shadows, the recessed area sometimes takes on the vibrant hues of reds and blues and greens as the illuminating tower flares."],"exits":[{"to":152,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":150,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":152,"x":20,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["Nestled firmly against the fence on the terrace's edge is a lone home, its facade worn greatly with the ravages of time.  Though certainly not much to look at, the home does stand out from every other one in the expansive area.  A quick observation of the multi-tiered den reveals that, unlike the others, this is the only structure to stand on the edge of any terrace rather than being set against the cavern's wall."],"exits":[{"to":153,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":151,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy recess"}]},
  {"id":153,"x":20,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["A pair of ruts runs several feet down the length of the winding pathway.  Buckets of crumbled rock rest beside the deepening holes along with a stack of abandoned parchments.  Supplies and more parchments lie near the fence-protected ledge, all left unattended and gathering dust."],"exits":[{"to":152,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":154,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":154,"x":0,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Harst Haalm","descriptions":["A lone wooden structure stands beside the stairway that leads down to the middle terrace.  An elderly Dwarven woman frequently sits at the window, casually watching the traffic come and go from the three terraces.  Several of the visitors stop to inquire for directions to the various visitation spots.  Flashing a youthful smile to each, she points and gestures in numerous directions as she describes the different routes."],"exits":[{"to":153,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":155,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone stairway"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":155,"x":0,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["A large covered wagon rests beside the stairway that leads up to the third terrace.  The full aromas of freshly baked goods and meats waft out from one of the many openings.  As the guard shifts change, many stop by the wheelless structure to share a meal with friends while others pass it by only to return later with their families.  Laughter echoes from within at all hours of the day and night."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":156,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":154,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone stairway"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Midhik Haalm"]},
  {"id":156,"x":-20,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["Several Dwarven statues have been erected around a small green, all in poses of great heroics.  Jesters put on shows in the middle of the square while spectators laugh at them and with each other.  The occasional passerby will stop and admire one of the statues before moving on.  The mouth-watering scent of meat and cheese wafts through the air, coming from somewhere nearby."],"exits":[{"to":155,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":157,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":157,"x":-40,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["The road here becomes a small path as it winds between two halves of a garden.  The hearty smells of wild flowers and herbs mix in the air, creating an invigorating yet unobtrusive aroma.  Attendants wander about the area, tending to the vegetation and adjusting the artificial lighting from gaethzen globes to simulate the conditions of the surface.  Troughs of water sit at either end of the cultivated ground."],"exits":[{"to":156,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":158,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":158,"x":-50,"y":110,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["Several stone benches about the area provide ample seating around a large granite fountain.  Travelers occasionally stop and rub the base of the fountain for good luck before continuing on their relaxing strolls.  Laughter echoes into the room from other parts of the city, adding to the calming atmosphere.  Lavish embellishments on the barrier wall obscure most the view of Akigwe Tower."],"exits":[{"to":157,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":159,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"aliases":["Fountain"]},
  {"id":159,"x":-40,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["Carved from the stone of the middle terrace is a pair of stairways that lead to the base of the tower below.  From atop the descent, a fine view of Akigwe Tower's front side is visible, its beautiful architecture and grandiose lanterns complimenting one another perfectly.  Small crowds of well-dressed visitors stand near the brick wall that guards the edge.  The occasional painter stops by such groups and offers to capture the view for them...for a price."],"exits":[{"to":158,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":163,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone stairway"}]},
  {"id":160,"x":10,"y":110,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["An artistic barrier formed by stacked and colored bricks carved to resemble Dwarven faces separates the homes facing this terrace and the ledge that drops to the base level below.  Some of the bricks have signatures carved beneath the face."],"exits":[{"to":161,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":155,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":161,"x":0,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["Grey spots discolor the pathway in numerous places, most only a hand's width.  Some, however, are large enough for a well-fed Gor'Tog to lie comfortably across and still have room left for stretching!  A trio of wooden barrels rests against a wall with a crisp parchment tacked to the side of one of them."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":162,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":162,"x":-10,"y":130,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Midhik Haalm","descriptions":["A grand view of the rear of Akigwe Tower dominates the vista and obscures the view of the northern most areas of the second terrace.  Though the tower falls short of the third level of the cavern, it soars well above the second.  Flashes of vibrant lights fill the cavern periodically, illuminating the grand houses down below and drawing shouts of amazement from visitors above."],"exits":[{"to":161,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":163,"x":-25,"y":114,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tower Base","descriptions":["A pair of stairways, carved directly from the stone of the cavern's walls, leads to the terrace above.  Short, fence-like barriers of rounded dark rocks separate the private gardens of the Dwarves that have made their homes here.  A walkway of perfectly cut and laid stone leads around the base of the massive tower."],"exits":[{"to":164,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":166,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":159,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone stairway"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Tower Base"]},
  {"id":164,"x":-25,"y":104,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tower Base","descriptions":["A well tended garden with neat rows of sand and multicolored rock decorating its surface occupies much of the otherwise stone ground.  Centered within the garden is a tall green marble fountain that has been expertly carved into the image of a young Dwarven maiden wielding a huge hammer.  A wide stone bench and a pot full of preserved daisies are placed near the fountain."],"exits":[{"to":165,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":163,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":165,"x":-15,"y":104,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tower Base","descriptions":["Lanterns of brass hang on either side of a wide door of iron and oak that sits recessed within the granite tower.  Twisting and turning over the door is a thick vein of black gold-flecked marble with graceful geometric designs.  The faint sound of flowing water emanates from a nearby rock garden."],"exits":[{"to":166,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":164,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":166,"x":-15,"y":114,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tower Base","descriptions":["Perpetual light bathes the tower's base and the surrounding cavern from an unseen source atop the tower.  Though the cavern is constantly illuminated, the light flutters as if it were a flame caught in a breeze.  Oranges and reds fade to cool blues and greens before flaring back to life once again.  A stone bench rests outside of a nearby home, often occupied with the city's visitors who are unaccustomed to the fiery display."],"exits":[{"to":165,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":163,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":167,"x":20,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Traveler's Yurt","descriptions":["Daylight shines down through a wide circular hole in the center of the roof, illuminating the interior.  Unlit candles sit on brass holders mounted to the ironwood lattice-work walls of the yurt.  Woven multicolored rugs marred with muddy tracks cover the entire floor.","Lit candles sit on brass holders mounted to the ironwood lattice-work walls of the yurt, casting wan illumination through the interior.  The acrid smoke of the tapers escapes out of a wide circular hole in the center of the roof.  Woven multicolored rugs marred with muddy tracks cover the entire floor."],"exits":[{"to":168,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":114,"exit":"go","move":"go moongate"}],"aliases":["Trabe Plateau"]},
  {"id":168,"x":20,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Northern Edge","descriptions":["A vertical drop, far too steep to climb down, marks the northern limits of the plateau.  The Arid Steppe stretches for countless miles north, a flatland of uninterrupted frost and tall grasses.","A vertical drop, far too steep to climb down, marks the northern limits of the plateau.  Everything beyond the drop has been plunged into a primal darkness by the night, without so much as a single dot of light across the steppe."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":175,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":173,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":167,"exit":"go","move":"go yurt"}]},
  {"id":169,"x":60,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Eastern Edge","descriptions":["Far to the east, beyond the vertical edge of the plateau, a narrow river cuts through a portion of the steppe.  A few stunted trees, little more than brown dots from this vantage point, cling to the distant riverbank.","Far to the east, beyond the vertical edge of the plateau, a few pale points of light can be seen on the steppe floor.  Other than those faint hints of civilization, the night's cloak is complete."],"exits":[{"to":174,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":170,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":168,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":400,"exit":"go","move":"go goat-skin yurt"}]},
  {"id":170,"x":40,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, The Spire","descriptions":["Veins of silvery-blue crystal run through the surface of the plateau, like the roots of a tree.  No grass grows within a few feet of even the smallest shoot of the vein, leaving a vast swath of the area barren.  A large spire made of the same material rises to the west.","Veins of glowing blue crystal run through the surface of the plateau, like the roots of a tree.  No grass grows within a few feet of even the smallest shoot of the veins, leaving a vast swath of the area barren.  A large spire made of the same material rises to the west, casting light across the entire plateau."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":176,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":171,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":175,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":171,"x":20,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, The Spire","descriptions":["An enormous spire of silvery-blue crystal rises from the center of plateau, dozens of feet across and hundreds of feet straight into the air.  Walkways connect the spire at various heights to crystalline structures to the north and south, while a broken spur juts out into the air to the west.","An enormous spire of silvery-blue crystal rises from the center of plateau, dozens of feet across and hundreds of feet straight into the air.  Walkways connect the spire at various heights to crystalline structures to the north and south, while a broken spur juts out into the air to the west.  The entire construct glows with an inner luminescence, casting the barren ground in blue light."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":170,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":176,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":172,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":177,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline arch"}]},
  {"id":172,"x":0,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, The Spire","descriptions":["Broken crystal towers rise up from the grass, brittle and white as bone.  The towers are massive, dozens of feet across and thrice as high.  Yet despite their mass, they end in jagged shards and deep fractures, as though a giant had shattered the crystals.  A large spire rises to the east, silvery-blue and undamaged.","Broken crystal towers rise up from the grass, brittle and white as bone.  The towers are massive, dozens of feet across and thrice as high.  Yet despite their mass, they end in jagged shards and deep fractures, as though a giant had shattered the crystals.  A large spire rises to the east, glowing like Xibar in the night."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":171,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":176,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":173,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":173,"x":-20,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Western Edge","descriptions":["Loose dirt and rocks cover the western edge of the plateau, which descends in a slope rather than a vertical wall of stone.  The incline sharply drops down a few hundred feet to the steppe, where the debris turns into miles upon miles of grass.","Loose dirt and rocks cover the western edge of the plateau, which descends in a slope rather than a vertical wall of stone.  The incline sharply drops down into the darkness below, where the debris turns into an expanse of unlit land."],"exits":[{"to":168,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":172,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":174,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":174,"x":20,"y":360,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Southern Edge","descriptions":["A seemingly endless plain of grass stretches out to the south, dotted sporadically by sparse copses of stunted trees.  The wall of the plateau dips and forms a steep switchback path down its southern face.","A seemingly endless plain of grass stretches out to the south, blighted and desolate under the shadows of the night.  The wall of the plateau dips and forms a steep switchback path down its southern face."],"exits":[{"to":176,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":169,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":173,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":175,"x":20,"y":300,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, The Spire","descriptions":["Smooth silvery-blue crystal towers rise up from the grass.  The towers are massive, dozens of feet across and at least a hundred feet high at their apices.  Lifeless dirt surrounds the base of each tower, creating distinct barren circles that radiate a few feet outward.  An even larger spire rises to the south, connected to these towers by walkways high above.","Smooth silvery-blue crystal towers rise up from the grass.  The towers are massive, dozens of feet across and at least a hundred feet high at their apices.  Lifeless dirt surrounds the base of each tower, creating distinct barren circles that radiate a few feet outward.  Connected to these towers by walkways high above, an even larger spire rises to the south, glowing like the surface of Xibar."],"exits":[{"to":168,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":170,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":171,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":172,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":176,"x":20,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, The Spire","descriptions":["Bizarre shapes of silvery-blue crystal seem to grow from the earth.  A veritable forest of crystalline plants cluster together, their slender limbs twisted into spirals and entangled amongst each other a few dozen feet above.  No grass grows around the crystal objects, leaving the entire area barren of life.  A large spire made of the same material rises to the north.","Bizarre shapes of glowing blue crystal seem to grow from the earth.  A veritable forest of crystalline plants cluster together, their slender limbs twisted into spirals and entangled amongst each other a few dozen feet above.  No grass grows around the crystal objects, leaving the entire area barren of life.  A large spire made of the same material rises to the north, bathing the entire area in silvery-blue light."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":170,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":174,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":172,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":177,"x":-20,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, First Floor","descriptions":["Elk-fur rugs decorate the floors, sharply contrasting with the near-total presence of the color blue.  A uniform silvery-blue covers most of the floors, walls, and distant ceiling, interrupted only by jagged white scars.  The scars are gouged into the crystalline substance and appear frequently near the arch to the outside.  A staircase leads up a considerable distance to the next floor, following the spiral of the circular inner wall."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline arch"},{"to":178,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}]},
  {"id":178,"x":-40,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Second Floor","descriptions":["Concentric grooves radiate evenly along the floor, leading to a shattered white crystal in the center of the room.  Large furs cover the crystalline walls, but do little to stop the wind from whipping through wide slits along the cardinal directions.  A spiral staircase follows the inner wall, leading both further up the spire and down toward the ground."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":180,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":182,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":179,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":177,"exit":"climb","move":"climb descending staircase"},{"to":183,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ascending staircase"}]},
  {"id":179,"x":-60,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Broken Walkway","descriptions":["Shattered towers of bone-white crystal rise around a broken walkway that is suspended a hundred feet above the plateau.  The walkway stops abruptly before it reaches the center of the cluster, ending in a jagged edge of white shards.  Wind from the steppe plays across the shattered crystals, creating a high-pitched moan.","Shattered towers of bone-white crystal, lit by the blue light of the eastern spire, rise around a broken walkway that is suspended in the darkness.  The walkway stops abruptly before it reaches the center of the cluster, ending in a jagged edge of white shards.  Wind from the steppe plays across the shattered crystals, creating a high-pitched moan."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":180,"x":-20,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Balcony","descriptions":["A wide semi-circular platform extends outward from the middle of the crystalline spire and faces the east.  Winds blow across the platform freely, unhindered due to the lack of any rail or parapet.  The Arid Steppe stretches out across the horizon from this vantage point, filled with sparse trees, narrow rivers and countless acres of grass.","A wide semi-circular platform extends outward from the middle of the crystalline spire and faces the east.  Winds blow across the platform freely, unhindered due to the lack of any rail or parapet.  The Arid Steppe stretches out across the horizon from this vantage point, a vast flatland of shadows beneath the night sky."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":181,"x":-40,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Walkway","descriptions":["Gusts of wind blow up from the steppe below, howling like a madman across the exposed walkway.  Ten feet wide and a hundred feet up from the plateau, the structure lacks the roof and rails that might otherwise help keep the elements off and a traveler on.  The walkway is straight as an arrow, connecting the top of a tower to the north with the middle of a much larger spire to the south.","Gusts of wind blow up from the steppe below, howling like a madman across the exposed walkway.  Ten feet wide and suspended in the darkness, the structure lacks the roof and rails that might otherwise help keep the elements off and a traveler on.  The walkway is straight as an arrow, connecting the top of a glowing blue tower to the north with the middle of a much larger spire to the south."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":185,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline archway"}]},
  {"id":182,"x":-40,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Walkway","descriptions":["A lattice of narrow walkways expands outward from the northern spire to the top of a maze of twisted crystalline structures.  Five feet wide and a hundred feet up from the plateau, the walkways lack the roof and rails that might otherwise keep the wind off and a traveler on.","A lattice of narrow walkways expands outward from the northern spire to the top of a maze of glowing crystalline structures.  Five feet wide and suspended in the night, the walkways lack the roof and rails that might otherwise keep the wind off and a traveler on."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":184,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline archway"}]},
  {"id":183,"x":-60,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Guildleader's Chamber","descriptions":["Great arched windows are carved from the crystalline walls, allowing an unparalleled view of the Arid Steppe whenever the wind jostles the heavy leather curtains.  Heavy furs are heaped across the floor, their piles indented inward from use.  The low howl of the winds outside mixes with the creaking of the curtains, filling the chamber with a constant drone.","Great arched windows are carved from the crystalline walls, allowing an unparalleled view of the night whenever the wind jostles the heavy leather curtains.  Heavy furs are heaped across the floor, their piles indented inward from use.  The low howl of the winds outside mixes with the creaking of the curtains, filling the chamber with a constant drone."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Moon Mage","GL MM","Cherulisa","RS Moon Mage"]},
  {"id":184,"x":-40,"y":300,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Chamber of Artifice","descriptions":["A spacious enchanter's workshop is set up in the chamber, bringing such disparate furnishings as a writing desk and an anvil together in the same room.  A vice holds the femur of a lamb over a furnace of incandescent energy, while thin iron rods hang on the southern wall, far away from the rest of the equipment."],"exits":[{"to":182,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline archway"}]},
  {"id":185,"x":-40,"y":220,"z":1,"title":"The Spire, Chamber of Contemplation","descriptions":["Four sheep-skin rugs are laid across the cold floor at the cardinal points of the room, providing places to sit with minimal discomfort.  Pale white streaks mar the otherwise pristine silvery-blue crystalline walls, clustered predominately on the northern wall."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"go","move":"go crystalline archway"}],"color":"#FF00FF","aliases":["Dor'na'torna","Grazhir","Ways","Astral Plane"]},
  {"id":186,"x":50,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Behind the Forge","descriptions":["Blasts of heat rise from a radiant vent in the floor, far too hot for any mortal to survive.  Several smaller crevices exhibit the same molten glow.  Curiously, a tempered steel grate covers the vent, and guards stand duty just outside the door.  Other, cooler cracks lead downward, though only one is wide enough to allow you to squeeze through."],"exits":[{"to":132,"exit":"go","move":"go iron-barred door"},{"to":216,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow crack"}]},
  {"id":187,"x":60,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Public Library","descriptions":["Skillfully cut into the stone of the mountain, this chamber houses many books that the people of Hibarnhvidar find important.  Several citizens mill about, browsing the books on the shelves, speaking softly to one another and discussing their opinions on various subjects.  The Dwarven librarian welcomes patrons into the library, gesturing to an engraved silver sign."],"exits":[{"to":92,"exit":"go","move":"go mahogany door"}],"aliases":["Public Library"]},
  {"id":188,"x":60,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, Entryway","descriptions":["Stark walls of cold polished stone gleam with an eternal beauty all their own.  Dark obsidian benches line each side of the entryway while tall iron sconces lend their light to the darkness, outlining a broad archway nearby."],"exits":[{"to":93,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":189,"exit":"go","move":"go broad archway"}]},
  {"id":189,"x":80,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, Sitting Room","descriptions":["Dark leather armchairs flank a large, carved stone fireplace.  Its wide mantle is decorated with dried flowers and a mixture of semi-precious stones.  A mirror above the mantle reflects light from dozens of lit candles placed throughout the room."],"exits":[{"to":190,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":192,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":188,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"}]},
  {"id":190,"x":100,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, East Hallway","descriptions":["This short hallway features curved ceilings and polished iron chandeliers.  Along its pale grey walls are caricatures of various patrons of the club, some in bizarre positions while others look almost lifelike.  Music is heard from one end of the hall, enticing those nearby to enter."],"exits":[{"to":191,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":189,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":191,"x":120,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, Cavern","descriptions":["This spacious cavern provides room for gatherings that the club hosts.  A scattering of tables and chairs offer seating for those listening to visiting bards, while decorative screens lead to the dance floor.  Dark iron chandeliers hung from the high ceiling light the whole area in a nice, soft warm glow."],"exits":[{"to":190,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":192,"x":60,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, West Hallway","descriptions":["This short hallway connects to the busiest part of the hub.  Patrons come and go from the banking area, often muttering about funds and fees.  Painted along the walls are muted images of various plant life."],"exits":[{"to":189,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":193,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":193,"x":40,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, Banking Needs","descriptions":["Pewter sconces light this stark granite area.  Bank clerks sit behind dark oak tables with rugged Dwarven guards standing nearby.  Dark red woven rugs line the floor for warmth and offer a nice contrast to the otherwise bare decor."],"exits":[{"to":192,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":194,"exit":"go","move":"go arched doorway"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Premium Bank","Premium Teller","Premium Exchange"]},
  {"id":194,"x":40,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"The Stony Hub, Exchange","descriptions":["A brazier placed in the corner warms this small room.  Half of the area is fitted with iron bars, which keep the clients separated from the Moon Mages who move coins from different locations."],"exits":[{"to":193,"exit":"go","move":"go arched doorway"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Premium Transfer"]},
  {"id":195,"x":20,"y":370,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, City Offices","descriptions":["Small gaethzen spheres line this foyer leading to the city's offices.  Atop a pedestal, a marble statue of Hexoch, the Dwarven king, supervises all the work that goes on in the offices to the south.  During business hours, various denizens of the mountain city rush about to do business in the city's administrative center."],"exits":[{"to":196,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":197,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":198,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":89,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"}]},
  {"id":196,"x":40,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Office of Debts","descriptions":["The Debtor's Office for Hibarnhvidar stretches off into the mountain, its back wall obscured by pipe smoke and distance.  A lone Dwarf sits behind the service counter, taking the money of the citizens of the province of Forfedhdar.  Behind him, rank upon rank of desks are placed in neat orderly rows, where, during the day, clerks sit updating the accounts of all the citizens in the land."],"exits":[{"to":195,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Debt"]},
  {"id":197,"x":20,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Office of Citizenship","descriptions":["A squat counter stretches from wall to wall, behind which a lone Dwarven clerk sits smoking a pipe.  The smoke from his pipe winds its way up through a tiny slit in the ceiling.  Occasionally, another Dwarf will run in and hand something to the clerk, but the exchange is too fast to see what is being passed."],"exits":[{"to":195,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Citizenship"]},
  {"id":198,"x":0,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Office of Housing","descriptions":["Desks line the walls of this room, though only one is occupied.  The others are piled high with what look to be architectural drawings and other documents.  The one clerk on duty continues looking over a pile of papers on his desk, glancing up only briefly when someone enters the office."],"exits":[{"to":195,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":199,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Housing Office"]},
  {"id":199,"x":-20,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Office of Moving","descriptions":["Tucked away into a small alcove, a lone clerk fusses about the cramped office.  Parchments and maps line the walls and ceiling, many covered with poorly drawn neighborhoods from throughout the realms.  Traffic here is slow, but the clerk is quick to notice and greet those who enter."],"exits":[{"to":198,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#00FF00"},
  {"id":200,"x":-20,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Justice Office, Front Desk","descriptions":["The glow cast by oil lamps set into the rough granite walls fails to bring any warmth to this grim cavern.  A bored looking Dwarven constable sits behind a slate desk covered with neat stacks of papers.  The walls narrow toward the rear of the chamber, but a glint of light indicates that there is something more beyond."],"exits":[{"to":202,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":201,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"},{"to":91,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"aliases":["Justice Office","Guard House","Jail"]},
  {"id":201,"x":-40,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"Justice Office, Chief Constable's Office","descriptions":["A large, blocky desk spans nearly the entire breadth of this room.  Behind it sits a white-bearded Dwarf, peering over the top of a pair of square-rimmed spectacles.  The walls are lined with several framed portraits of Dwarves in constable uniforms."],"exits":[{"to":200,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Constable's Office","Discipline"]},
  {"id":202,"x":-20,"y":290,"z":0,"title":"Justice Office, Judge's Chambers","descriptions":["A squat grey marble dais sits in the center of one end of this room.  Cold stone walls add to the foreboding aura of the chamber.  From here judgment is passed upon those who run afoul of the law in Hibarnhvidar."],"exits":[{"to":200,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"aliases":["Judge's Chambers"]},
  {"id":203,"x":-60,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Bank Foyer","descriptions":["The ornate entrance arch gives way to a long hall, filled with accountants and bookkeepers.  Opposing the arch, two tunnels lead deeper into the bank to the foreign exchange and teller windows.  Several Dwarven employees wander about, conversing with colleagues seated at the desks."],"exits":[{"to":205,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":204,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":78,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}],"aliases":["1Bank","Bank"]},
  {"id":204,"x":-80,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Teller Windows","descriptions":["Two Dwarven guards stand at the entrance to the tunnel leading back to the bank foyer, insuring the safety and security of deposited funds.  Several alcoves are available in the cavern walls to allow for privacy as one converses with the tellers on the other side of the stone counters."],"exits":[{"to":203,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["1Teller","Teller"]},
  {"id":205,"x":-80,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Foreign Exchange Office","descriptions":["A small opening sits embedded in the wall opposite the tunnel to the bank foyer.  This part of the cavern claims only a narrow garbage trough and the exchange window as adornment.  A short Dwarven banker sits behind the metal grille, waiting to exchange patron's money into other currencies."],"exits":[{"to":203,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["1Exchange","Exchange"]},
  {"id":206,"x":-40,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Hospital, Entrance Room","descriptions":["This room, located just off the main cavern, serves as a junction for the different locations within the hospital.  In addition to serving as the workplace for the resident healer Shalvarn, whose office is located through a small door to the west, the infirmary allows other healers to stop by and help with the demand for healing."],"exits":[{"to":207,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":208,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":77,"exit":"go","move":"go stone arch"},{"to":380,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"}]},
  {"id":207,"x":-40,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Hospital, Volunteer Room","descriptions":["Small alcoves set into each of the four walls hold short canvas cots to raise the patients off the cold stone.  The center of the room is mostly empty save for several large pillows piled there.  A white cabinet rests against the north wall between two of the bays."],"exits":[{"to":206,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":208,"x":-40,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Hospital, Sitting Room","descriptions":["Located just off the entrance hall, this room allows members of the community a quiet space to sit and relax while waiting to be seen by Shalvarn.  Several chairs lie scattered about the room in small groups, enabling friends to have a quiet chat."],"exits":[{"to":206,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":209,"x":-40,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Dadzi's Skrawt Stal, Glan Gulth","descriptions":["Its polished ebonwood and heavy crystal doors set the tone of opulence and Dwarven artisanship continued within this shop.  Pale pink granite floors peek from beneath luxuriously bleached and combed wooly sheepskin.  Cool alabaster showcases, themselves artistically shaped, display their contents on velvet beds.  A silk divan in the center of the room provides seating for weary shoppers, or those suffering from sticker shock."],"exits":[{"to":211,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":210,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":212,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":79,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Dadzi's Skrawt Stal","Jewelry"]},
  {"id":210,"x":-30,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Dadzi's Skrawt Stal, Kwar Stof","descriptions":["Soft lights, recessed in the stone ceiling, bathe this space with a faint blue glow and create the impression of the night sky.  A small settee covered in silver bear pelts sits on a midnight blue carpet sheared in a latticework pattern.  Four displays, topped with silver velvet, resemble the moons of Elanthia and encircle the settee."],"exits":[{"to":209,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":211,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":213,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":211,"x":-40,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Dadzi's Skrawt Stal, Hivdar Stof","descriptions":["This white granite room has an intricately carved dome supported by a series of arcades.  Refreshing breezes move unimpeded through the open design, creating a sense of spacious grandeur.  Beneath a strong gaethzen orb is a glass showcase, where Dadzi's most scintillating designs tend to elicit desire in the eyes of Hibarnhvidar's residents."],"exits":[{"to":213,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":210,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":209,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":212,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":212,"x":-50,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Dadzi's Skrawt Stal, Rawdh Stof","descriptions":["Muffling sounds down to the level of a whisper, dark red carpeting covers the floor and provides a subtle showcase for silver toned displays.  A brocade sofa at the far end of the room is flanked by a dainty white table with cups and a teapot for those contemplating a purchase."],"exits":[{"to":213,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":211,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":209,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":213,"x":-40,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Dadzi's Skrawt Stal, Gwel Stof","descriptions":["Bits of various colored jade interspersed with cool, white tile create an almost antiseptic atmosphere which continues with only one display, centered in the room.  A low, narrow green bench rests against the wall leading to the red room."],"exits":[{"to":210,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":211,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":212,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":214,"x":160,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"Cargil's Engraving, Showroom","descriptions":["Shields displaying examples of the fine work done by the proprietor line the walls of this neat, compact shop.  On a low marble counter sits a gold-embossed menu board, which enumerates the options offered.  Cargil, the engraver, sits atop a squat stool in front of a heavy curtain leading to his workroom."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"go","move":"go steel door"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Cargil's Engraving","Engraver"]},
  {"id":215,"x":160,"y":220,"z":1,"title":"Stawk's Brothers Mineral and Supply","descriptions":["The entire room has been roughly chipped out of the surrounding stone.  Crates and boxes are haphazardly strewn about with merchandise, while a single chunk of stone with a slightly flattened surface sits in the middle of the room, chained to the floor.  An old corner table stands in the back of the cavern, covered with a thick layer of dust and carrying a lone item which apparently receives little attention from the local customers.  Across from the exit into the upper cavern is a bolted iron door."],"exits":[{"to":123,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Stawk's Brothers Mineral and Supply","Alchemy","Tawks"]},
  {"id":216,"x":50,"y":40,"z":1,"title":"Cavern of Fire, Stalagmite Maze","descriptions":["The air feels thick and heavy with humidity as the heat bakes away what moisture seeps from the cavern's rocky walls.  Stalagmites jut up from the floor, forcing travelers to make their way through a confusing maze of passages that twist and turn, some rising, some falling, some doubling back upon themselves.  The haze of smoke, lit by a faint glow emanating from hairline cracks in the walls, makes the cavern even more disorienting."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"linksTo":"Map118e_Firecats.xml"},
  {"id":217,"x":-390,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Gate to Hibarnhvidar","descriptions":["Nestled against a steep incline, a massive stone gate stands between the road proper and the city of Hibarnhvidar.  Slight movement can be seen high atop the platforms that flank the gate's entrance.  Carefully laid stonework provides a broad area just before the gate, and narrows into the path leading away from the city.  Brushed and smoothed, the stones are evenly spaced, all traces of weed or loose gravel removed.  A multi-pointed star marks the stone at the center of the entryway."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":24,"exit":"go","move":"go hibarnhvidar gate"}],"aliases":["N Gate","W Gate","Boar Clan","wgate"],"linksTo":"Map126_Hawstkaal_Road.xml"},
  {"id":218,"x":-260,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Vandorf's House of Hides","descriptions":["The smell of curing hides clings to the air, cloying the nostrils with a heavy unpleasant smell of decayed animal flesh.  A thick cord draped with various furs extends from one end of the room to the other, acting as a makeshift curtain that leads to the back room.  The shop owner Vandorf tends to his furs, stopping every so often to acknowledge customers that walk in to do business."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Vandorf's House of Hides","bundles","skins"]},
  {"id":219,"x":-80,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Drangvold's Sundries, Sales Floor","descriptions":["Stacked stone chinked with straw and plaster form the base for an unusual lichen painting on the back wall of the shop.  Subtle shades of blues and greens mingle with grey and brown in a seascape, far from the sight or smell of the ocean.  The other walls are hidden by rows of shelves creaking beneath the weight of the goods offered for sale in the town's general store."],"exits":[{"to":12,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Drangvold's Sundries","General"]},
  {"id":220,"x":-100,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"The Singing Raven, Common Room","descriptions":["A perpetual haze of tobacco smoke hangs just under the low ceiling, illuminated from beneath by the orange glow of the roaring fire in the flagstone fireplace that takes up most of one wall.  Opposite it, a long bar runs the length of the room.  Rough wooden tables and chairs are scattered about, of wildly varying sizes to accommodate travelers of all races.  Day and night, the room is filled by those stopping for a bite to eat or liquid refreshment."],"exits":[{"to":221,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":13,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"},{"to":222,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wide staircase"}],"aliases":["Singing Raven"]},
  {"id":221,"x":-110,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Inn, Private Parlor","descriptions":["The sounds of activity from the common room are muted here, although the pungent smell of tobacco smoke drifts in on a slight draft.  Small and windowless, the room is lit by a stone fireplace on the far wall, and a hurricane lamp placed in the middle of the centered round table."],"exits":[{"to":220,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":222,"x":-100,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"The Singing Raven, Upstairs Hall","descriptions":["A single glass-enclosed lantern on one wall provides the only light on the narrow landing.  The flickering flame inside wavers and gutters, casting moving shadows along the wood-paneled walls."],"exits":[{"to":220,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wide staircase"},{"to":223,"exit":"go","move":"go pine door"},{"to":224,"exit":"go","move":"go peregan door"}]},
  {"id":223,"x":-110,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"The Singing Raven, Pine Room","descriptions":["A faint scent of baking bread drifts through the small room, apparently located somewhere near the kitchens.  The knotty pine paneling's warm yellow hue is matched by the bed coverings on the low, thick mattress."],"exits":[{"to":222,"exit":"go","move":"go pine door"}],"aliases":["Tarts"]},
  {"id":224,"x":-110,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"The Singing Raven, Peregan Room","descriptions":["Warm golden highlights glint from the deep brown wood-paneled walls.  An immense four-poster bed dominates the room, covered in thick, clean-smelling down comforters and piles of fluffy pillows.  A small table is placed conveniently close to the bed, holding simple refreshments."],"exits":[{"to":222,"exit":"go","move":"go peregan door"}]},
  {"id":225,"x":-120,"y":-45,"z":0,"title":"Second Provincial Bank of Hibarnhvidar","descriptions":["The tiny fires of hundreds of candles placed in all corners of the room cast gleaming warm highlights that reflect off the polished wood from which the bank lobby was built.  Thick beams criss-cross the ceiling, and solid pillars -- looking as though they were made of whole tree trunks -- march along all four walls.  The wood is a medium shade, neither oppressively dark nor so light as to appear freshly cut, and has been lovingly polished until it glows."],"exits":[{"to":226,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":227,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":14,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["2Bank"]},
  {"id":226,"x":-110,"y":-45,"z":0,"title":"Second Provincial Bank of Hibarnhvidar, Exchange","descriptions":["The exchange clerks sit behind a low counter, separated from the entry area by a thick pane of glass with a small hole cut in it at mouth-level, and a scooped-out area cut into the wooden counter underneath it so coins can be pushed through to the other side.  The bored-looking clerks scurry to and fro within their glass cage, moving papers from one desk to another with a great show of efficiency."],"exits":[{"to":225,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["2Exchange"]},
  {"id":227,"x":-130,"y":-45,"z":0,"title":"Second Provincial Bank of Hibarnhvidar, Teller","descriptions":["Bored-looking Gor'Tog clerks sit behind a high counter topped by a bronze railing, wakening as people come and go.  Large, solid wooden desks fill their area, and sturdy file cabinets line the walls.  On the customer side of the counter, the floor is covered with plush carpeting and the walls are covered in rich brocade cloth and wainscotted below."],"exits":[{"to":225,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["2Teller"]},
  {"id":228,"x":-140,"y":-8,"z":0,"title":"Drones and Drums","descriptions":["Several shelves and racks line the flagstone walls of the shop, each displaying a variety of instruments and accessories.  Anniana, the Gor'Tog proprietor, stands behind a prominent counter near the wall opposite the entry, dusting and cleaning her wares when not assisting customers.  Resting at one end of the counter is a packed scroll case, while a display stand flanks the other.  In the center of the room, a long oak table displays an assortment of bagpipes."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Drones and Drums","Music","Anniana"]},
  {"id":229,"x":-120,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Reliable Pawn and Dry Goods Emporium","descriptions":["Tiny and dark, the shop is lit only by a smoke-darkened lantern hanging directly over the tall counter dividing the room.  In front of the counter is only a bucket and an expanse of wood-planked floor, dirt-blackened in the corners but with a polished trail leading straight in from the doorway.  Behind the counter are heaps and piles of used goods, some sorted and others simply stacked."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Pawn Shop","Relf"]},
  {"id":230,"x":-140,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"New Lamps for Gold","descriptions":["Hibarnhvidar's lamp and lantern shop is either cozy or cramped, depending on one's outlook.  Three or four customers would crowd this tiny establishment, but almost all of the wares are within arm's length, except for the flammable stuff.  That sits behind a high counter out of reach of the public."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Lamp Shop"]},
  {"id":231,"x":-220,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Traders' Guild Auction Tent","descriptions":["The tent is made of durable off-white canvas, secured by heavy ropes and nine large metal poles.  Lanterns hang from small hooks on each pole, making the room bright enough to examine all the goods being sold.  An auction table sits on a platform fashioned out of crates, while boxes and barrels of merchandise hug the walls.  Screwed into the central pole is a metal plaque upon which rests the auction list.","The tent is made of durable off-white canvas and secured by heavy ropes and eight large metal poles.  Natural light filters through the material, while lanterns hang from small hooks on each pole in case more is needed.  An auction table sits on a platform fashioned out of crates, while boxes and barrels of merchandise hug the walls.  Screwed into the central pole is a metal plaque upon which rests the auction list."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"go","move":"go tent flap"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Auction"]},
  {"id":232,"x":-180,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, The Floor","descriptions":["This long, wide room appears to be a partially converted brewery, the air still filled with the scent of ale.  Rows of casks line the walls, leaving the center of the floor clear to make room for business.  Clerks, traders and commodity brokers intermingle with local farmers and miners to discuss the ever-changing prices of commodities, while the noisy sound of braying animals can be heard to the east."],"exits":[{"to":233,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":234,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":16,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":236,"exit":"go","move":"go open doorway"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["trade minister","shipment clerk","Trading Clerk","Trading Minister"]},
  {"id":233,"x":-160,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Stables","descriptions":["Mountain hardy beasts of all sorts find themselves in neighboring stalls in this slightly cramped but serviceable stable.  Bales of alfalfa and hay have been pushed against the wall, leaving only the bare minimum amount of area needed to lead caravans and carts in and out from the road."],"exits":[{"to":232,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":16,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":235,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow doorway"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Caravan Stable"]},
  {"id":234,"x":-200,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Office of Interprovincial Trade","descriptions":["A foil map hangs across the back wall, tinted and textured to show the five provinces of Elanthia.  Other than that single piece of elegance, the room is completely utilitarian with a wooden plank floor and a single desk of neatly stacked paperwork."],"exits":[{"to":232,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":235,"x":-160,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Rock Garden","descriptions":["This long abandoned portion of the brewery has been cleaned up and turned into an exquisite rock garden.  An intentionally meandering path of carefully pieced slate rock connects the stables and cask room, as well as a shiny brass contraption in the western garden.  Old ale casks, cut in half, have been used as picturesque flower boxes, while other pieces of cask have been used as trimming around individual beds nestled within colorful collections of polished stone."],"exits":[{"to":233,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":236,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":237,"exit":"go","move":"go applewood door"}]},
  {"id":236,"x":-180,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Rock Garden","descriptions":["The dazzling rock garden occupying the wide warehouse portion of this old brewery has been muted by the presence of a lone working still that takes up the western portion of the wall.  Several Dwarven workers tend to the still, oblivious to the beauty of the arrangements of colored rock and crystal around them.  Channels of water run through the garden both to further beautify the area as well as to keep the room at a comfortable temperature."],"exits":[{"to":232,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":235,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":238,"exit":"go","move":"go low-cut door"}]},
  {"id":237,"x":-160,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Cask Room","descriptions":["Damp and cool, this room acts as a tasting room for guests and a break room for clerks, although it is hard to say who is actually doing the most sampling."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Cask Room"]},
  {"id":238,"x":-200,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Trader Guild, Guild Leader's Office","descriptions":["The Guildmaster's office has been carefully coordinated to incorporate the vision of a sun rising above the mountains.  Purple and gold silk drapes hang loosely against the stone walls with light from wall sconces peeking through behind it like the first rays of a new morning in a cloudy sky.  A large gold-inlaid rosewood desk glows in the reflected light from the smokeless candles set about the room.  On a small shelf behind the desk rests a crystal decanter and four matching wine glasses."],"exits":[{"to":236,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Trader","Raelem","RS Trader"]},
  {"id":239,"x":-190,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Entry Hall","descriptions":["Carved inside a huge mica streak with the entrance in a corner, the shrine walls confer the impression of being inside a diamond.  Stone balustrades create a diagonal pathway leading further into the shrine while life-size doves carved from pure white quartz hover over alcoves on either side.  Slight variations in height and color give the blue tile floor a resemblance to waves in an ocean.","Carved inside a huge mica streak with the entrance in a corner, stone balustrades create a diagonal pathway leading further into the shrine."],"exits":[{"to":243,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":241,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":240,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":38,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}]},
  {"id":240,"x":-200,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Peace Alcove","descriptions":["A stone bench faces the semi-circular wall of the alcove providing seating for those who would contemplate the bas-relief artwork.  The carved collage depicts moments in Elanthian history that range from a quiet gathering to a signing ceremony between fierce warriors.  Inset into the ocean-blue mosaic floor is a beautiful white dove.","A stone bench faces the semi-circular wall of the alcove providing seating for those who would contemplate the bas-relief artwork depicting Elanthian history."],"exits":[{"to":242,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":239,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"aliases":["Peace Alcove"]},
  {"id":241,"x":-180,"y":140,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Family Alcove","descriptions":["Situated within individual niches in the cavern wall are miniature figures of families doing things together.  Tableaus depict families at work, at play, at a wedding, doing daily chores, celebrating a birth and mourning the loss of a loved one.  Stone stools in several heights are arranged before the niches.","Situated within individual niches in the cavern wall are miniature figures of families doing things together.  Stone stools in several heights are arranged before the wall."],"exits":[{"to":244,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":239,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Family Alcove"]},
  {"id":242,"x":-200,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Offering Room","descriptions":["The roughly chiseled walls and dirt floor contrast sharply with the artistic bent in the other areas of the shrine.  A lone covered table stands in the center of the floor with a paltry selection of offerings for sale.  Some cooing sounds escape from beneath the tablecloth.","A lone table, covered with paltry offerings for sale, stands in the center of the room's dirt floor."],"exits":[{"to":240,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Offering Room","Cleric Shop"]},
  {"id":243,"x":-190,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Hall of Reflections","descriptions":["The long, narrow mirrors that line the walls of this area are hung so as to infinitely reproduce each other and the altar.  This design results in constant reflection, which deliberately encourages occupants to look deep within to find reality.","The long, narrow mirrors that line the walls have been designed to infinitely reproduce each other and the altar, encouraging occupants to look deep within themselves."],"exits":[{"to":239,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Albreda's Shrine","pilgrim's badge","altar","shrine-5-03"]},
  {"id":244,"x":-180,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Albreda's Shrine, Healer's Haven","descriptions":["Blue and green tiles set in an alternating diamond pattern give an expansive feeling to the floor.  Divans sit along the walls beneath frescos of herbs and gardens that soar to the vaulted ceiling where a huge wagon wheel full of lit candles brightens the area.","Divans sit along the walls beneath frescos of herbs and gardens that soar to the vaulted ceiling."],"exits":[{"to":241,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"aliases":["Divans"]},
  {"id":245,"x":-180,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Agrobov's Green Grocer","descriptions":["The foyer of this three-story building also doubles as a produce shop and has been lined with wood-chips and straw to facilitate cleaning.  Agrobov slumps on a stool in the corner, next to a bushel of corn husks.  A bucket containing bags marked with their supposed weight rests beneath a set of scales suspended from the ceiling."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"go","move":"go street"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Agrobov's Green Grocer","Grocer"]},
  {"id":246,"x":-180,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Micmi's Fruit Shop","descriptions":["Tiers of carefully crafted baskets hold fruit not yet ripe enough to satisfy Micmi's penchant for selling perfect fruit.  A spare set of blocks rests against one wall, waiting to steady her stand if need be."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"go","move":"go street"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Micmi's Fruit Shop","Fruit"]},
  {"id":247,"x":-320,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Fortuneteller's Tent","descriptions":["Beneath a colorful sign draped along the length of the tent's roof is a small round table covered in a loud paisley-patterned cloth.  A thick scent of incense permeates the air, and the room is dimly illuminated by a single lantern shielded with red glass.  Seated in the back is an elderly Gor'Tog woman wearing dangly earrings and a folded kerchief on her head."],"exits":[{"to":47,"exit":"go","move":"go tent flap"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Fortuneteller's Tent","Wisdom"]},
  {"id":248,"x":-230,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"The Three Turnips, Common Room","descriptions":["A semicircle of lumpy overstuffed chairs faces a roaring fire crackling in a large flagstone hearth set into the rear wall of this spacious chamber.  The remainder of the space is covered by heavily scarred oaken tables, most of them replete with massive frothing tankards and wide platters heaped with the hearty fare favored by Toggish laborers.  Based on the relaxed postures of many of the patrons, it is clear that they consider this their home away from home."],"exits":[{"to":58,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"},{"to":249,"exit":"go","move":"go dark-beamed archway"},{"to":250,"exit":"go","move":"go batwing door"}],"aliases":["Three Turnips"]},
  {"id":249,"x":-220,"y":340,"z":0,"title":"The Three Turnips, Banquet Hall","descriptions":["Unlike the atmosphere in the rest of this establishment, there is an air of formality here.  The enormous long table that runs nearly the entire length of the room is draped in white linen, and there are centerpieces of freshly cut flowers at regular intervals.  The chairs are in markedly better repair than those found in the common room."],"exits":[{"to":248,"exit":"go","move":"go dark-beamed archway"}],"aliases":["Banquet Hall"]},
  {"id":250,"x":-220,"y":320,"z":0,"title":"The Three Turnips, Taproom","descriptions":["Several thick-legged stools, braced for the weight of the pub's massive patrons, line the front of a long wooden, slightly warped bar.  On the barkeep's side are stands supporting three large kegs and a shelf filled with a motley array of bottles and jars.  A large rectangular mirror covers most of the back wall, affording drinkers the opportunity to make faces at themselves while they enjoy their libations."],"exits":[{"to":251,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":248,"exit":"go","move":"go batwing door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Taproom"]},
  {"id":251,"x":-220,"y":310,"z":0,"title":"The Three Turnips, Game Room","descriptions":["This room has been set aside for 'Togs who wish to divert themselves with something other than mere eating and drinking.  Mounted on the back wall is a well-used two-colored dartboard.  Numerous nicks and gouges beyond the border of the target silently testify to the fact that the contestants are often more enthusiastic than skillful.  A few scattered armchairs are provided for the comfort of those waiting their turns to cause structural damage."],"exits":[{"to":250,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"aliases":["Game Room"]},
  {"id":252,"x":-300,"y":350,"z":0,"title":"Yamka Wan Bakery","descriptions":["Motes of white drift through the air, dusting patrons with flour or coating them in sugar depending on what is baking at the moment.  A wood counter, built of peeled logs thick enough to support the weight of customers peering over at the merchandise, displays pans with the shop's offerings for the day."],"exits":[{"to":63,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":253,"exit":"go","move":"go wide doorway"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Yamka Wan Bakery","Bakery"]},
  {"id":253,"x":-300,"y":330,"z":0,"title":"Yamka Wan Bakery, Lapnaka Udak","descriptions":["Heat radiates from a huge oven that dominates one wall of this expansive kitchen.  Pots, pans, and a variety of cooking utensils hang from hooks above the broad counters.  Off to one side is a long bench next to a picnic table piled high with piping hot pies."],"exits":[{"to":252,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Lapnaka Udak","Stamina"]},
  {"id":254,"x":-240,"y":390,"z":0,"title":"Smavold's Toggery","descriptions":["The heavy treads of many Gor'Tog customers have worn down the well-swept flagstone floor.  The same stone creates the walls, leading to a thatched roof.  Flanking the doors on either side are two large windows which gaze upon the Green.  Several shelves adorn the walls, leading to what seems to be the sales counter.  The shopkeeper, Smavold, wields a broom as he patrols the store, cleaning the floor and keeping a watchful eye on his merchandise.","The heavy treads of many Gor'Tog customers have worn down the well-swept flagstone floor.  The same stone creates the walls, leading to a thatched roof.  Torches line the walls, illuminating the shop.  Several shelves adorn the walls, leading to what seems to be the sales counter.  The shopkeeper, Smavold, rests upon a stool, keeping an eye on his goods. ","The heavy treads of many Gor'Tog customers have worn down the well-swept flagstone floor.  The same stone creates the walls, leading to a thatched roof.  Torches line the walls, illuminating the shop.  Several shelves adorn the walls, leading to what seems to be the sales counter.  The shopkeeper, Smavold, rests upon a stool, keeping an eye on his goods."],"exits":[{"to":68,"exit":"go","move":"go oak doors"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Smavold's Toggery","Toggery"]},
  {"id":255,"x":-280,"y":410,"z":0,"title":"Gor'Tog District, Behind a Stone Hut","descriptions":["Leaning against the back wall of the hut, a massively muscular Gor'Tog hums to himself.  He is having some difficulty staying on key, but it doesn't seem to bother him much.  Several massive sledgehammers lie amid fragments of rock scattered widely about the area, almost as if there had been an explosion."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"go","move":"go dirt path"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Strength"]},
  {"id":256,"x":-260,"y":460,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Common Room","descriptions":["The confines of a low ramshackle building converted to living quarters are furnished haphazardly.  Doors, arch, hallway and alcove branch off from the long squat common room without symmetry, giving the appearance of being tacked on as needed.  A wood stove burns brightly, mismatched benches and chairs pulled in a cluster around it.  Only windows on the street side of the building contribute light or fresh air, and although the room looks frayed and made of collected discards, it is clean and neat."],"exits":[{"to":257,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":74,"exit":"go","move":"go front door"},{"to":259,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"},{"to":258,"exit":"go","move":"go paneled door"},{"to":260,"exit":"go","move":"go headmaster's office"}],"aliases":["Orphanage"]},
  {"id":257,"x":-280,"y":460,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Classroom","descriptions":["A shelf holds writing slates and chalk for lessons, and long backless benches stand arranged in symmetrical rows.  At the far side of the room is a table displaying student efforts.  Of note is a large, chipped ceramic bowl furnished with water, pebbles and turtle."],"exits":[{"to":256,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":258,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}]},
  {"id":258,"x":-280,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Library","descriptions":["Tucked in the front corner of the common room, the library bookshelves form two of the walls to divide it as a separate room.  The largest window in the whole orphanage looks out into the street, so during daylight hours it is the brightest lit and cheeriest of nooks.  A comfortable chair is a favorite spot, and its faded cover and squashed cushion suggest many children have retreated here."],"exits":[{"to":256,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":257,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}],"aliases":["Orphanage Library"]},
  {"id":259,"x":-240,"y":460,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Dining Room","descriptions":["Three long tables and their associated benches nearly fill the room it requires a good deal of careful stepping and squeezing to move past them.  Old bottles holding bouquets of flowering weeds serve as centerpieces.  Light from an old oil lantern dangling from a ceiling chain can barely chase the dark from the windowless space -- shadows dance crookedly as it sways each time the swinging door opens and closes."],"exits":[{"to":256,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":261,"exit":"go","move":"go swinging door"}]},
  {"id":260,"x":-260,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Headmaster's Chamber","descriptions":["The Headmaster's chamber is no more elaborate than any other area of the orphanage.  His battered desk is missing a drawer, and his chair's rungs are reinforced with twine.  A window - a luxury - looks out into the street, and behind a screen is a small cot.  Drawings pinned to the wall only add to the clutter.  Nevertheless, there is a hint of good will in his disorder, that there is too much work for one man, but what is left undone has been put aside for the priority of affection rather than neglect."],"exits":[{"to":256,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":261,"x":-240,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Kitchen","descriptions":["A monstrous wood stove, a tall heavy table, and a large wash basin dominate this room dedicated to providing nourishment for the children.  Soup simmers in a big iron pot, and although no one will go hungry, the meals are clearly basic.  To look upon the surroundings, one would suspect that nothing like a birthday cake or sweet treats that children love comes forth from this kitchen."],"exits":[{"to":259,"exit":"go","move":"go swinging door"},{"to":262,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}]},
  {"id":262,"x":-220,"y":480,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Orphanage Backyard","descriptions":["Out the back door there is room in a strip of yard for a small herb garden and a few vegetables scratched into the hard ground.  A water pump near the door is the source of water for the kitchen, baths, and drinking.  At one end of the property, which runs the length of the back of the building, are a few toys that someone has forgotten to put away."],"exits":[{"to":261,"exit":"go","move":"go back door"}],"aliases":["Water Pump"]},
  {"id":263,"x":-350,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Tunal","descriptions":["A huge granite boulder from Outer Hibarnhvidar leads into this sharply sloping tunnel.  Bricks of red-streaked granite populate the grey stone of the walls, floor, and ceiling more and more until nothing but the granite bricks frame a black iron door at the lower end."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go granite boulder"},{"to":264,"exit":"go","move":"go iron door"}]},
  {"id":264,"x":-360,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Gatikalar Stof","descriptions":["Enormous granite blocks, fitted with no visible mortar, create thirty-foot walls and a vaulted ceiling.  Thick veins of ore meet in a whorl in the center of the floor.  In the east wall, a wrought iron keystone twenty-five feet above the floor supports a red granite arch which is flanked by two fifteen-foot-high granite arches, one black and the other grey.  Flames that light the chamber rise from a trough along the top of each wall."],"exits":[{"to":263,"exit":"go","move":"go iron door"},{"to":265,"exit":"go","move":"go red arch"},{"to":382,"exit":"go","move":"go black arch"},{"to":382,"exit":"go","move":"go stone doors"}],"aliases":["Elding Gwilt","Barbarian"]},
  {"id":265,"x":-370,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Vigan Stof","descriptions":["Curving granite blocks form the circular walls for this huge chamber.  Thick veins of brick-red hematite emanate from the wrought iron keystone that supports the arch in the west wall.  Long low benches have been hewn from the granite floor and surround a huge map constructed from fine metals and gemstones that is inlaid into the floor.  A broad set of low stairs leads to a dais to the east."],"exits":[{"to":264,"exit":"go","move":"go red arch"},{"to":266,"exit":"climb","move":"climb low stairs"}]},
  {"id":266,"x":-380,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Tawkisik Stof","descriptions":["The veins of hematite change to solid iron in the granite blocks nearest the dais.  A raised square of granite holds the Guildleader's seat, and a nearby pedestal holds the Guildleader's tankard.  A table at the rear of the dais holds an oaken hogshead.  Stairs lead down from the dais."],"exits":[{"to":265,"exit":"climb","move":"climb low stairs"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Barbarian","Stumara"]},
  {"id":267,"x":-340,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Stable","descriptions":["Solidly built of thick, expertly hewn and mortared rock, the stable provides snug housing and protection from the worst of the storms that sometimes sweep over the city.  A thick layer of fresh hay blankets the stone-flagged floor, cushioning the horses' hooves as they pass in and out.  In one corner is a large pen holding the horses and ponies currently offered for sale."],"exits":[{"to":268,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":269,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":23,"exit":"go","move":"go stable door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Stable","Horses"]},
  {"id":268,"x":-320,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Stable","descriptions":["Soft rustling sounds come from behind the wooden stalls lining each side of the stable, with an occasional whicker and the thump of hooves on straw-padded stone.  Glass-enclosed lanterns hang at intervals from the exposed beams and rafters overhead, providing soft light for workers while not disturbing the sleep of the animals."],"exits":[{"to":267,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Kwint"]},
  {"id":269,"x":-360,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Stable","descriptions":["With a truly luxurious auburn beard, impressive even by Dwarven standards, Stableman Hvik presides over his small shop, offering all the supplies a horse owner requires to keep a steed in top condition.  Occasionally muttering to himself in a basso profundo growl, Hvik busies himself day and night with keeping the items for sale in superb condition."],"exits":[{"to":267,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Tack","Hvik"]},
  {"id":270,"x":-270,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Square","descriptions":["Cut into the southeast portion of a low stone wall, a wide ironwork archway acts as the entrance into the Market Square.  Stones of varying shades of grey and dark red lay like a giant puzzle on the ground, flawlessly placed with no visible grouting in between.  A pair of long plates of treated metal lies across a channel of water that interrupts the eastern side of the square.  In the center of the market is a leather tent with colorful pennants on the northern side."],"exits":[{"to":272,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":271,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":18,"exit":"go","move":"go ironwork archway"}]},
  {"id":271,"x":-240,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Square","descriptions":["The echo of burbling water can be heard from here along with the occasional clanging sound of footsteps as shoppers cross over the metal plates that keep unwary passersby from stepping into the water channel that cuts through the northeast corner.  Iron poles have been carefully set into the stonework, a sign that the central tent of the square is a permanent structure.  A low wall provides the idea place to sit and rest.  Hearty warm smells drift through, perhaps from a small kiosk visible to the north."],"exits":[{"to":273,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":270,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":272,"x":-270,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Square","descriptions":["Carefully pruned trees on the other side of the low stone wall to provide limited shade and shelter from the elements for those who might like to rest there.  Locals, travelers and merchants alike wander in and out of the Traders' tent entrance, attracted by its colorful pennants and the anticipation of a good bargain."],"exits":[{"to":273,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":270,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":274,"exit":"go","move":"go tent entrance"}]},
  {"id":273,"x":-240,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Market Square","descriptions":["Nestled in the corner beside the low stone wall is a wooden kiosk covered with painted wooden figures of Dwarves in traditional costumes and fanciful depictions of cave flowers.  A long iron pole hovers out over the water channel with several ropes tied along its length.  To the west is a brightly colored entrance that leads into the tent in the center of the market square."],"exits":[{"to":271,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":272,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":274,"x":-260,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Traders' Tent","descriptions":["The treasures of ages past pass through this tent from every part of the five provinces, making for a colorful display of goods to cater to both the wealthy and the wealthy at heart.  Locals bustle in and out to peer at the curiosities brought in from the outside world and exchange coin for trinkets from the local Traders.","The treasures of ages past pass through this tent from every part of the five provinces, making for a colorful display of goods to cater to both the wealthy and the wealthy at heart.  Locals bustle in and out to peer at the curiosities brought in from the outside world and exchange coin for trinkets from the local Traders.  Beautifully carved lanterns dangle in a line from the ceiling and brighten up the interior."],"exits":[{"to":275,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":272,"exit":"go","move":"go tent flap"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Tables"]},
  {"id":275,"x":-250,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Outer Hibarnhvidar, Traders' Tent","descriptions":["The treasures of ages past pass through this tent from every part of the five provinces, making for a colorful display of goods to cater to both the wealthy and the wealthy at heart.  Locals bustle in and out to peer at the curiosities brought in from the outside world and exchange coin for trinkets from the local Traders.","The treasures of ages past pass through this tent from every part of the five provinces, making for a colorful display of goods to cater to both the wealthy and the wealthy at heart.  Locals bustle in and out to peer at the curiosities brought in from the outside world and exchange coin for trinkets from the local Traders.  Beautifully carved lanterns dangle in a line from the ceiling and brighten up the interior."],"exits":[{"to":274,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":276,"x":110,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Entryway","descriptions":["Leading from the bustle of Inner Hibarnhvidar toward a solid oaken door, the walls of this tunnel are flanked by carvings celebrating the joys of ale.  Down one side are etchings revealing numerous kegs and tavern patrons enjoying their contents.  Along the other wall is a deeply engraved mural depicting the brewing process."],"exits":[{"to":100,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":277,"exit":"go","move":"go oaken door"}]},
  {"id":277,"x":120,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Barroom","descriptions":["A heavy oaken door separates the cold comfort of the barroom from the echoes of the cavern outside.  To either side of the bar stand several large, hunched figures, who glance furtively over their mugs and tankards as the occasional side-stepping barmaid or staggering lush wanders a bit too close for comfort.  Behind the counter stands Haldram, a grey-bearded Dwarf with a fierce gaze."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":276,"exit":"go","move":"go oaken door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Thirteenth Passage"]},
  {"id":278,"x":130,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Dining Room","descriptions":["Despite the hustle and bustle, the dining room is well decorated.  Ornate lamps hang from the rafters, colorful light streaming through stained glass panels set into wrought iron frames.  Three secluded booths are accessible from here, one standing behind a suit of heavy plate armor on a wrought iron stand.  The second is blocked from view by a delicate tapestry depicting a cottage set in the mountains, and the third is separated by a folding privacy screen detailed in marquetry."],"exits":[{"to":277,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":279,"exit":"climb","move":"climb winding staircase"},{"to":420,"exit":"go","move":"go delicate tapestry"},{"to":421,"exit":"go","move":"go privacy screen"},{"to":422,"exit":"go","move":"go armor"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Dining Room"]},
  {"id":279,"x":120,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Downstairs Hallway","descriptions":["Settled at the bottom of a long winding staircase, the short hallway has been spared both the smoke and noise of the gaiety upstairs.  Two solid doors, one banded in brass and the other in iron, lead toward private rooms while the passage continues to the southwest."],"exits":[{"to":280,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":278,"exit":"climb","move":"climb winding staircase"},{"to":281,"exit":"go","move":"go brass door"},{"to":282,"exit":"go","move":"go iron door"}]},
  {"id":280,"x":110,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Downstairs Hallway","descriptions":["Two doors, one banded in copper and the other in bronze, mark the end of the short hallway.  Still well crafted from the rock of the mountain, this area seems less decorated than the upstairs, as though the available rooms it leads to were added as a necessity, rather than extra income for establishment."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":283,"exit":"go","move":"go copper door"},{"to":423,"exit":"go","move":"go bronze door"}]},
  {"id":281,"x":120,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Private Room","descriptions":["Directly across from the door are several recessions cut into the stone walls.  Each contains candles of a wide variety, casting their light against the bare rock that is most of the room.  The sole comfort here is an overstuffed mattress, which itself is also nested in a bowl of hollowed stone.  Bolts of tatted lace form a canopy over the bed through which shadows cast by the candlelight dance endlessly."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"go","move":"go brass door"}]},
  {"id":282,"x":110,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Private Room","descriptions":["Wrought iron lends itself to frame a large four-posted bed in the center of this room.  To one side is a nightstand on which rests an oil lamp, casting a steady glow which reflects the bright colors of the mosaic tiled floor."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"go","move":"go iron door"}]},
  {"id":283,"x":100,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Private Room","descriptions":["A long window of darkly tinted amber glass reaches from one side of the room to the other.  While too dark to see through, the window lets in just enough light from the tunnels beyond to illuminate the chamber in an orange glow.  A thick rug covers the stone floor giving the room a soft touch.  A bed, framed in maple and covered in plush blankets, stands against the far wall."],"exits":[{"to":280,"exit":"go","move":"go copper door"}]},
  {"id":284,"x":80,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Hvairn's Showldh Stal","descriptions":["A polished bell hung from a spring on the door tinkles merrily each time someone enters the room.  Redolent of pungent oak and acrid metal polish, the rough timber floorboards and walls are bare of superfluous ornament save for the wares on sale.  Shields of every hue and color, shape and design fill the glass case and the wide shelf, their sumptuous elegance counterfeiting glamour where in fact there is none."],"exits":[{"to":285,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"},{"to":101,"exit":"go","move":"go belled door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Hvairn's Showldh Stal","Shields"]},
  {"id":285,"x":100,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Hvairn's Heraldry Room","descriptions":["Pervading every nook and cranny is the prevalent stink of paint thinners and the acrid smell of burnt metal.  A counter divides the room neatly into two, behind which stands a desk whose surface is edged in miniature compartments, each holding items of the trade -- ink pots, brushes, and stylus.  Lyewend, who oversees the ordered chaos, stands framed by myriad small square drawers, each wooden front dotted with a small copper knob."],"exits":[{"to":284,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"}]},
  {"id":286,"x":80,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Carousel Central","descriptions":["In the center of this small cavern, a circular staircase leads further into the mountain below.  A small plaque bearing the words \"Rundmolen Carousel\" hangs above the staircase and points into the darkness.  Shouts, whistles and clicks constantly emerge from the hole in the ground -- occasionally, the entire cavern rumbles as a vault is maneuvered into place."],"exits":[{"to":491,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":102,"exit":"go","move":"go ornate door"},{"to":287,"exit":"climb","move":"climb circular staircase"}]},
  {"id":287,"x":120,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, The Carousel","descriptions":["Being so far underground, the only light this cavern receives comes from thirty gaethzen spheres set into the ceiling of the room.  The spiral staircase from the main cavern enters through a hole in the ceiling and deposits its travelers in the center of the room.  Frequent rumblings betray the presence of the Carousel machinery behind the solid stone walls."],"exits":[{"to":286,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":286,"exit":"climb","move":"climb circular staircase"},{"to":288,"exit":"go","move":"go registration desk"},{"to":289,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":483,"exit":"south","move":""}],"aliases":["Carousel","Vault"]},
  {"id":288,"x":140,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Carousel Desk","descriptions":["The distinct rumbling of Rundmolen machinery pulses behind the walls in this tiny alcove.  A tall Dwarven clerk sits behind the small stone pillar that serves as his desk and the repository of all money collected by the company."],"exits":[{"to":287,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":484,"exit":"go","move":"go registrar's office"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Lost and Found"]},
  {"id":289,"x":140,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Carousel Booth","descriptions":["A polished steel lever protrudes from the eastern wall of the small, granite-surfaced room, flanking a steel door to the north."],"exits":[{"to":287,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":290,"exit":"go","move":"pull lever;go door"}]},
  {"id":290,"x":160,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Carousel Chamber","descriptions":["A sturdy vault, set in the back wall, stands ready for your use.  A soft thick carpet of deep red covers the floor, and the walls are streaked with traces of alexandrite.  Looking at the back wall, you notice a tiny gap between it and the rest of the room.","A sturdy vault, set in the back wall, stands ready for your use.  A soft thick carpet of deep red covers the floor, and the walls are streaked with traces of alexandrite.  Looking at the back wall, you notice a tiny gap between it and the rest of the room.  Against the wall to the left of the door sits an elegant urn on an almhara pedestal.","A sturdy vault, set in the back wall, stands ready for your use.  A soft thick carpet of deep red covers the floor, and the walls are streaked with traces of alexandrite.  Looking at the back wall, you notice a tiny gap between it and the rest of the room.  Resting on a tsavorite stand is a tiny porcelain figure.","A sturdy vault, set in the back wall, stands ready for your use.  A soft thick carpet of deep red covers the floor, and the walls are streaked with traces of alexandrite.  Looking at the back wall, you notice a tiny gap between it and the rest of the room.  On the wall to the left of the door hangs an oil painting."],"exits":[{"to":289,"exit":"go","move":"close vault;go door"}]},
  {"id":291,"x":80,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"The Fashion Firmament","descriptions":["The room is as dark as night, and in fact seems designed to give that illusion: through some art or science, scores of little lights twinkle on the ceiling like stars in the sky.  In the darkness, the only furnishing clearly visible is a counter with a large menu beside it."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Fashion Firmament","Hilda","Clothing"]},
  {"id":292,"x":60,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Gemsmith, Rasiya's Appraisal","descriptions":["Sized like an after thought, this room has just enough space for the gemsmith to conduct her business.  Whether to give this area the illusion of space, or to provide something for Rasiya to rest her eyes on, the stone walls have been sculpted with flowers representative of the province."],"exits":[{"to":104,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow arch"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Rasiya's Appraisal","Gems"]},
  {"id":293,"x":40,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Orfna's Oddlies","descriptions":["The shop is large, sectioned into separate climates and decors to accommodate a variety of animals.  A small portion of the area is shrouded in shadow for the benefit of the more nocturnal beasts, while the rest is clean and brightly lit."],"exits":[{"to":94,"exit":"go","move":"go doors"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Orfna's Oddlies","Pet Shop"]},
  {"id":294,"x":60,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Entry","descriptions":["Illuminated warmly by flaring torches, the entrance hall has been elaborately and intricately carved into the rock.  To the north, a broad ramp leads down deeper into the mountain, lined on either side by rows of columns that create patterns of shadows crisscrossing the sloping floor."],"exits":[{"to":295,"exit":"down","move":"down"},{"to":99,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":295,"x":60,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Entry Passage","descriptions":["Raccoons carved in bas-relief march across the base of the walls while stone ravens take wing near the ceiling.  Elaborately carved columns spaced down the corridor provide shallow alcoves and shadows to rest or hide in.  Images of shy welkin peek at passersby from niches in the wall and from behind columns."],"exits":[{"to":294,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":296,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":296,"x":60,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Entry Passage","descriptions":["The bright yellow-orange light cast by the burning torches to either side creates flickering shadows, and the same errant breeze carries with it a faint, lovely scent of some costly incense.  In the moving light, the wall carvings take on life and color."],"exits":[{"to":295,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":297,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":297,"x":60,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Central Chamber","descriptions":["An enormous vaulted cavern opens out deep into the heart of the mountain, the ceiling lost in shadows far overhead.  The walls of the chamber appear untouched by any tools, displaying the natural beauty of the rock cradling this underground cathedral.  In its center, a highly polished granite altar rises, unadorned by carvings or ornamentation, and flanked to either side by two steadily burning tapers.","An enormous vaulted cavern opens out deep into the heart of the mountain.  In its center, a highly polished granite altar rises, unadorned by carvings or ornamentation."],"exits":[{"to":302,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":300,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":298,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":296,"exit":"up","move":"up"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Temple of Kertigen","Kertigen","pilgrim's badge","altar","shrine-5-04"]},
  {"id":298,"x":50,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Passage","descriptions":["Two simple torches, one on each wall, illuminate this short passage with flickering, shifting light.  Unlike the flames almost anywhere else in the city, they smoke and gutter as though made defectively or in too much haste.  The cavern to the west is dark, the light not reaching into it."],"exits":[{"to":297,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":299,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":299,"x":40,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Zachriedek's Altar","descriptions":["The cavern is small and the ceiling is rounded, barely high enough for a tall Human to stand without crouching, as though the workmen who created it wanted to spend no more time here than necessary.  A matte black stone altar in the center of the room is split in two by a jagged crack running its full width."],"exits":[{"to":298,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"aliases":["Zachriedek's Altar"]},
  {"id":300,"x":70,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Passage","descriptions":["The faint sound of chanting comes from somewhere not far off, reverberating softly in the narrow tunnel just enough to make determining its direction impossible.  The walls are almost within touching distance to either side."],"exits":[{"to":301,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":297,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":301,"x":80,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Divyaush's Altar","descriptions":["Though small, every inch of the snug cavern has been lovingly carved and worked by the finest masters of Dwarven stonecutting.  Ribbons of precious metals intertwine with great chunks of precious and semi-precious stones, to flow and weave in patterns so complex it is difficult to believe it is all cut from the surrounding rock.  In one corner, an iron railing marks a narrow stairway spiraling downward."],"exits":[{"to":300,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":307,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}],"aliases":["Divyaush's Altar"]},
  {"id":302,"x":60,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Passage","descriptions":["The passage has been carved through solid stone, straight and square-cut.  Twin sets of torches burn steadily to either side, their warmth held by the rock walls."],"exits":[{"to":303,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":297,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":303,"x":60,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Kertigen's Altar","descriptions":["A brilliant shaft of multicolored light slants down from the ceiling where a vein of prismatic quartz crystal reaches through the crust of the mountain.  Day or night, whether sun or moon, natural or Dwarf-made, the beautiful rainbow of light illuminates the cavern, shining directly onto a gleaming white quartz altar."],"exits":[{"to":304,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":302,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":305,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"aliases":["Kertigen's Altar"]},
  {"id":304,"x":70,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Hall of the Dead","descriptions":["Stretching off into the distance as far as the light reaches, the long, low cavern holds the remains of the residents of Hibarnhvidar who have passed on to remain with their gods.  Stately rows of stone catafalques bear the bones of heroes and kings, while precisely carved niches line the walls for those of poorer purse or less fame."],"exits":[{"to":303,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"aliases":["Hall of the Dead"]},
  {"id":305,"x":50,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Pool","descriptions":["Irregularly shaped and with only a packed earth floor, the small cavern is warm and well-lit.  A small stream falls in a musical descant from the ceiling far above to fill a small clear pool in the center of the room.  There appears to be no outlet for the water though the pool remains always the same size and depth."],"exits":[{"to":303,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":306,"exit":"go","move":"go still pool"}]},
  {"id":306,"x":40,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Serenity Pool","descriptions":["Surprisingly warm, the waters of the pool lap gently at its edges.  While the water would be chest deep on a Dwarf, rocks protruding from the sides provide comfortable seating for almost any size bather."],"exits":[{"to":305,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rock-cut steps"}],"color":"#0000FF","aliases":["Serenity Pool"]},
  {"id":307,"x":100,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Gathering Room","descriptions":["Set at intervals along the walls, crystal-chimneyed oil lamps provide bright illumination for reading and studying.  Comfortable chairs and couches are placed around the room in groups, with a few small study tables in the corners."],"exits":[{"to":308,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":309,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":310,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":301,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral stairway"}]},
  {"id":308,"x":100,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Clerical Dining Hall","descriptions":["Long tables with benches pulled up to the sides range the length of this narrow room.  At the far end, a massive sideboard is burdened with a dizzying array of food and drinks to rejuvenate tired bodies."],"exits":[{"to":307,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":309,"x":110,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Library","descriptions":["Ancient books and scrolls line the floor-to-ceiling shelves.  Rolling ladders provide access to higher volumes.  Deep-cushioned couches and chairs are scattered about the room, offering comfort during long hours spent studying the ponderous texts.  Special lamps, designed to emit the least amount of smoke into the air, are spaced around the room in elaborate silver sconces."],"exits":[{"to":307,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Kertigen Library"]},
  {"id":310,"x":100,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Temple of Kertigen, Clerical Dormitory","descriptions":["Rows of Dwarf-sized cots run down both sides of the low-ceilinged room, each separated by a moveable screen and with a carved wooden chest at its foot.  Although the accommodations are not elaborate, the mattresses are thick and comfortable-looking, and the blankets warm and fluffy."],"exits":[{"to":307,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":311,"x":20,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Dwarven Stomp Studio","descriptions":["This large rectangular chamber is bare of furniture.  Several rows are marked off by chalked lines drawn along the floor.  Carefully arranged against one wall are dozens of pairs of steel-toed boots from which a few people are making their selections.  Above the boots is a carefully lettered sign."],"exits":[{"to":136,"exit":"go","move":"go bronze-banded door"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Dwarven Stomp Studio","Agility"]},
  {"id":312,"x":-100,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Academy of Grunting","descriptions":["This cavern is very deep, and the slightest sound sets off an impressive series of echoes.  A cart to one side holds a tray of cheeses along with large pitchers of milk and ale.  In front of the food and drink are a stern-faced Dwarf and a hulking Gor'Tog who shoo away anyone trying to grab freebies."],"exits":[{"to":141,"exit":"go","move":"go copper-banded door"}],"color":"#FFFF00","aliases":["Academy of Grunting","Charisma"]},
  {"id":313,"x":100,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"MAMAS Hibarnhvidar, Main Office","descriptions":["Several small work stations ring the large cavern of the Merchant Adventurers' Mapping, Assay, and Survey Company's primary office in Forfedhdar.  Tools and survey instruments lie stacked at the various stations, soon to be available for purchase by adventurers needing the latest in mining equipment.  At the end of the cavern, a lone clerk stands by a counter with a set of small scales used to weigh individual items and stones of valuable minerals."],"exits":[{"to":128,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["MAMAS"]},
  {"id":314,"x":180,"y":280,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Ladar's Shop","descriptions":["The sounds of industry are mysteriously quiet in this small alcove of the mountain.  Since many of his potential customers can perform their own repairs, the proprietor of this small shop, Ladar, has much of his time to himself.  He sits on a stool at the side of the room, moving only to take care of the rare customer who wanders in."],"exits":[{"to":130,"exit":"go","move":"go solid arch"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Ladar's Shop","Repair Metal"]},
  {"id":315,"x":180,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Bards' Guild, Entry Hall","descriptions":["Numerous landscape paintings cover the walls of this short hallway, giving the room an illusion of windows that open on widely varying vistas.  The faint noise of a commotion can be heard, seeming to emanate from a pair of gilt doors opposite the arch to the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":117,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":316,"exit":"go","move":"go gilt doors"}]},
  {"id":316,"x":190,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Bards' Guild, Meeting Hall","descriptions":["The expansive room resembles a boisterous tavern more than it does a guildhall.  Tankards and glasses on the room's four tables indicate that the revelry has been going on for quite some time, and shows no sign of slowing down.  Weapon and armor racks standing near training dummies against the walls, however, hint at a time when the mood was far less celebratory.  An entryway to the south seems a bit quieter."],"exits":[{"to":317,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":315,"exit":"go","move":"go gilt doors"},{"to":427,"exit":"go","move":"go shimmering portal"}]},
  {"id":317,"x":190,"y":150,"z":1,"title":"Bards' Guild, Guildleader's Office","descriptions":["Although small, this office feels larger due to what appear to be windows.  A second glance, however, reveals that they are actually landscapes, similar to those in the entry hall of the guild.  A worktable holds some scrolls, but any guild records seem almost to be an afterthought, as the majority of the surface is covered in various containers of paintbrushes and paints.  An easel in the corner displays another picture, of which the artist is either proud, or lacks wall space for display."],"exits":[{"to":316,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Bard","Yaziyi","RS Bard"]},
  {"id":318,"x":200,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Doorway","descriptions":["This short corridor leads to an ironwood door covered with an iron grating.  On both sides of the door are bronze sconces set with wide, flickering candles.  Occasionally small spiders skitter across the ground towards their silken homes."],"exits":[{"to":116,"exit":"go","move":"go entry"},{"to":319,"exit":"go","move":"go ironwood door"}]},
  {"id":319,"x":230,"y":120,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Gathering Hall","descriptions":["Large obsidian braziers light up granite walls inside this hexagonal hall.  Although the air is slightly musty, there is no dust to be seen.  Two sets of plate armor stands flank the ironwood door as if standing guard.  Padded benches and chairs are scattered around the hall but do not hinder entry to other areas of the guildhall.  A stairwell chiseled from the natural stone leads up to a landing."],"exits":[{"to":321,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":323,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":322,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":320,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":318,"exit":"go","move":"go ironwood door"},{"to":332,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairwell"}],"aliases":["Paladins' Guild"]},
  {"id":320,"x":210,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Assembly Chamber","descriptions":["Primitive paintings of battles form a decorative band around the ceiling while an artistic mosaic of the Paladin Guild's crest is inlaid in the floor.  Granite chairs, covered with various furs, are arranged in a semi-circle around a raised podium.  A suit of darkened plate armor is displayed on a glass stand behind the podium.  In the far back of the room are some deeply carved steps that lead down into darkness."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":329,"exit":"climb","move":"climb carved steps"}]},
  {"id":321,"x":250,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Hallway","descriptions":["Along one wall is a picture drawn from charcoal and chalk.  While much of it is smudged, a crowd of Dwarven warriors fighting off a raging dragon can still be seen.  At the far end are some massive iron doors."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":326,"exit":"go","move":"go iron doors"}]},
  {"id":322,"x":220,"y":130,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dining Hall","descriptions":["This circular hall is a tribute to the skilled design of the guild's architect.  An expansive painted ceiling depicts a male Dwarf holding his arms out, each exaggerated arm extending down two walls.  Wax candles glitter from a ruby and crystal chandelier and the wall sconces, creating light and shadows across the painted Dwarf.  A long taborwood table with matching benches dominates the center of the room."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":324,"exit":"go","move":"go pantry door"}]},
  {"id":323,"x":240,"y":130,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Training Room","descriptions":["Polished battle-axes and shields hang from reinforced wooden beams that line the stone ceiling.  Large oak cabinets with bronze plaques affixed to the doors stand opposite each other against two of the walls.  A Dwarven sentry stands near the doorway, eyes occasionally shifting to some squires sparring on training mats."],"exits":[{"to":319,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"aliases":["Training Room"]},
  {"id":324,"x":220,"y":140,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Pantry","descriptions":["The floor is made from sturdy planks of lumber combined with mortar.  The whitewashed walls have pine shelves filled with food for a chef to prepare meals with.  A lacquered pine countertop is available for food preparation.  Two buckets filled with water are available in the corner."],"exits":[{"to":322,"exit":"go","move":"go door"},{"to":325,"exit":"climb","move":"climb darkened steps"}]},
  {"id":325,"x":220,"y":150,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Cellar","descriptions":["The scents of drying tobacco and herbs blend with that of aging ale and wine, creating an odd but not unpleasant odor within this large but cramped area.  The walls are barely visible behind stacked barrels.  The tobacco, hanging from wooden beams, scarcely allows a person space to walk without bumping against a bundle or two."],"exits":[{"to":324,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}],"aliases":["Tobacco"]},
  {"id":326,"x":250,"y":90,"z":1,"title":"Chapel of the Last Hope, Spiritual Gardens","descriptions":["Sweet jasmine and orchids, resting in hanging brass pots, exude fragrances that fill the senses with each breath taken.  A pale yellow luminescence hangs heavy in the room, providing light to the foliage living here."],"exits":[{"to":321,"exit":"go","move":"go iron doors"},{"to":327,"exit":"go","move":"go granite building"}],"aliases":["Chapel of the Last Hope","Spiritual Gardens"]},
  {"id":327,"x":250,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Chapel of the Last Hope, Inner Sanctum","descriptions":["Cracked whitewashed walls add a cold but sanitary feeling.  A few straw mats are piled in a corner awaiting the next pilgrim.  A large gold-flecked candleholder hugs one wall while a shelf filled with white candles lines the other.  Through the far archway is a small pool."],"exits":[{"to":326,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":328,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}]},
  {"id":328,"x":250,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Chapel of the Last Hope, Serenity Alcove","descriptions":["Some hanging lanterns with luminescent globes illuminate this serene room, highlighting the various plant life springing forth from moist cracks in the walls.  Thin streams of water hug the wall before settling into a small pool.  The floor is lined with woven prayer mats layered with fresh gardenias."],"exits":[{"to":327,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}],"aliases":["Serenity Alcove"]},
  {"id":329,"x":210,"y":90,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Passageway","descriptions":["As if saluting any who enter from the steps, a pair of ox-tongue spears cross at the blades.  The narrow passageway seems claustrophobic as smoke tendrils from torches swirl in the air.  At the far end of the hall is an archway leading to an underground chamber.","The narrow passageway seems claustrophobic as smoke tendrils from torches swirl in the air.  At the far end of the hall is an archway leading to an underground chamber."],"exits":[{"to":320,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"},{"to":330,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"},{"to":443,"exit":"go","move":"pull torch;go secret entrance"}]},
  {"id":330,"x":210,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Memorial of Champions","descriptions":["Block candles line a carpeted walkway through this enormous gallery.  A myriad of canvas paintings and tapestries hang high on the stone walls.  Arranged in strategic locations are carvings and wheels depicting stories through pictographs or in Haakish."],"exits":[{"to":329,"exit":"go","move":"go darkened archway"},{"to":331,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"}],"aliases":["Memorial of Champions"]},
  {"id":331,"x":210,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Tomb of the Fist","descriptions":["Thirteen wide braziers, glowing brightly, provide plenty of light in this enormous cavern.  Large bearskin rugs are scattered over the stone floor.  Near the center of the cavern are four stone lions standing guard around the corners of a marble dais.  Looming high from the center of the dais, a granite vault dominates the space, its edges worn from age.","Thirteen wide braziers, glowing brightly, provide plenty of light in this enormous cavern.  Looming high from the center of a dais, a granite vault dominates the space, its edges worn from age."],"exits":[{"to":330,"exit":"go","move":"go double doors"}],"aliases":["Tomb of the Fist"]},
  {"id":332,"x":230,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Landing","descriptions":["A mortar wall and steel bar railing create the bulk of this narrow walkway.  Beyond the steel bar is a spectacular view of the hexagonal-shaped gathering hall in all its glory.  Although there is little warmth up here, wolf pelts line the wall, and a long blue carpet leads to the guildleader's den."],"exits":[{"to":333,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":319,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairwell"}]},
  {"id":333,"x":230,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Guildleader's Den","descriptions":["Faded tapestries depicting the thirteen Immortals are meticulously hung from the walls in this spacious office.  Twin sets of plate mail, designed for the smaller races, sit on stands in two corners of the den.  A carved rosewood desk and antiquated chair dominate the center of the room.  Below them, an immaculate stone floor stretches from one end of the den to the other, partially covered with a plush rug in a deep burgundy thread."],"exits":[{"to":332,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":334,"exit":"go","move":"go rosewood door"},{"to":335,"exit":"go","move":"go stone archway"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Paladin","Darius","RS Paladin"]},
  {"id":334,"x":220,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Guildleader's Quarters","descriptions":["A large gaethzen sphere illuminates the area, lighting up the hues of dark brown and muted copper that make up the color scheme of the walls and furniture.  A mid-sized canopy bed and walnut armoire fill the bulk of the room, while a glass bar and stove are tucked away in the corner."],"exits":[{"to":333,"exit":"go","move":"go rosewood door"}]},
  {"id":335,"x":240,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, War Room","descriptions":["Books and documents line the walls on shelves with brass railings near the top.  Attached to the railings are tall ladders on wheels.  In the center of the room is a large, wiirwood table shaped like a nine-pointed star.  Velvet cushioned chairs are placed strategically around the room while a sand table and short ironwood case sit in one corner."],"exits":[{"to":333,"exit":"go","move":"go stone archway"}],"aliases":["War Room"]},
  {"id":336,"x":180,"y":100,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tunnel","descriptions":["Solid rock walls curve gently toward each other and come together somewhere above but the peak has been lost in the shadows.  Torches line the walls at regular intervals, their illumination nearly drowned out by a more intense light coming through an ogee arch.  The other end of the tunnel fades into a murky darkness to the north, only visible because of the torches lining the walls."],"exits":[{"to":337,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":118,"exit":"go","move":"go ogee arch"}]},
  {"id":337,"x":180,"y":90,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tunnel","descriptions":["A pinprick of light to the south is the only indication that this tunnel has any end.  The darkness is held at bay by a number of flickering torches bolted to the wall.  Carved into the rock wall, small arrows next to the crest of the Warrior Mage guild point north."],"exits":[{"to":338,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":336,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":338,"x":180,"y":80,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tunnel","descriptions":["A narrow staircase plunges at a sharp, but passable, angle downward into darkness.  Torches bracketed to either side illuminate both the tunnel leading southward, and the rough stone of the first few steps down."],"exits":[{"to":337,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":339,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow staircase"}]},
  {"id":339,"x":180,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Narrow Stairs","descriptions":["A set of narrow stairs leads up at a sharp angle towards a doorway in the distance.  The climb is steep in comparison to a set of broader steps which lead gently downward.  The air is damp and algae has grown in the cracks between squared stone blocks which form the staircase walls."],"exits":[{"to":338,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow stairs"},{"to":340,"exit":"go","move":"go stone steps"}]},
  {"id":340,"x":180,"y":60,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Narrow Stairs","descriptions":["A long hall separates two sets of steps, the algae-covered walls flanked by plain stone pillars.  Broad stone steps gently slope upwards towards the south while to the north narrow stairs ascend steeply to an archway high above.  The air is rank with a musty scent caused by stagnant puddles formed in low spots in the floor."],"exits":[{"to":339,"exit":"go","move":"go stone steps"},{"to":341,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow stairs"}]},
  {"id":341,"x":180,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Tunnel","descriptions":["Two large, fire-filled bronze bowls sit on either side of a small archway, working to light up the large tunnel.  The flames are bright enough that they illuminate the smooth stone walls which slope upwards into a tapered point as well as a set of narrow stairs which lead down on the other side of the arch."],"exits":[{"to":342,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":340,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow stairs"}]},
  {"id":342,"x":180,"y":40,"z":1,"title":"Inner Hibarnhvidar, Cavern Lake","descriptions":["Two torches are bracketed to the unnaturally smooth stone walls of an arched tunnel, dimly lighting a crag which juts out above a body of water.  The feeble light does little and shadows press in oppresively as the walls fade away into oblivion, giving off a sense of vastness."],"exits":[{"to":341,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":343,"exit":"go","move":"go stone bridge"}]},
  {"id":343,"x":180,"y":30,"z":1,"title":"Cavern Island, Sandy Beach","descriptions":["A stone bridge rises out of the lake and traverses the gap between an arch in the southern wall and the shore, leading up to a gateway.  Tall wicker torches line the small beach, illuminating the stone fortress' walls and giving it a menacing look.  Two silver banners hang down from the crenellations and flank the gateway, each bearing the crest of the Warrior Mage Guild."],"exits":[{"to":344,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":345,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":342,"exit":"go","move":"go stone bridge"},{"to":346,"exit":"go","move":"go arched gateway"}]},
  {"id":344,"x":190,"y":30,"z":1,"title":"Cavern Island, Sandy Beach","descriptions":["Torches line the beach, flickering and sputtering in the damp cavern air and illuminating the fortress walls.  The dominant sound is that of water lapping against the sandy shore, but occasionally there is the drip of falling water elsewhere in the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":343,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":345,"x":170,"y":30,"z":1,"title":"Cavern Island, Sandy Beach","descriptions":["Torches line the beach, flickering and sputtering in the damp cavern air and illuminating the fortress walls.  The dominant sound is that of water lapping against the sandy shore, but occasionally there is the drip of falling water elsewhere in the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":343,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":346,"x":180,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Courtyard","descriptions":["Large stone blocks stack atop one another to create a dull grey wall that surrounds the courtyard.  A steel portcullis is raised, allowing access to and from the courtyard through an arched gateway.  Large slabs of green slate pave the ground, covering nearly every square inch.  Care has been put into maintaining the area as none of the slabs contain cracks or even pitting."],"exits":[{"to":349,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":347,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":348,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":350,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":343,"exit":"go","move":"go arched gateway"}]},
  {"id":347,"x":200,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Courtyard","descriptions":["A catapult sits broken in this corner of the courtyard.  The wood shows signs of rot and the throwing arm is completely smashed beyond any repair.  A ladder has been set up next to the catapult, leading up the south wall."],"exits":[{"to":346,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":349,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":354,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"},{"to":357,"exit":"go","move":"go domed building"}]},
  {"id":348,"x":160,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Courtyard","descriptions":["A variety of mushrooms, ranging in size from pebbles to large Gnomes, fill this section of the courtyard.  A drainage ditch reveals a thick layer of soft loamy soil that spreads across the stone plateau, giving the mushrooms ample fertilizer.  Tightly fitted stones form what looks to be a low wall, ending almost a foot above the courtyard floor.  A sign is placed at the edge of the garden bearing large, white letters."],"exits":[{"to":350,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":349,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":346,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":349,"x":180,"y":-10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Courtyard","descriptions":["A flight of white marble steps leads from the courtyard to a limestone hall.  Two large brass braziers sit outside the door of the hall, casting off light and a generous amount of smoke.  The limestone walls are highly polished, gleaming even in the light cast off by the braziers."],"exits":[{"to":347,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":346,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":348,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":350,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":351,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}]},
  {"id":350,"x":160,"y":-10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Courtyard","descriptions":["A covered stone well sits next to a tall wall, which surrounds the courtyard.  The well looks to be no longer in use as a large board covers up the mouth and the bucket is missing.  A sign bearing large, white letters sits next to the well."],"exits":[{"to":349,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":346,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":348,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":351,"x":180,"y":-20,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Hall","descriptions":["A smoky smell from years of burning torches mingles with the smell of roasted food coming from the direction of a long table.  The polished oak table spans the hall, sitting directly below the peak of the thatched roof.  Flanking the table on either side is a row of thick stone columns that support wooden crossbeams.  A large bronze-banded oak door leads out to a courtyard paved with green slate."],"exits":[{"to":352,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":349,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}]},
  {"id":352,"x":180,"y":-30,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Hall","descriptions":["A long, polished oak table sits in the center of the hall.  On either side of the table are benches where a few weary looking warriors sit, eating food slowly from plates set before them.  Columns artificially partition the area into three segments, creating a wide walkway on either side of a long table that makes it easier to traverse the hall without bothering feasting warriors."],"exits":[{"to":353,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":351,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":353,"x":180,"y":-40,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Hall","descriptions":["A large space has been cleared at this end of the hall where a tall throne sits.  The gilded chair bears the Warrior Mage Guild crest on the back.  Behind the throne, two elaborate tapestries flank a small door that seems plain in comparison.  A polished oak table spans the length of the hall."],"exits":[{"to":352,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":366,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}]},
  {"id":354,"x":250,"y":0,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Battlement","descriptions":["Iron sconces, bracketed to the walls outside the fortress just below crenellations in its fortifications, dimly illuminate the battlement and the lake below.  Small pinpricks of light illuminate a bridge that leads to an arching entrance in a rock wall across the water from the keep.  The top of a ladder can be seen peeking above the inside of the wall, leading down to the green slate floor of the courtyard."],"exits":[{"to":355,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":347,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":355,"x":230,"y":0,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Battlement","descriptions":["Iron sconces have been bracketed to the walls on the outside of the keep and provide a dim illumination.  The battlements stretch from east to west, overlooking a stone bridge that leads to the southern wall of the cavern.  The entrance of the Warrior Mage Guild is visible here, the crenellations angled so that a casual glance down would allow one to see anyone entering or leaving the guild.  Two silver banners are visible through the crenellations, each bearing the crest of the Warrior Mage Guild."],"exits":[{"to":354,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":356,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":354,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":356,"x":210,"y":0,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Battlement","descriptions":["Iron sconces, bracketed to the walls outside the fortress just below crenellations in its fortifications, dimly illuminate the battlement and the lake below.  Water from the lake laps up against a sandy shore near the base of the fortifications while a large rock wall rises up to the south.  Occasionally, a loud dripping echoes from elsewhere in the cavern, disturbing the soothing sounds made by waves upon the sand."],"exits":[{"to":355,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":357,"x":200,"y":-10,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Supplies","descriptions":["Smooth stone walls have been polished to a glassy sheen.  The smell of smoke is heavy in the air and comes mostly from the direction of a leather flap in the northern wall.  A Dwarven attendant mutters to himself as he goes about his business of arranging and re-arranging the same items for no apparent reason."],"exits":[{"to":347,"exit":"go","move":"go southern door"},{"to":358,"exit":"go","move":"go leather flap"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Forge Supplies"]},
  {"id":358,"x":220,"y":-40,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Hall","descriptions":["An intersection is formed of two hallways, one running north and south and the other east and west.  In any direction the smell of smoke is thick, but breathable, made possible by the curved slope of the domed roof which leads the smoke to a large chimney directly above."],"exits":[{"to":363,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":359,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":361,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":357,"exit":"go","move":"go leather flap"}]},
  {"id":359,"x":240,"y":-40,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Honing Room","descriptions":["An occasional shriek of metal being pressed against a grindstone echoes throughout the corridor like a victim being tortured.  A light smoky scent fills the air, filtering in from elsewhere in the forge.  A casual glance upwards reveals most of the smoke being directed through a chimney in the center of the ceiling.  Every so often someone wanders by, carrying an assortment of weapons and looking extremely pleased."],"exits":[{"to":360,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":358,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":360,"x":230,"y":-30,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Honing Room","descriptions":["An occasional shriek of metal being pressed against a grindstone echoes throughout the corridor like a victim being tortured.  A light smoky scent fills the air, filtering in from elsewhere in the forge.  A casual glance upwards reveals most of the smoke being directed through a chimney in the center of the ceiling.  Every so often someone wanders by, carrying an assortment of weapons and looking extremely pleased."],"exits":[{"to":359,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":361,"x":200,"y":-40,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Foundry","descriptions":["A pile of coal sits near the southern wall, waiting to be fed to a fire in the large pit occupying the center of the room.  A crucible hangs from a wooden beam between the fire and several molds to facilitate the process of creating various ingots, plates and wires.  Large bellows sit next to the crucible, ready to be used to fan the flames when necessary."],"exits":[{"to":358,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":362,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":362,"x":210,"y":-30,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Foundry","descriptions":["A pile of coal sits near the southern wall, waiting to be fed to a fire in the large pit occupying the center of the room.  A crucible hangs from a wooden beam between the fire and several molds to facilitate the process of creating various ingots, plates and wires.  Large bellows sit next to the crucible, ready to be used to fan the flames when necessary."],"exits":[{"to":361,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":363,"x":220,"y":-50,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Hall","descriptions":["A bench gently curves along with the northern wall, serving as a resting place for those waiting to use various parts of the forge.  Every so often someone wanders in and out of the different arches, most likely impatient smiths waiting for their turn."],"exits":[{"to":358,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":364,"exit":"go","move":"go marble arch"},{"to":365,"exit":"go","move":"go granite arch"}]},
  {"id":364,"x":230,"y":-70,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Smithy","descriptions":["The room is filled with a reddish glow cast by the forge taking up most of the room.  The sounds of hammer against anvil and metal grinding against stone fills the air, along with the occasional hiss of hot metal meeting water.  A smoky scent fills the air every so often for a brief moment, only to be carried up the chimney in the forge's dome or one of the smaller ventilation shafts."],"exits":[{"to":363,"exit":"go","move":"go marble arch"}]},
  {"id":365,"x":210,"y":-70,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild Forge, Smithy","descriptions":["The room is filled with a reddish glow cast by the forge taking up most of the room.  The sounds of hammer against anvil and metal grinding against stone fills the air, along with the occasional hiss of hot metal meeting water.  A smoky scent fills the air every so often for a brief moment, only to be carried up the chimney in the forge's dome or one of the smaller ventilation shafts."],"exits":[{"to":363,"exit":"go","move":"go granite arch"}]},
  {"id":366,"x":180,"y":-50,"z":1,"title":"Warrior Mage Guild, Office","descriptions":["A high-backed wooden chair, bearing a large pair of antlers, sits behind a cluttered desk so that it faces a small door.  A large gilded bookcase sits squarely against the northern wall and has been stuffed near to bursting with various books, tomes and scrolls."],"exits":[{"to":353,"exit":"go","move":"go small door"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Warrior Mage","GL WM","Jorent"]},
  {"id":367,"x":120,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Entry","descriptions":["Golden-hued marble flooring flows to grey granite walls that vault high.  Thick oak beams crisscross overhead, with a copper lantern suspended from each cross section, to keep the shadows at bay.  Facing the arch to the cavern, an enormous tapestry composed of two horizontal panels drapes from ceiling to floor, its presence diminishing the echoes caused by the marble floor."],"exits":[{"to":368,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":372,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":120,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}],"aliases":["Empath"]},
  {"id":368,"x":140,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, East Hall","descriptions":["Small niches pepper the main wall, each fitted with a faceted crystal lens encircled by an iron frame.  Tiny iron hinges to the left of each lens indicate a method of access to the candles that nestle in the niches.  When lit, the glowing image of a riolur leaf casts a sprinkling of rainbows across the floor."],"exits":[{"to":369,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":367,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":371,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":369,"x":150,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, East Hall","descriptions":["Large iron lanterns depend from the ceiling and host a multitude of candles that brighten the hall to a near daylight glow.  The majority of the light focuses on a mural that dominates the southern wall, stretching from floor to ceiling.  Due to the earthy tones and raised sections on the mural, the light casts shadows that seem to shift and move along the wall at different points."],"exits":[{"to":370,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":368,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":370,"x":160,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, East Gallery","descriptions":["Down the center of the floor, a blue rug edged with black cord lines up evenly with the walls on each side.  The hall, and the rug, ends at a pair of ornate glass doors mounted with silver-finished handles.  The doors curve at the top, flaring slightly where they meet the hinges on either side."],"exits":[{"to":369,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":377,"exit":"go","move":"go glass doors"}]},
  {"id":371,"x":120,"y":30,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, North Hall","descriptions":["Uncluttered by artifacts, the marble floor stretches across a broad, open area.  Against the south wall, a golden velvet curtain tied back with a matching cord partially shrouds a staircase that spirals downward.  A large break in the wall opposite the stair accesses a passage leading north."],"exits":[{"to":375,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":368,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":372,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":395,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"}]},
  {"id":372,"x":100,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, West Hall","descriptions":["Tucked into the wall, a shallow alcove houses a bubbling fountain.  Fresh orange blossoms float in the glass basin of the fountain, illuminated from beneath by a carefully positioned candle.  Copper-colored curtains, tied back with black silk cord, frame the space.  A small mirror is mounted at the curve of the hallway leading westward to prevent collisions with those needing to turn the corner in a hurry."],"exits":[{"to":371,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":367,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":373,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":373,"x":90,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, West Hall","descriptions":["A simple oak bench sits against the wall, padded with a smooth leather cover.  Across the hall, marble columns support a latticed arch.  Woven through the lattice, silk jadice flowers coil and twine around a glass representation of the Empath Guild crest.  A small sign, mounted on the left column, bids welcome in many languages."],"exits":[{"to":372,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":374,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":374,"x":80,"y":50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, West Hall","descriptions":["Down the center of the floor, a tan rug edged with gold cord lines up evenly with the walls on each side.  The hall and the rug end at a large oak door that is partially ajar.  Brass sconces flank the door, the candles inside flickering and leaving a thin layer of dark soot on the granite."],"exits":[{"to":373,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":378,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}]},
  {"id":375,"x":120,"y":20,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, North Hall","descriptions":["The hall narrows, decorated with clusters of portraits and paintings on the western wall.  The eastern wall is blank but for a single painting surrounded by a gilded frame.  To the right of the frame, a small brass plaque embedded in the granite identifies the picture."],"exits":[{"to":376,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":371,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":376,"x":120,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, North Gallery","descriptions":["Here the passage widens again, giving way to a large arch that marks the transition into a broad room beyond.  The lighting is subtle, as if to soothe and hush the regular bustle of the guildhall.  An elaborately arranged stone jadice flower tiles the floor below the arch."],"exits":[{"to":375,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":379,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}]},
  {"id":377,"x":160,"y":40,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Library","descriptions":["Spacious and well lit, the library has plenty of seating covered in lush wine-colored fabric.  Desks and bookcases in warm wood tones complement the fabric, giving the room a serene, comforting glow.  A bespectacled young man sits at an information desk, quietly scribing on parchment as his finger taps absently against an open book.  Behind him, a large case holds the most frequently requested tomes."],"exits":[{"to":370,"exit":"go","move":"go glass doors"}]},
  {"id":378,"x":80,"y":40,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Guildleader's Office","descriptions":["A large fireplace, carved deeply into the granite wall, dominates the space.  The logs inside glow red, as if the fire inside had just died down.  To the right of the fireplace sit a plain desk and chair, stained in a dark finish.  Muted green glass lanterns hang at various points in the room, the largest centered over the desk.  Matching bookcases stand against the wall, their contents piled up and overflowing in stacks on the floor nearby."],"exits":[{"to":374,"exit":"go","move":"go oak door"}],"color":"#FF8000","aliases":["GL Empath","Dagreth Rendarak"]},
  {"id":379,"x":120,"y":0,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Social Lounge","descriptions":["Plush rugs in shades of blue and purple carpet the ground, quieting passing footsteps.  Large leather sofas and chairs cluster in small groups, occasionally decorated with throw pillows designed to coordinate with the rugs.  In the far corner, a small grated fireplace set into the wall lends warmth to a room surrounded by cool granite.  A stone staircase nestles against the eastern wall."],"exits":[{"to":376,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":414,"exit":"climb","move":"climb staircase"}],"aliases":["Social Lounge"]},
  {"id":380,"x":-50,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Hospital, Shalvard's Room","descriptions":["This small alcove off the main room is the work area of the resident healer of Hibarnhvidar.  Although many adventurers utilize the services of the primary Empaths' guild, Shalvard set up this small hospital to service those who do not desire to seek help from the guild."],"exits":[{"to":206,"exit":"go","move":"go wooden door"}],"color":"#00BF80","aliases":["Healer","Hospital","Shalvard Khalgrimis"]},
  {"id":381,"x":-50,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Hospital, Charnal Pit","descriptions":["Each breath forms a frosty cloud in the cold air of the room.  With no windows, it is impossible to tell where you are, but the faint click of footsteps outside the door is amplified as it echoes against the stone walls.  Bodies lie on tables, covered by stained sheets -- mute victims of the harshness of mountain life, and the difficulty of burial in the winter."],"exits":[{"to":207,"exit":"none","move":"knock metal door"}]},
  {"id":382,"x":-360,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Sarv Stof","descriptions":["Whorls of copper, malachite, and azurite run from the black granite arch in the northwest corner to the open stone doors in the east wall.  Large racks line the south and west walls."],"exits":[{"to":264,"exit":"go","move":"go black arch"},{"to":383,"exit":"go","move":"go stone doors"}]},
  {"id":383,"x":-360,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Kvafelar Stof","descriptions":["An occasional cry of pain can be heard through the loud laughter echoing around the circular bar that dominates this room.  Stone stools of varying heights surround the bar, and tankards of numerous sizes clutter it.  Midway between matching sets of stone doors to the west and northeast, a set of steps climbs the wall to a raised balcony."],"exits":[{"to":384,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone steps"},{"to":382,"exit":"go","move":"go stone doors"},{"to":385,"exit":"go","move":"go sturdy doors"}],"aliases":["Kvafelar Stof","Kegs"]},
  {"id":384,"x":-350,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Ram Viikalar","descriptions":["Stone steps climb the wall from the drinking hall below to this wooden balcony.  Large squared mikkhalbamar timbers are cantilevered from square holes in the stone wall, and thick red oak planks are laid across them.  Simple stools line the stone wall, and two low oak chairs in the center of the balcony face each other across a table set with blocks and handles."],"exits":[{"to":383,"exit":"climb","move":"climb stone steps"}]},
  {"id":385,"x":-370,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Eldar Stof","descriptions":["Eleven statues of barbarians line the walls, each on one knee and facing the flaming brazier in the center of the chamber.  Triangular stones inlaid in the floor point from the edge of the brazier to the statues honoring it."],"exits":[{"to":388,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":386,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":386,"x":-380,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Tunal","descriptions":["Dozens of alcoves in this broad corridor keep an arsenal of weapons and armor at the ready.  Torches are set into the wall between each pair of alcoves.  Guild guards keep watch over the alcoves."],"exits":[{"to":385,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":387,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":387,"x":-400,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Viikalar Stof","descriptions":["Bright silver strata flow through the granite blocks, catching the torchlight to illuminate even the far corners.  Training dummies are scattered about, obviously rended and repaired many times, and makeshift weapon racks stand along the north wall.  Stones of various sizes protrude from the floor at different heights, no doubt meant to keep warriors mindful of their footwork."],"exits":[{"to":386,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":264,"exit":"go","move":"go grey arch"}],"aliases":["RS Barbarian"]},
  {"id":388,"x":-360,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Turn Stedh","descriptions":["Polished granite walls surround a massive iron chain that is sunk into the inlaid marble floor and climbs into the darkness above.  Stairs lead up the north wall around the chain and into the Guildhall's famous tower, and a brushed bronze door is centered on the east wall."],"exits":[{"to":385,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":389,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"},{"to":394,"exit":"climb","move":"climb iron chain"}]},
  {"id":389,"x":-350,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Shal Turn","descriptions":["Silver runs in veins throughout the walls.  Intricate patterns guide the eye to stairs that continue upward around the walls from the steps below.  Torches are pushed through the large links of an iron chain that hangs through the center of the chamber from high above."],"exits":[{"to":390,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"},{"to":388,"exit":"climb","move":"climb steps"}]},
  {"id":390,"x":-350,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Shal Turn","descriptions":["Streaks of gold glitter in the blocks of stone carefully fit together to form the six walls that the stairs continue to spiral around.  The walls smoothly transition from the four walls below into what appears to be eight above.  The massive iron chain, laden with torches, continues above and below."],"exits":[{"to":391,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"},{"to":389,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite steps"}]},
  {"id":391,"x":-350,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Shal Turn","descriptions":["Eight granite walls are covered with a web of platinum threads inset into the stone.  Stairs, due to their lack of platinum embellishment, can be clearly seen to continue up and around the eight walls.  The platinum glitters in the light from the torches jammed into the iron chain hanging through the center of the chamber.  The torches barely light the steps leading down the tower."],"exits":[{"to":392,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"},{"to":390,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite steps"}]},
  {"id":392,"x":-370,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Shal Turn","descriptions":["The platinum spiderweb below gives way to a lace of silver and grey animite that covers every block of this chamber's twelve walls.  The heavy lace embedded in each step and makes the stairs hard to discern from the walls.  A massive iron chain is set into the granite ceiling and torches have been shoved into its links.  The stairs continue around the walls and upward from the steps below."],"exits":[{"to":393,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"},{"to":391,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite steps"},{"to":394,"exit":"climb","move":"climb iron chain"}]},
  {"id":393,"x":-380,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, Shal Hrot","descriptions":["A yard-tall rampart, punctuated with large stone slabs, surrounds two-thirds of the circular area carved from the mountainside.  The jet-black granite of the floor and rampart sets off the smooth grey of the stone slabs.  The architecture amplifies every footstep into an echoing clatter.  Two spears stabbed into the granite mark the sides of an opening to stairs leading down."],"exits":[{"to":392,"exit":"climb","move":"climb granite stairs"}]},
  {"id":394,"x":-360,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Elding Gwilt, An Iron Chain","descriptions":["A wider gap between torches offers a relatively safe respite from your climb."],"exits":[{"to":388,"exit":"none","move":"script autoclimbdown"},{"to":392,"exit":"none","move":"script autoclimbup"}]},
  {"id":395,"x":100,"y":30,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Lower Floor","descriptions":["A spiraling staircase coils against the wall flanked by iron banisters embedded in the granite for additional safety.  Tucked into the curve of the staircase sits a large settee covered in a burnished gold fabric.  A woven grass mat spans the oddly shaped floor, fitted carefully around the curves of the walls and staircase and halting a few inches short of a blue-tiled arch."],"exits":[{"to":371,"exit":"climb","move":"climb spiral staircase"},{"to":396,"exit":"go","move":"go tiled arch"}]},
  {"id":396,"x":100,"y":20,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Antechamber","descriptions":["Cool blue and green tiles fan out from the arch to sprinkle the floors and walls of this small dressing room which smells slightly of damp.  Warm air gusts through a doorway to the north, bringing with it the sounds of trickling water.  Near the doorway, hooks line the wall, some holding assorted colored towels.  A smooth wooden bench provides seating for those who wish to change."],"exits":[{"to":395,"exit":"go","move":"go tiled arch"},{"to":397,"exit":"go","move":"go doorway"}]},
  {"id":397,"x":100,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Warm Springs","descriptions":["A large cavern filled with gently bubbling water spans the space, with only a small ledge running around the rim.  Granite below the water near the ledges allows for easy footing when entering or exiting the pool before it descends into darkness at the midpoint.  A discarded red towel lies forgotten near the doorway to the dressing room."],"exits":[{"to":396,"exit":"go","move":"go doorway"},{"to":398,"exit":"go","move":"go pool"}]},
  {"id":398,"x":90,"y":10,"z":1,"title":"Warm Springs, Shallow End","descriptions":["Sloping from the outer ledge to a level just at a Human male's knee, the pool deepens gradually, allowing guests to relax at their own comfort.  Soothing waters lightly scented with something similar to eucalyptus bubble lightly, frothing slightly from the agitation.  At the center of this section, a flattened stone protrudes from the water, the surface darkened in patches from the damp."],"exits":[{"to":399,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":397,"exit":"go","move":"go ledge"}],"color":"#0000FF","aliases":["Warm Springs"]},
  {"id":399,"x":90,"y":0,"z":1,"title":"Warm Springs, Deep End","descriptions":["The granite slope ends suddenly, giving way to a deep pool of water that not even a Gor'Tog can stand in.  At the back of the pool, a large stack of chiseled stone slabs rises high, with runnels extending beneath an overhang and out of sight to funnel water out of the spring.  At the top of the pile, one slab extends out over the center of the pool."],"exits":[{"to":398,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":400,"x":80,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Trabe Plateau, Yurt","descriptions":["Thick furs line the walls and almost the entire floor, filling the interior with a heavy musk.  A wide circular hole sits in the roof above an inert fire pit, letting in light and allowing for a glimpse up into the sky."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Nomad"]},
  {"id":401,"x":140,"y":320,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Bookstore","descriptions":["A glaes arch divides the public forge from the main cavern.  Owned by Juln, a master smith of Hibarnhvidar, the area resounds with the dull roar of the furnaces, the screech of metal against grindstones and the hiss of hot metal being quenched beyond the hatch in the south wall.  At the entry, tables and counters groan beneath the weight of books for both casual and master smiths."],"exits":[{"to":402,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":131,"exit":"go","move":"go glaes arch"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Forging Society","Forging Books"]},
  {"id":402,"x":140,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Inner Corridor","descriptions":["Granite walls and arches support and decorate this hallowed hall of metalworking.  The crackle of fire from the forges and smithies and the sharp hiss of grinding metal echo around the area in a symphony for the senses.  A small hatch lined with soot leads back towards the main cavern and storeroom, and racks containing tools for sale line the walls.  The other tunnels lead to destinations most suited to a smith."],"exits":[{"to":401,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":403,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":407,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":410,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":487,"exit":"go","move":"go battered doors"}]},
  {"id":403,"x":160,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Foundry","descriptions":["The forging area feels warmer than most places in Hibarnhvidar due to a large fire kept constantly burning in the basement of the forge.  Heat from the blaze below bleeds up into a smaller standby fire in the room, enabling a well-trained smith to work with even the most difficult of metals.  A small pile of fuel sits by, waiting to be added to the fire."],"exits":[{"to":404,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":402,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Foundry"]},
  {"id":404,"x":180,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Foundry","descriptions":["A vent high in the ceiling helps to alleviate some of the heat circulating in this room.  A hearth has been set up against one wall, its fire fed from the blazes below, allowing work to proceed at all hours of the day.  A pile of fuel has been shoveled against the wall, allowing a smith to easily stoke the fire up to a raging inferno."],"exits":[{"to":405,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":403,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":405,"x":200,"y":360,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Foundry","descriptions":["Various forging accoutrements line the walls, encircling the fire located in the center of the room.  Blasts of heat from below constantly surge through the room."],"exits":[{"to":406,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":404,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":406,"x":180,"y":380,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Foundry","descriptions":["The forge fire takes up the entire northwest wall -- the roar of the blaze drowns out all but the strongest of noises.  A small access port in the center of the wall allows a smith to use the heat within for his own purposes.  On the opposite side of the room a pile of fuel waits to be used."],"exits":[{"to":405,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":407,"x":140,"y":360,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Tool Shop","descriptions":["A small alcove to one side of the room contains tables displaying tools for sale.  Several vents in the ceiling gently pull warm air from the foundries nearby."],"exits":[{"to":402,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":408,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Forging Tools"]},
  {"id":408,"x":140,"y":380,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Maker's Mark Hall","descriptions":["Maker's mark attendants wait in a small alcove above which hangs a variety of tools.  Prestigious crafters mill about and eagerly discuss trade skills with each other.  An old grindstone sits off to one side."],"exits":[{"to":407,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":409,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Maker's Marks"]},
  {"id":409,"x":140,"y":400,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Supply Depot","descriptions":["Fashioned similarly to the rest of the forge, this room offers additional space for the storage and sale of crafting supplies.  Large wooden pallets display materials that can be ordered at any time."],"exits":[{"to":408,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Forging Supplies","Deeds"]},
  {"id":410,"x":120,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Smithy","descriptions":["More suited to fine detail work than mass production, this room does not contain all the amenities the larger foundries possess.  However, it is much quieter, enabling smiths to concentrate on the projects at hand."],"exits":[{"to":402,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":411,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Smithy"]},
  {"id":411,"x":100,"y":340,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Smithy","descriptions":["The fire in the small forge, primarily used to reheat weapons or to prepare smaller items, burns merrily in the south wall.  A large anvil stands ready for smiths to pick up the hammer and set to work."],"exits":[{"to":410,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":412,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":412,"x":80,"y":360,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Smithy","descriptions":["The workbench, forge and anvil take up the entire west wall of this room, though there is plenty of room to walk around.  Smells of burning coal and warm metal vie for supremacy here, indicating the amount of work this room normally sees."],"exits":[{"to":411,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":413,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":413,"x":100,"y":380,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, Smithy","descriptions":["Two large counters bracket the forge and anvil located in the southeastern corner of this room.  An irregular layer of soot films the walls and counters near the forge and the smell of burning flesh lingers in the room."],"exits":[{"to":412,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":414,"x":120,"y":-20,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Hall of Healing","descriptions":["Shaded lanterns softly illuminate the gauzy, natural beige fabric draping the walls.  A woven reed chair thickly padded and covered with a white cotton material sits against the wall beneath a blue painting.  Under the chair sits a matching footstool.  The arms of the chair are shaped to resemble crutches, the sides arcing inward slightly before joining and descending to the floor."],"exits":[{"to":415,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":418,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":379,"exit":"climb","move":"climb staircase"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":415,"x":140,"y":-20,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Hall of Three","descriptions":["Like walking into a painting, the walls of this hall are filled with color and images.  Near the ceiling, shades of the sky at dawn meld into the yellowish glows of daybreak.  Beneath the sky, painted scenes flow from frozen barren wasteland to the early life of spring to wheat fields in the full growth of harvest.  In the center, a unicorn and a cow stand together, a foreleg of each touching the other lightly.  Nearly hidden in the grasses, an adder coils tightly around the touching forelegs."],"exits":[{"to":416,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":414,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":416,"x":150,"y":-30,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Hall of Research","descriptions":["Smelling slightly of crushed blocil berries, the hall features a marble-topped counter against one wall.  A copper basin with a small drain is mounted on one side of the counter, while the other side features a stove and other assorted experimental tools.  Above the counter, a plain wooden cabinet with clear glass doors displays shelves of mortars and jars ready for use."],"exits":[{"to":415,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":417,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":417,"x":130,"y":-50,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Hall of Guardians","descriptions":["A fabricated tree extends from the wall, its created branches twisting and dipping overhead.  Tiny images of woodwisps peep down through the branches.  Painted on the wall, as if standing in the shadow of the tree, an alfar stands proudly, head angled to look in the distance."],"exits":[{"to":416,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":418,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":418,"x":100,"y":-20,"z":1,"title":"Empaths' Guild, Hall of Battle","descriptions":["A dark red carpet covers the floor of a hallway dimly illuminated by guttering iron wall sconces.  An armor stand against one wall features a chainmail armor display, with some links rusted, broken, or bloodstained.  At the display's feet rest a battered shield emblazoned with the Empath Guild crest and a bundle of dried flowers tied with a sapphire-blue ribbon.  Mounted on the wall, a wooden plaque featuring brass nameplates lists some of those lost in the fields.","An armor stand against one wall features a chainmail display.  The hall is dimly lit and carpeted in dark red."],"exits":[{"to":417,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":414,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["RS Empath"]},
  {"id":419,"x":20,"y":130,"z":3,"title":"Fang Cove, Fate's Fortune Lane","descriptions":["A towering marble archway opens a gap in the wall to the north and separates the ongoing construction and somewhat more refined completed structures of Fate's Fortune Lane from the crude structures and makeshift walkway along the beach.  The entrance to a squat, wide bungalow sits in opposition to the arch, and the sheltering cliffs of Fang's Peak rise up from behind it.  To either side of the arch, cobblestones of different shapes and sizes have been laid out to form the wide Fate's Fortune Lane."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":0,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":96,"exit":"go","move":"go exit portal"}],"linksTo":"Map150_Fang_Cove.xml"},
  {"id":420,"x":140,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, A Concealed Booth","descriptions":["In this secluded corner, a stone bench encircles a sturdy table.  A recess in the wall holds a small lamp before a plate of polished silver causing light to pour into the booth."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":421,"x":130,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, A Booth Behind The Screen","descriptions":["Several small brackets above the seats hold lamps which illuminate the area.  A squat table sits in the center of the booth, hidden from view by the privacy screen."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":422,"x":130,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, A Secluded Booth","descriptions":["An iron frame suspended from the wall supports a row of cushions lining the edge of this corner booth.  A stone column in the middle has been fitted with a sheet of hammered copper, serving as a tabletop."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":423,"x":100,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Thieves' Den","descriptions":["A haze of smoke spitting from fatty tapers and streaming from ember-tipped cigars blankets the ceiling.  The walls of the room are not without windows however, shutter, curtain and pitch effectively block out even the faintest slivers of light from the tunnels beyond.  Several people can usually be found gathered around a scarred end-table, gambling on a game of dice or cards, either of which is usually accompanied by the retelling of close calls and daring escapes."],"exits":[{"to":280,"exit":"go","move":"go bronze door"},{"to":424,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow steps"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Thief Bin"]},
  {"id":424,"x":100,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Chamber","descriptions":["The chamber atop the steps is on level ground with the main barroom, though well recessed into the rock.  From here the clinking of coins and tumbling of dice is audible across the stone floor downstairs.  A single dim lamp casts barely enough light to make out the deadbolt lock on a solid steel door."],"exits":[{"to":423,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow steps"},{"to":425,"exit":"go","move":"go steel door"}]},
  {"id":425,"x":100,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"The Thirteenth Passage, Meeting Hall","descriptions":["A few lamps in wall brackets cast a faint glow across the long hall.  The remaining light filters in through bottles of assorted liquor on shelves that immediately open into the back of the barroom.  The center of the room is occupied by a long table.  Heavy rugs covering every inch of the floor muffle footsteps, while an incredibly thick tapestry covers the back wall, making any noise sound hollow and empty."],"exits":[{"to":424,"exit":"go","move":"go steel door"}]},
  {"id":426,"x":-180,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Paasvadh Forest, Clearing","descriptions":["The wide clearing has random patches of lush grass intermingled with large bare spots.   Workers rush to and fro, deftly cutting festival goers from the sticky bonds that confine them to the treetops enclosing the area.  Children and adults alike are abuzz with excited chatter as they cross the brightly festooned bridge into the festival grounds."],"exits":[]},
  {"id":427,"x":180,"y":150,"z":1,"title":"Bards' Guild, Siryn's Study","descriptions":["Mahogany panels cover the walls of this room, warmly reflecting the light from the suspended gaethzen orbs.  Several chairs around the room invite guests to sit in comfort as they discuss topics of interest.  A desk sits in front of a bookcase, which is filled with tomes and scrolls on music, magic, and other subjects.  A quill rests across the desk, as if only recently laid down, next to a full glass of wine."],"exits":[{"to":316,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":428,"x":170,"y":70,"z":1,"title":"Bards' Guild, Conference Room","descriptions":["A large oak table surrounded by a number of stools dominates the room.  Maps cover the walls, displaying four of the provinces.  On the table lies the map of Zoluren, arrows marked in red across the parchment."],"exits":[]},
  {"id":429,"x":100,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Entry","descriptions":["Gleaming like a bright star in a night sky, an uthamar arch separates the Enchanting Society from the main cavern.  Small gaethzen tetrahedrons are strategically placed to provide just enough light to see by, but not so much as to inhibit the dim, soothing ambience of the room."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":127,"exit":"go","move":"go uthamar arch"}],"aliases":["Enchanting Society"]},
  {"id":430,"x":100,"y":245,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Hall","descriptions":["Embedded within the stone walls, bits and pieces of mica sparkle underneath the gaethzen string lights that are strung across the cavern's high ceiling.  Four arches of orichalcum, loimic, mistglass, and animite are positioned at each corner of the square hall and placed equidistant to each other."],"exits":[{"to":431,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":429,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":435,"exit":"go","move":"go orichalcum arch"},{"to":436,"exit":"go","move":"go loimic arch"},{"to":437,"exit":"go","move":"go mistglass arch"},{"to":438,"exit":"go","move":"go animite arch"},{"to":490,"exit":"go","move":"go recessed alcove"}]},
  {"id":431,"x":100,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Bookstore","descriptions":["The cavern narrows into a long, skinny chamber where one side is completely covered in bookshelves formed of marble slabs.  Dwarven attendants dressed in sturdy canvas coveralls stand ready to take book orders."],"exits":[{"to":432,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":430,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Enchanting Books"]},
  {"id":432,"x":100,"y":215,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Tool Store","descriptions":["The cavern expands outwards into a shape similar to that of a trapezoid.  Carved into the back wall, open shelves are neatly stacked with various tools of the trade.  Dwarven attendants dressed in sturdy canvas coveralls stand ready to take tool orders."],"exits":[{"to":433,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":431,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Enchanting Tools"]},
  {"id":433,"x":100,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Supply Store","descriptions":["The cavern opens up into a large rhombus-shaped room with squat metal cabinets lined up against the walls.  Dwarven attendants dressed in sturdy canvas coveralls stand ready to take supply orders."],"exits":[{"to":434,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":432,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Enchanting Supplies"]},
  {"id":434,"x":100,"y":185,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Society Master's Office","descriptions":["The cavern terminates into a large round chamber that is softly lit with gaethzen stars.  Ranging from simple to complex, sigils of all sorts are carved into the curved stone walls.  A wide uthamar desk and matching chair are set at the center of the room."],"exits":[{"to":433,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":435,"x":85,"y":245,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Orichalcum Workroom","descriptions":["Deeply recessed from the hallway, the small cavern's dense stone walls protect the workroom's inhabitants from being unduly disturbed by outside noise.  A sturdy granite table placed to the side of the room provides ample working space."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go orichalcum arch"}],"aliases":["Enchanting Workroom 1","Orichalcum Workroom"]},
  {"id":436,"x":115,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Loimic Workroom","descriptions":["Deeply recessed from the hallway, the small cavern's dense stone walls protect the workroom's inhabitants from being unduly disturbed by outside noise.  A sturdy granite table placed to the side of the room provides ample working space."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go loimic arch"}],"aliases":["Enchanting Workroom 3","Loimic Workroom"]},
  {"id":437,"x":115,"y":245,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Mistglass Workroom","descriptions":["Deeply recessed from the hallway, the small cavern's dense stone walls protect the workroom's inhabitants from being unduly disturbed by outside noise.  A sturdy granite table placed to the side of the room provides ample working space."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go mistglass arch"}],"aliases":["Enchanting Workroom 4","Mistglass Workroom"]},
  {"id":438,"x":85,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, Animite Workroom","descriptions":["Deeply recessed from the hallway, the small cavern's dense stone walls protect the workroom's inhabitants from being unduly disturbed by outside noise.  A sturdy granite table placed to the side of the room provides ample working space."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go animite arch"}],"aliases":["Enchanting Workroom 2","Animite Workroom"]},
  {"id":439,"x":-280,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Traveler's Shrine, Vestibule","descriptions":["Ranging through all the fiery shades of yellow, orange and red, the natural variance in color of the stone walls resembles dancing flames.  An unusual piping song whispers through the area, occasionally falling quiet at irregular intervals.  The source of the haunting music is a series of hollowed sticks fashioned into flutes and cleverly secured by the arched entry to catch any gusts of air.","Ranging through fiery shades of orange and red, the variance in color of the stone walls resembles dancing flames.  A piping song whispers through the area, falling quiet at irregular intervals."],"exits":[{"to":440,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":50,"exit":"go","move":"go arched entry"},{"to":441,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"}]},
  {"id":440,"x":-270,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Traveler's Shrine, Refectory","descriptions":["Sturdy trestle tables and low stone benches offer a place to eat, drink and rest.  Brass lanterns hang from the walls between pine shelves, filling the windowless room with a soft glow and the scent of lamp oil mingled with fresh baked bread and coffee.  Braided rag rugs cover the stone floor between the tables and the kitchen area, where a large iron stove and a battered pine sideboard offer a variety of foods.","Sturdy tables and benches offer a place to eat.  Brass lanterns hang from the walls filling the windowless room with a soft glow.  Braided rag rugs cover the floor between a large iron stove and a battered pine sideboard."],"exits":[{"to":439,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":442,"exit":"go","move":"go pine door"}]},
  {"id":441,"x":-280,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Traveler's Shrine, Altar Alcove","descriptions":["Soaring upwards to form a dome overhead, the white walls are decorated predominantly with paint and stone mosaics that will not interfere with the exemplary acoustics of the chapel.  Phoenixes shimmering with traces of copper gilt are depicted emerging from gold-streaked crimson marble flames.  Each bird's attention is focused upon a portrait of a slender Elven woman with red hair.","The chapel is decorated with paint and stone that will not interfere with the exemplary acoustics.  Emerging from a mosaic of flames, phoenixes direct their attention to a portrait of a slender Elven woman with red hair."],"exits":[{"to":439,"exit":"go","move":"go curtained archway"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Traveler's Shrine","Murrula","pilgrim's badge","altar","shrine-5-02"]},
  {"id":442,"x":-260,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Traveler's Shrine, Dormitory","descriptions":["Amber-shaded lamps illuminate the area with warm light.  Spartanly furnished, the dormitory is lined with iron cots piled with wool blankets and stone bins to keep clutter to a minimum.  Thick curtains divide the room into smaller areas, to give some modicum of privacy as well as to keep out chilling drafts.","Amber-shaded lamps illuminate the area.  Spartanly furnished, the dormitory is lined with iron cots and stone bins.  Thick curtains divide the room into smaller areas.","Spartanly furnished, the dormitory is lined with iron cots piled with wool blankets and stone bins to keep clutter to a minimum.  Thick curtains divide the room into smaller areas, to give some modicum of privacy as well as to keep out chilling drafts.  The soft glow of amber-shaded lamps light the room enough so late arrivals do not stumble in the dark, but not brightly enough to disturb sleepers.","Spartanly furnished, the dormitory is lined with iron cots and stone bins.  Thick curtains divide the room into smaller areas.  The lamps light the room enough so late arrivals do not stumble in the dark, but not brightly enough to disturb sleepers."],"exits":[{"to":440,"exit":"go","move":"go pine door"}]},
  {"id":443,"x":320,"y":170,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":443,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true},{"to":331,"exit":"none","move":"touch image"}]},
  {"id":444,"x":300,"y":170,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":444,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":443,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":445,"x":320,"y":190,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":445,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":444,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":446,"x":340,"y":190,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":446,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":445,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":447,"x":320,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":447,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":446,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":448,"x":300,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":448,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":447,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":449,"x":320,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":449,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":448,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":450,"x":340,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":450,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":449,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":450,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":451,"x":340,"y":250,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  A chill in the air makes the silence nearly tangible and thickly oppressive, capable of driving even the most level-headed Dwarf completely mad.  In the middle of the floor is a small image.","The ceiling and floor are made of smooth marble.  In the middle of the floor is a small image."],"exits":[{"to":450,"exit":"north","move":"north","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"east","move":"east","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"south","move":"south","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest","hidden":true},{"to":452,"exit":"west","move":"west","hidden":true},{"to":451,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":452,"x":320,"y":250,"z":1,"title":"Paladins' Guild, Dark Passageway","descriptions":["A single torch lights up the small tunnel and an archway on the western end.  Two stone lions, intricately carved directly from the wall, flank the archway.  Soulstone eyes appear to blink in the flickering torchlight.","A single torch lights up the small tunnel and an archway on the western end.  Two stone lions, intricately carved directly from the wall, flank the archway."],"exits":[{"to":451,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":453,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"}]},
  {"id":453,"x":320,"y":270,"z":1,"title":"Excavated Site, Burial Chamber","descriptions":["Although well-kept, this chamber appears to have been hollowed out with little thought for aesthetics.  Lining the back wall are animite chests with thick locks.  Sitting on top of each chest are various sets of armor worn by time.  Near the center of the room is a half-rotten wooden coffin, barely preserved but for a large glass box sealed over it.  Displayed on top of the box is a set of old mail armor with butted links.","Lining the back wall are animite chests with thick locks.  Near the center of the room is a half-rotten wooden coffin, barely preserved but for a large glass box sealed over it."],"exits":[{"to":452,"exit":"go","move":"go archway"},{"to":454,"exit":"go","move":"look wall shield;go opening"}],"aliases":["Excavated Site","Burial Chamber"]},
  {"id":454,"x":320,"y":290,"z":1,"title":"Excavation Site, Antechamber","descriptions":["Like the burial chamber, this room has been hastily dug out.  It appears that the builder put more thought into what items would be in here than ensuring safety when traversing the jaggedly cut walls and uneven floor.  Hanging from a hook is a metal mobile with hammered discs dangling from it.","Like the burial chamber, this room has been hastily dug out.  Hanging from a hook is a metal mobile with hammered discs dangling from it."],"exits":[{"to":453,"exit":"go","move":"go opening"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Excavation Site","Antechamber","holy weapon exchange","Chadatru","pilgrim's badge","altar","shrine-5-01"]},
  {"id":455,"x":-320,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Skin Deep","descriptions":["Distressed bricks line the walls of this small room, their muted red hue complementing the dark russet tones of the black locust wood floor.  A trio of lanterns hung from the center of the ceiling illuminates the room and casts a soft light over the space.  In the corner rests a small desk strewn with tiny doodles captured on scraps of paper."],"exits":[{"to":48,"exit":"go","move":"go iron-framed door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Skin Deep","tattoo"]},
  {"id":456,"x":0,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Many Sign of Many Savage, Open Chamber","descriptions":["Holes in the chamber's roughly hewn walls allow air to circulate in and out from other nearby facilities.  Tapestries and maps depicting far off places are prominently displayed, and the shop's owner frequently pauses before one or another to stare wistfully.  As patrons come and go, he seems particularly excited by non-Dwarven visitors and does his best to speak to them in very broken common."],"exits":[{"to":84,"exit":"go","move":"go rough-hewn opening"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Many Sign of Many Savage","Signs","Markers","Area Markers"]},
  {"id":457,"x":260,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Entrance","descriptions":["Polished stone walls gleam in the diffused light cast by bronze lamps overhead.  A pair of frosted glass doors leads back out into the bustling caverns of Hibarnhvidar.  A long carpet runner, decorated with alchemical herbs and tools, runs from the doors deeper into the society."],"exits":[{"to":458,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":121,"exit":"go","move":"go glass door"},{"to":489,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy entryway"}]},
  {"id":458,"x":260,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Lobby","descriptions":["Cozy groupings of chairs and sofas provide a spot to socialize and network for those society members taking a break from alchemical processes.  Wall sconces provide subdued lighting that helps relieve eyestrain from staring at too many retorts or stoves.  The quiet murmur of conversations fills the background as members relax and unwind."],"exits":[{"to":457,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":459,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":460,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"aliases":["Alchemy Society","Alchemy Prestige"]},
  {"id":459,"x":270,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Books","descriptions":["Shelves display books available for purchase while a chart shows techniques.  A clerk notes work order completions on a board."],"exits":[{"to":464,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":461,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":460,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":458,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Alchemy Books"]},
  {"id":460,"x":250,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Supplies","descriptions":["Shelves of spices, herbs, and other ingredients line the walls while clerks dart to and fro filling orders for customers.  A long counter allows for the inspection of the various supplies before final purchase."],"exits":[{"to":458,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":459,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":464,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":461,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Alchemy Supplies"]},
  {"id":461,"x":250,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Workroom","descriptions":["A set of alchemical equipment is centered in this laboratory carved out of living rock.  Pipes along the ceiling are covered with holes that provide a way for any deadly gasses released to eventually be piped to the surface."],"exits":[{"to":460,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":459,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":464,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":463,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":462,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"aliases":["Alchemy Workroom","Alchemy Dryer","Alchemy Press"]},
  {"id":462,"x":240,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Workspace","descriptions":["A set of alchemical equipment is centered in this laboratory carved out of living rock.  Pipes along the ceiling are covered with holes that provide a way for any deadly gasses released to eventually be piped to the surface."],"exits":[{"to":461,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":463,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":463,"x":260,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Workshop","descriptions":["A set of alchemical equipment is centered in this laboratory carved out of living rock.  Pipes along the ceiling are covered with holes that provide a way for any deadly gasses released to eventually be piped to the surface."],"exits":[{"to":464,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":465,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":462,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":461,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":464,"x":270,"y":230,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Tools","descriptions":["Stacks of supply crates line the walls while the counter displays various alchemical tools for sale.  Frazzled-looking clerks help customers with their purchases."],"exits":[{"to":459,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":465,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":463,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":461,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":460,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Alchemy Tools"]},
  {"id":465,"x":280,"y":240,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, Office","descriptions":["Except for a desk, there is little to mark out this area as belonging to the Society Master.  The heaps of papers on the desk vie with bits of dried plants and various other ingredients, all of them fighting a losing battle to not slide off the messy desk onto the floor."],"exits":[{"to":463,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":464,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":466,"x":200,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Reception","descriptions":["Carved into the living stone, the large circular room has eight equally spaced exits.  A desk stands near the wall, situated to keep an eye on all the traffic moving through the outfitting society.  The mirror smooth walls are hung with bright tapestries that display the talents of the members of the society."],"exits":[{"to":470,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":471,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":472,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":473,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":474,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":467,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":468,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":469,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":486,"exit":"go","move":"go tall archway"},{"to":122,"exit":"climb","move":"climb circular staircase"}],"aliases":["Outfitting"]},
  {"id":467,"x":190,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Spinning Hall","descriptions":["Large wicker baskets stand near the spinning wheel in the center of the room, ready for holding supplies for artisans working on new projects.  While one stool is placed at the wheel, a few others of varied heights line the walls, allowing spinners of any height to sit comfortably at the wheel and work."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":468,"x":190,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Spinning Room","descriptions":["Large wicker baskets stand near the spinning wheel in the center of the room, ready for holding supplies for artisans working on new projects.  While one stool is placed at the wheel, a few others of varied heights line the walls, allowing spinners of any height to sit comfortably at the wheel and work."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"aliases":["Outfitting Spinning"]},
  {"id":469,"x":190,"y":190,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Weaving Hall","descriptions":["A few sturdy shelves rest against the stone walls of the chamber, providing space for supplies to be stored.  In the center of the room, a wooden loom stands under a series of hanging lanterns which bathe the room in brilliant light.  A bench stands in front of the loom, ready for someone to sit and weave."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"aliases":["Outfitting Weaving"]},
  {"id":470,"x":200,"y":190,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Weaving Hall","descriptions":["A few sturdy shelves rest against the stone walls of the chamber, providing space for supplies to be stored.  In the center of the room, a large loom stands under a series of hanging lanterns which bathe the room in brilliant light.  A bench stands in front of the loom, ready for someone to sit and weave."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":471,"x":210,"y":190,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Supply Emporium","descriptions":["Cubbyholes chiseled from the rock walls display the vast array of fabrics, leathers and other supplies available to members for their projects.  Swatches of some of the textiles and threads are set out on the counter for inspection before purchase."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Outfitting Supplies"]},
  {"id":472,"x":210,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Book Emporium","descriptions":["Racks hold the manuals and booklets available for purchase, allowing the patrons to peruse before taking their selections to the polished stone counter near the door.  A bearded Dwarf stands ready at the counter to assist shoppers with questions or to complete purchases."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Outfitting Books"]},
  {"id":473,"x":210,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Tool Emporium","descriptions":["Sturdy shelves behind the long wooden counter hold a variety of tools needed by the members of the society, all neatly stored away for easy access.  A burly looking Dwarf stands behind the counter, his beady eyes missing nothing that happens in the chamber."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Outfitting Tools"]},
  {"id":474,"x":200,"y":210,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, Office","descriptions":["Thick tapestries cover the walls, obscuring the stone the chamber was carved from.  Papers are piled on the desk in haphazard stacks, threatening to spill over the floor at any moment.  Swatches of cloth and design sketches fill a small rolling cart next to the desk, ready for the next project."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":475,"x":70,"y":187,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Entry","descriptions":["Scents of oils, ash, and other unidentifiable odors waft through the entryway, drifting from deeper within the Society.  A passageway to the east leads to the master's office, while a wider tunnel in the south wall provides access to the rest of the working areas.  A few chairs, battered from much use, sit on the polished stone floor."],"exits":[{"to":476,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":477,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":113,"exit":"go","move":"go iron hatchway"},{"to":488,"exit":"go","move":"go rectangular doorway"}]},
  {"id":476,"x":83,"y":187,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Office","descriptions":["Metal racks line the walls, holding a variety of bins, boxes, and baskets.  Each container is labeled with a neatly-lettered tag denoting what is stored within.  A wide table in the center of the room is covered with paperwork while a comfortable chair is pushed back from the surface."],"exits":[{"to":475,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Engineering Prestige"]},
  {"id":477,"x":70,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Depot","descriptions":["Standing in the center of the room is a large semi-circular counter, behind which busy clerks take and fulfill orders for the crafters.  A large crate stands at one end of the counter while a sign hangs on one wall."],"exits":[{"to":475,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":479,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":478,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":480,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":481,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":482,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Engineering Supplies"]},
  {"id":478,"x":83,"y":213,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Workspace","descriptions":["Roughly in the center of the room stands a work bench covered with tools.  Gouges and scratches mar the thick planks of the worktable's surface.  Wood shavings and stone bits dot the polished stone floor."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":479,"x":83,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Workshop","descriptions":["Roughly in the center of the room stands a work bench covered with tools.  Gouges and scratches mar the thick planks of the worktable's surface.  Wood shavings and stone bits dot the polished stone floor."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"aliases":["Engineering Workshop","Gear Press"]},
  {"id":480,"x":70,"y":213,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Workroom","descriptions":["Roughly in the center of the room stands a work bench covered with tools.  Gouges and scratches mar the thick planks of the worktable's surface.  Wood shavings and stone bits dot the polished stone floor."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":481,"x":57,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Toolstore","descriptions":["Tools hang from corkboard decorating this long, rectangular room.  A thick scent of oil clings to the air, and the scraping sound of stone sharpening metal drones on in the background.  Some nearby salespeople wait to help customers."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Engineering Tools"]},
  {"id":482,"x":57,"y":187,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, Bookstore","descriptions":["Most of the room is blocked off by a long counter behind which stand tall bookshelves in neat rows.  Busy clerks move between the counter and the shelves, filling orders for the engineers.  An overpowering scent of ink and leather fills the area."],"exits":[{"to":477,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Engineering Books"]},
  {"id":483,"x":120,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Carousel Family Services","descriptions":["A series of guarded arches line the southern wall.  The complicated framework of iron and timbers spans across the ceiling.  Countless gears, pulleys and weights form the strikingly complex mechanism which drives the Carousel."],"exits":[{"to":287,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"aliases":["Family Services","family vaults"]},
  {"id":484,"x":160,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Item Registration Office","descriptions":["A few gaethzen spheres on the ceiling provide a dim light to the underground office.  Damp walls surround the office which has a few cabinets and a low counter with a content looking Dwarven clerk behind it."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":485,"exit":"go","move":"go simple curtain"}]},
  {"id":485,"x":180,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Registrar's Office","descriptions":["An even smaller portion of the cave is portioned off for the registrar.  A single gaethzen sphere is set into a carved stone desk providing just enough light to get the necessary paperwork accomplished.  A few cabinets can be made out, hiding amongst the shadowy walls."],"exits":[{"to":484,"exit":"go","move":"go simple curtain"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Item Registration Office","Registrar's Office"]},
  {"id":486,"x":220,"y":200,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Outfitting Society, A Private Outfitting Room","descriptions":["A pure-white wainscoted hall is topped by lilac-hued paisley painted walls.  Occupying the back third of the room is a solid-looking loom, while a large spinning wheel sits near the entrance.  Resting atop a deep purple rug is a sturdy worktable and a comfortable, wicker chair.  Running parallel along opposing walls are several hooks and shelves, holding practically every conceivable tool, spool of thread, bobbin, thimble and scrap."],"exits":[{"to":466,"exit":"go","move":"go tall archway"}],"aliases":["Private Outfitting"]},
  {"id":487,"x":160,"y":360,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Forging Society, A Private Forge","descriptions":["Thick walls struggle to contain the blistering heat of the workshop where the fires blaze endlessly night and day.  The flickering flames give a reddish glow to the racks and shelves of tools and equipment, all neatly placed and ready for use.  Workers enter in their protective gear from time to time, checking the equipment and reporting back to a sentry at the entry."],"exits":[{"to":402,"exit":"go","move":"go tall archway"}],"aliases":["Private Forge"]},
  {"id":488,"x":57,"y":213,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Engineering Society, A Private Engineering Room","descriptions":["A fine layer of wood and stone shavings covers most of the well-worn granite floor.  The white walls have seen better days, and black and grey scuff marks adorn much of the open space.  A large workstation along one wall is unnaturally free of clutter and holds several organized tools and implements.  Grunts, curses, and labored breathing from other patrons echo throughout the large workroom."],"exits":[{"to":475,"exit":"go","move":"go rectangular door"}],"aliases":["Private Engineering"]},
  {"id":489,"x":270,"y":180,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Alchemy Society, A Private Alchemy Room","descriptions":["A large workbench dominates one side of the room with numerous pieces of alchemical equipment scattered haphazardly upon its surface.  The high, vented windows provide relief from the common, yet unpleasant, smell that permeates the room."],"exits":[{"to":457,"exit":"go","move":"go shadowy entryway"}],"aliases":["Private Alchemy"]},
  {"id":490,"x":85,"y":260,"z":1,"title":"Hibarnhvidar Enchanting Society, A Private Enchanting Room","descriptions":["Pieced together by a seemingly blind worker, the walls are covered with scraps of rugs, blankets, and carpets in a kaleidoscope of colors.  A burly, light pink feldspar table is stashed in a corner of the room, providing plenty of room to work."],"exits":[{"to":430,"exit":"go","move":"go recessed alcove"}],"aliases":["Private Enchanting"]},
  {"id":491,"x":100,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Hibarnhvidar, Rundmolen Post Office","descriptions":["Tucked away in a corner of the cavern is a long stone counter set out from the wall.  A colorful mural covers the wall behind the counter, depicting brawny dwarves at work at a variety of tasks.  Vast, countless rows of differently sized shelves are behind the counter, and complex Dwarven mechanisms can be heard as they rearrange the package-covered storage.  Clerks shuffle endlessly back and forth between the counters and shelving as they assist patrons with their packaging and mailing needs."],"exits":[{"to":286,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["post office","mail"]},
  {"id":492,"x":60,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Dabrush Brawn, Inside","descriptions":["Haphazardly placed into crevices within the surrounding craggy stone walls, oil lanterns provide a steady light with no flickering.  A pair of displays are placed side by side at the center of the cavern, showcasing the fine wares of the shop."],"exits":[{"to":101,"exit":"go","move":"go steel archway"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Dabrush Brawn"]},
  {"id":493,"x":280,"y":100,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Fire, Rough Tunnel","descriptions":["Someone or something has crudely hacked out an extension of the passage, roughly working the walls just enough to allow travel deeper into the caverns and subterranean areas that surround Hibarnhvidar.  The unfinished feel of the excavation extends to the flooring, which is uneven and treacherous underfoot."],"exits":[{"to":132,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":494,"exit":"go","move":"go charred archway"},{"to":500,"exit":"go","move":"go side passage"}]},
  {"id":494,"x":300,"y":80,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Entrance","descriptions":["Cut from the walls of the twisting cavern, a blackened archway stands as testament to the efforts of explorers to delve deeper underneath the mountains.  Fault lines within the rock strata allowed the formation of this sinuous opening within the mountain."],"exits":[{"to":499,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":495,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":493,"exit":"go","move":"go charred archway"}]},
  {"id":495,"x":320,"y":80,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Rocky Alcove","descriptions":["Piles of fallen boulders lie heaped on the rough floor, providing an approximation of walls for this small alcove within the larger cavern.  Something has burned the rocks and the floor, coating them all with a dark film of soot that mixes with the dust to turn everything dark and dingy."],"exits":[{"to":496,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":494,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":496,"x":340,"y":60,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Rocky Cavern","descriptions":["A partial ceiling collapse here forces anyone traveling through to veer around the fallen rock.  Wafting through the air is the vague scent of fire and smoke that fights with the more normal musty odor of deep underground spaces."],"exits":[{"to":497,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":495,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":499,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":497,"x":340,"y":40,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Rocky Cavern","descriptions":["Nothing moves in this corner of the cavern, not even the slightest bit of breeze or zephyr.  Further passage deeper within the rock is blocked by the soot-stained walls, so heavily blackened that it is impossible to know what the rocks are beneath their layers of gunk."],"exits":[{"to":496,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":498,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":498,"x":320,"y":40,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Rocky Cavern","descriptions":["The cavern ends in a solid wall of granite, its granular surface covered with overlapping splotches of soot and smoke residue.  Although it appears that something has attempted to blast an opening through the rockface with fire, the attempt was in vain as the walls still enclose the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":497,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":499,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":499,"x":320,"y":60,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Rocky Cavern","descriptions":["A natural dip in the cavern floor is filled with seepage, forming a stagnant pool among the mostly dry and desolate cavern.  Oddly, the grimy surface of the pool is covered with a thin scum of soot and ash, although how it occurred is unknown."],"exits":[{"to":498,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":496,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":494,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":500,"x":280,"y":50,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Charred Grotto","descriptions":["Dips and holes litter the cavern floor, some filled with dark and dank liquids that seep from the walls and pool on the floor.  A few scattered boulders also lie haphazardly about, testimony to the unstable nature of the ceiling."],"exits":[{"to":501,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":502,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":493,"exit":"go","move":"go side passage"}]},
  {"id":501,"x":280,"y":30,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Charred Grotto","descriptions":["The scent of fire and ash lingers in the alcove, apparently coming from the grotto's walls that are coated with old blast marks.  Ash and soot mixes with the rock dust on the floor, each step causing a small cloud of the detritus to explode into the air before drifting slowly back to the ground."],"exits":[{"to":500,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":502,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":502,"x":260,"y":50,"z":2,"title":"Cavern of Flame, Charred Grotto","descriptions":["Overlapping blast circles cover one cavern wall, evidence of the attempts of the residents to escape their confinement within the depths of the earth.  A pile of rocks is capped by a teetering slab that balances precariously atop a rough pyramid."],"exits":[{"to":501,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":500,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]}
 ],
